}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db"}]},{"sha":"51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUxYjNjZDUxZjZmOTQ0ODhjMGUwNTU2NGNiY2FkOTUxMmY3M2UzZGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T23:07:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T23:07:34Z"},"message":"[codex] Tighten MCP connection manager API visibility and order (#27257)\n\n## Summary\n\n- order `McpConnectionManager` methods by visibility, with the primary\nconstructor and public API first\n- restrict `list_available_server_infos` to `codex-mcp`\n- make `new_uninitialized` a private test-only helper\n\n## Why\n\nThe manager exposed methods that are only used inside `codex-mcp` or its\nunit tests. Tightening those methods keeps the exported API intentional,\nwhile the new ordering makes the supported surface easier to scan.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- local tests not run; relying on CI","tree":{"sha":"10f4a57197a1ee58ae4ee55822b00e89afe355ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/10f4a57197a1ee58ae4ee55822b00e89afe355ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJy2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn4AQADTVktjEl645AHKBYt3FczSZ\nS1Y2niswtIY0M8SgOVGOmpBI4kQjMdyb9qRGqjxBQ2yEK2cMj9/7WI55jeuZl7pE\nKB944DTBk2DEM+lltx9wpuO4uRAQzakOwh2t/AoeLLPKMzj+cUsGrxrXw8OqqekT\n9ywrx26doYXWVJXI0ajk265RTcQ7LfCjFq0U7+1ABuDFs/lVu4LbOEmg6LZnIHsg\nFA7sNEe/YImEGQrJaC2X707XotZMk1Agf/vuR8F2e3yrucofLD3JPIXx2QmZvOXq\nOXJRV+dijJ6Ng9l2CPAmBEg5ZIN1f7sJTgCPfrc528jeQ5vyMV4X7PRTBnRJdP5R\nuOMG6ExBMPH0oGKh5CdBoK/0o380lwcRJ3UDC1Pr/dLuj3LCcQflpha62oVFn/kn\nvvf7H3ZiVaLZxkEFzdNr5G8q8QAzmW87iHWePG1Wkx6RFTH0HcF4Y93I7ZcuWyXe\ngJtIjsVRfUpioD53bVgtvaQlRwk/CGeBcxUIz7xSrwknrs6MR0Fr4dvyJbwJRocp\n8YB72hN9mCZTBmJhwMTnWGTYAZd7iATCBEZnLmUWlydSxvAu/hqe5DaudUFnX6/L\nUw2lS0Uq+VYG4rzu2675sgBn205DV2VSqAMwxMM25bO/4kYPocHMZaGufEZZlLI1\nMimyidRVH+t7ymF+tHuc\n=Oxh2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 10f4a57197a1ee58ae4ee55822b00e89afe355ca\nparent 490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1781046454 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781046454 -0700\n\n[codex] Tighten MCP connection manager API visibility and order (#27257)\n\n## Summary\n\n- order `McpConnectionManager` methods by visibility, with the primary\nconstructor and public API first\n- restrict `list_available_server_infos` to `codex-mcp`\n- make `new_uninitialized` a private test-only helper\n\n## Why\n\nThe manager exposed methods that are only used inside `codex-mcp` or its\nunit tests. Tightening those methods keeps the exported API intentional,\nwhile the new ordering makes the supported surface easier to scan.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- local tests not run; relying on CI","verified_at":"2026-06-09T23:07:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/51b3cd51f6f94488c0e05564cbcad9512f73e3db/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363"}]},{"sha":"490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ5MDM0MGZmY2Y1OTM1MThiY2Q4NDNlZTkwM2QxZWEyMTYwZDUzNjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"ssetty-oai","email":"ssetty@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:49:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:49:48Z"},"message":"[codex] Retry streamable HTTP initialize failures (#25147)\n\n## Summary\n- Retry transient streamable HTTP failures during RMCP startup when the\nfailure happens while sending the initialize request.\n- Retry transient streamable HTTP failures for tools/list, which is\nread-only and safe to replay.\n- Cover both retryable HTTP statuses and request-layer failures where no\nHTTP status is returned.\n- Surface retryable HTTP statuses from the streamable HTTP adapter as\ntyped client errors.\n- Add integration coverage for initialize retry, tools/list retry,\nno-status request failure retry, and non-retryable initialize status.\n\n## Root cause\nThe observed codex_apps failures can happen before normal tool\nexecution: RMCP startup fails while sending initialize, or the first\nread-only tools/list fails after startup. Retrying hosted_apps_bridge\ntools/call would not cover initialize and would risk replaying\nside-effecting tool calls. This change retries the streamable HTTP\nhandshake itself, recreates the transport between initialize attempts,\nand retries only tools/list among post-initialize service operations.\n\n## Validation\n- cargo fmt --package codex-rmcp-client\n- cargo test -p codex-rmcp-client --test streamable_http_recovery","tree":{"sha":"5f993d27a583717c681f9f3afd20dde4ab86015b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5f993d27a583717c681f9f3afd20dde4ab86015b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJiMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJHoQAFrhOSrCJwdWCIu48VntO0vX\nrSEMmAfEX2c2UiJBNFzilNJEp3PO2mZ1Yzs8oYqiMEpPyrDY+OV8GE9iZohb1mkv\nHda0vHs9bNcxjVSix7lka8lsQtumOHwmSIIPKIrZckU0nlo35cR7o3aO4S5VCdTb\nL7yducCZ0R9BQ0h8atvXUK+1XWgmpYfFAn+B7Bl1s7On+yGth9VsqgxaPioHmu17\ntKchMNSdgSyUXjouEi68aHAzO5gxNWyAHG7ACmUsRrACjQZ3XEhoLINfjc/m113m\nCfUBisj8O9LGw+fQdxCyXmPGH03cJF8rPd3IkqPjTxUTyF0AZgSHvMgscX2SbfVi\nKUHYsef7/RQcnCo8lZDBLuiKPuMDu6lsCO9QSKpcYL1HgLZ8btulqaSDnx+zJPfX\nTmmjUG/yhBhWB5LZKKOFLXSb01a2eKMGZQ9qsa/LWIh/vzOPVXWepuMFLm1WtqBF\n0mfTBLdAAGgE/aqQVJfHBtJQtbPP54g+qK1l3ng6THS4ZxLXhNH2NimGKHOVeTlX\nEpJZW9R1D+0Mh56XSCkzKmRwHlOm3JFZat0n0xZHrW+RVY1QG40OsVR6aBNTjDJj\nohFxkxIk14NyEXUc1QO8Mg7mcaBpdcyqy8CKH5z/5ZPW9JhKdlW2O85QBxbv8ZKL\nEk+xYyfdHV9L0uJC0+Nm\n=pwgn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5f993d27a583717c681f9f3afd20dde4ab86015b\nparent 9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419\nauthor ssetty-oai <ssetty@openai.com> 1781045388 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781045388 -0700\n\n[codex] Retry streamable HTTP initialize failures (#25147)\n\n## Summary\n- Retry transient streamable HTTP failures during RMCP startup when the\nfailure happens while sending the initialize request.\n- Retry transient streamable HTTP failures for tools/list, which is\nread-only and safe to replay.\n- Cover both retryable HTTP statuses and request-layer failures where no\nHTTP status is returned.\n- Surface retryable HTTP statuses from the streamable HTTP adapter as\ntyped client errors.\n- Add integration coverage for initialize retry, tools/list retry,\nno-status request failure retry, and non-retryable initialize status.\n\n## Root cause\nThe observed codex_apps failures can happen before normal tool\nexecution: RMCP startup fails while sending initialize, or the first\nread-only tools/list fails after startup. Retrying hosted_apps_bridge\ntools/call would not cover initialize and would risk replaying\nside-effecting tool calls. This change retries the streamable HTTP\nhandshake itself, recreates the transport between initialize attempts,\nand retries only tools/list among post-initialize service operations.\n\n## Validation\n- cargo fmt --package codex-rmcp-client\n- cargo test -p codex-rmcp-client --test streamable_http_recovery","verified_at":"2026-06-09T22:49:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/490340ffcf593518bcd843ee903d1ea2160d5363/comments","author":{"login":"ssetty-oai","id":214716837,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxRpQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/ssetty-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssetty-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419"}]},{"sha":"9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkzMTZhY2Y5YjIzOGRhNzU1OWQ3ZmJhNjdjNjEyNzEyYWNjM2I0MTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:32:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:32:15Z"},"message":"[2/4] Add private Python goal operations (#27111)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Python SDK must treat the runtime's initial goal turn and its\ncontinuations as one logical operation. That requires a private\nlifecycle engine before the public API can return the existing turn\nhandle and result types.\n\n## What\n\n- start goals by composing the existing clear/set goal RPCs\n- enforce persisted, idle threads and a bounded startup handshake\n- coalesce continuation notifications under a stable logical turn ID\n- aggregate items, usage, timing, and terminal status\n- support rollover-aware steering, interruption, cancellation, and\ncleanup\n- provide equivalent sync and async internals\n\nThis is the second PR in the stack and intentionally adds no public API.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- online CI, including the Python SDK suite\n- behavioral coverage is added in the following two stack PRs","tree":{"sha":"36ecab458da47577908ff4b6194c3421e0c5be7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/36ecab458da47577908ff4b6194c3421e0c5be7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJRvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmnQQAKbDHiNvQB4Q20wTo3aBiXSI\nQ8JKdBqhDB7wJmk+uqRD9EFeLKKuNRBtDg8bsLbaE9dv5pOHHvWiUywwbWnrsS0H\njX0QbTxCo5kZLaHOdwq4d2alGc+5/CuXAFcMVbilB0vatOujCinK7DIuRDXFZ0S4\nvCIKw9yN9pFt1M7iXKP8RN65fHLks5MQ/ieTt2r13IJVAgi+pGcA0UufNtbQnR1S\nEAIR3STa/3/Ki1ehBndvnf6fjbjInA/LZZbiZe6sjXTTLBPJYvPNwFvrJIx/oQ0L\n2NMrG5XgFu5xL5f7uBQydQeIePif+K8s9gyRvXgDpnxhmqx/ovx2gP4s6a6l4aEF\nnFPSQc1iNPt5RaXetMMYd8uZp/rfY8VQf3Ci54Ix3tq8qflhRDnrmgRxKzJ+8N70\n2spvrtcFKa0pydsVocLvTHhlxAIcekZVXhzSA7jonOet9nva1Rf07/nH8i3vH/yL\nEGp9TGjDTnhhQ/iC8vEP1v9zdzXIo3RiNhIeon6EvWzqy7D+Rm70GQUiYioxeOBV\n+ObXge3wCm26XXD8hGCJVZxO1Tp2FJgZ/7q04Rfc84Ieqv4Mj7RN341vDuZoh5kE\noQrSYbSvwN94rdtu6ReQJ14u9XYP3ICzFNE5R3kn9Qsb+8DN3E+jxjXJcsKCEvpV\nBru7ujDHTMztFtm8mKNf\n=47E8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 36ecab458da47577908ff4b6194c3421e0c5be7b\nparent cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1781044335 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781044335 -0700\n\n[2/4] Add private Python goal operations (#27111)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Python SDK must treat the runtime's initial goal turn and its\ncontinuations as one logical operation. That requires a private\nlifecycle engine before the public API can return the existing turn\nhandle and result types.\n\n## What\n\n- start goals by composing the existing clear/set goal RPCs\n- enforce persisted, idle threads and a bounded startup handshake\n- coalesce continuation notifications under a stable logical turn ID\n- aggregate items, usage, timing, and terminal status\n- support rollover-aware steering, interruption, cancellation, and\ncleanup\n- provide equivalent sync and async internals\n\nThis is the second PR in the stack and intentionally adds no public API.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- online CI, including the Python SDK suite\n- behavioral coverage is added in the following two stack PRs","verified_at":"2026-06-09T22:32:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9316acf9b238da7559d7fba67c612712acc3b419/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e"}]},{"sha":"cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNjODMyNWYxODE0MDFjNDgxZjRkYThjYTE2YzA3Mzg2N2U3OGQ0NmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"guinness-oai","email":"guinness@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:20:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:20:01Z"},"message":"Stop mirroring Codex user input into realtime (#27116)\n\n## Why\n\nThe realtime frontend model and the backing Codex thread should present\none coherent assistant. Raw typed messages, steers, and worker reports\nbelong to the orchestrator; the frontend model should receive the\norchestrator's user-facing result rather than a second copy of those\ninputs.\n\nToday normal `turn/start` input is automatically inserted into the\nrealtime conversation, while `turn/steer` is not. Besides creating\ninconsistent context, this can make the frontend model react\nindependently before Codex has produced the response it should speak.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove automatic accepted-user-input mirroring into realtime\n- Remove the mirror-only echo-suppression flag and dead V2 prefix helper\n- Preserve explicit app-to-realtime text injection and FEM-to-Codex\ndelegation\n- Replace the positive mirror tests and obsolete snapshots with a\nnegative routing regression test\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nconversation_user_text_turn_is_not_sent_to_realtime`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nconversation_startup_context_is_truncated_and_sent_once_per_start`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core inbound_handoff_request_starts_turn`","tree":{"sha":"d777a7754a4dacc3669f3a25b047f057a12126e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d777a7754a4dacc3669f3a25b047f057a12126e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKJGRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAllQQAHs3/KxjqQe0SG9CtnIW78je\naJx19EU03S6PmOQs1nmJp6XBPdJpwvVfy0CCRzHPT01U1z8IsiGAfbCsYiqnjSA6\nkqxyzFsB5BrW6Z1AdSdHb8Sacd0gH8CPwh5nrueWYZd9xyXFJdngG3ojCAD05ooP\n+eMe/vj+yymZeq+/15UtG61vNizvvJL1jF+jPxYAaVPnxpeV3sSeSP+01cyno1R2\n8SUjwlYkWuULiUSjGT3Js45noma3gaj5VSR9b4BlHvSgbKKjz3WwiARYyjFsA1Bn\naEghrnSzK0c4jpD2YbVtiZWL72ctb/Zl1lMeUoTdkbJp0Il6/46Y+gH/j2WVyG1q\nlGi0OzRYVmeTtHgfQ3oHXKbrDYaw3IRIatcc1lxFBG9WtvAxXyPj+W0wtUk635FV\nvcpzNPeY3amptoc70R/06ihOfKw7cSCH3hmz8pa5L30PD1Zbxqb2BIT/PM37CvKL\ndttrKGM/bewWfHEjVavPSGlsnyEYVtdhFnD+wZK3nrnhw0Rguw9btApFrn3F9Kbe\n1LmRl1DgM5vFSeILNoNUHYWW6bLAy821ohf+H/STB68OrwLkFXv0ZySvRxMifIxR\nFMk60t4UgM5LZ/8ZNfijlaDeSsku76Z7pM9mJdCKJhtneA5nZ+QYsFqwFvjMh1u1\n7r9CQTowfnn8bOKBhFI+\n=zDhx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d777a7754a4dacc3669f3a25b047f057a12126e3\nparent f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519\nauthor guinness-oai <guinness@openai.com> 1781043601 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781043601 -0700\n\nStop mirroring Codex user input into realtime (#27116)\n\n## Why\n\nThe realtime frontend model and the backing Codex thread should present\none coherent assistant. Raw typed messages, steers, and worker reports\nbelong to the orchestrator; the frontend model should receive the\norchestrator's user-facing result rather than a second copy of those\ninputs.\n\nToday normal `turn/start` input is automatically inserted into the\nrealtime conversation, while `turn/steer` is not. Besides creating\ninconsistent context, this can make the frontend model react\nindependently before Codex has produced the response it should speak.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove automatic accepted-user-input mirroring into realtime\n- Remove the mirror-only echo-suppression flag and dead V2 prefix helper\n- Preserve explicit app-to-realtime text injection and FEM-to-Codex\ndelegation\n- Replace the positive mirror tests and obsolete snapshots with a\nnegative routing regression test\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nconversation_user_text_turn_is_not_sent_to_realtime`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nconversation_startup_context_is_truncated_and_sent_once_per_start`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core inbound_handoff_request_starts_turn`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T22:20:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc8325f181401c481f4da8ca16c073867e78d46e/comments","author":{"login":"guinness-oai","id":254771997,"node_id":"U_kgDODy-DHQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254771997?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/guinness-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519"}]},{"sha":"f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYyOTY5ZjM2ZThiNmFhMmFlZmNkNjI1ZDJhOWZjODQyNWJiMmE1MTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:10:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T22:10:17Z"},"message":"[codex] Handle Ctrl-C for non-TTY unified exec (#26734)\n\n## Why\n\nA long-running unified exec process started with `tty: false` could not\nbe interrupted via `write_stdin`: ordinary non-TTY stdin writes are\nrejected once stdin is closed, but an exact U+0003 payload should still\nmap to a process interrupt. The interrupt should flow through the same\nprocess lifecycle path as a real signal so Codex preserves\nprocess-reported output and exit metadata instead of fabricating a\nCtrl-C exit code or tearing down the session early.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `process/signal` to exec-server with `ProcessSignal::Interrupt`\nand an empty response.\n- Add a non-consuming `ProcessHandle::signal` path for spawned\nprocesses; on Unix it sends SIGINT to the process group and leaves\nterminate/hard-kill unchanged.\n- Route non-TTY U+0003 `write_stdin` through `process.signal(...)`\ninstead of `terminate`, then let the normal post-write collection path\ndrain output and observe exit.\n- Add exec-server coverage where a shell `trap INT` handler prints the\nsignal and exits with its own code.\n- Add unified exec coverage where a `tty: false` process traps SIGINT,\nemits output, and exits with its own code.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server\nexec_process_signal_interrupts_process`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nwrite_stdin_ctrl_c_interrupts_non_tty_session`","tree":{"sha":"dd5847d2a60d96d8750b09a66d253e008589e85d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dd5847d2a60d96d8750b09a66d253e008589e85d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKI9JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjcUQAGT6V6r01Tc3QFyFwdpKkXDf\nQAQX4OGS7NkoQA1t0En5DZG+aEARi5ZoEQae9paDKXwJclHeMQh8wvqX13W+6QnW\ndBwTvpcetfpZwoaRUIhZsEPP7hVpkd6c7TEOfzAHAd+9Iai9iPKP99SjeCSvEmlx\nE1ZbHt1YZcF0JqW/FW3KrbFtt1wS0GppDffe6UF66/1zilqFdTCWzry4JsD5wrbw\nGqweH14sYnGoisc1cEsqR4OFJYaxMeA9YSkFpU4gltDogQuRlp8v/F/8hLEe30My\nLhQcoFH+jG230/lpAxcl93dccrBxh2yuTHw2mEykWjg9A5exZMGUdD9sPWjqV+Qz\nLRnLLMt5X/ksymG/yGdVDHkB3UjNbb9AEnxBXYNzNELb6vdYggHvXFXkm2UOWx2q\nwKSecZXVlQDUfm50ief1xKngPwNKvpUhPrdM9PwxiCdzgP9XoUg14OPsuEYeRg3x\nIdzq2SlfbpqH8AxorpHltkgPaFjEiGkfliiF0UgI8cF3ByYI5nysZf4+aJBthN6F\nUDgeEowSbSqnD/K0RkLgBUhGUyXTzMOt8qTi2z2LP3ED2y9PFZ0EgsM6j7IjwOZo\nNiAEgwBog7OGYiCEAlbU1l0PH9cxXulIaZabwl1Rk0DW6rCjr7U3CG4w+Umde+wf\nK9FJbwdfxB2+JAruuYTZ\n=GFYn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dd5847d2a60d96d8750b09a66d253e008589e85d\nparent f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781043017 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781043017 -0700\n\n[codex] Handle Ctrl-C for non-TTY unified exec (#26734)\n\n## Why\n\nA long-running unified exec process started with `tty: false` could not\nbe interrupted via `write_stdin`: ordinary non-TTY stdin writes are\nrejected once stdin is closed, but an exact U+0003 payload should still\nmap to a process interrupt. The interrupt should flow through the same\nprocess lifecycle path as a real signal so Codex preserves\nprocess-reported output and exit metadata instead of fabricating a\nCtrl-C exit code or tearing down the session early.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `process/signal` to exec-server with `ProcessSignal::Interrupt`\nand an empty response.\n- Add a non-consuming `ProcessHandle::signal` path for spawned\nprocesses; on Unix it sends SIGINT to the process group and leaves\nterminate/hard-kill unchanged.\n- Route non-TTY U+0003 `write_stdin` through `process.signal(...)`\ninstead of `terminate`, then let the normal post-write collection path\ndrain output and observe exit.\n- Add exec-server coverage where a shell `trap INT` handler prints the\nsignal and exits with its own code.\n- Add unified exec coverage where a `tty: false` process traps SIGINT,\nemits output, and exits with its own code.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server\nexec_process_signal_interrupts_process`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nwrite_stdin_ctrl_c_interrupts_non_tty_session`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T22:10:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2969f36e8b6aa2aefcd625d2a9fc8425bb2a519/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d"}]},{"sha":"f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY1NzQ5NDY5NjBhNGQyMWU4ODQ0NTNhYzk5NjNhODY5MTUzYjg0N2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T21:18:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T21:18:24Z"},"message":"[codex] Report unusable MCP OAuth credentials as logged out (#26713)\n\n## Why\n\nPersisted MCP OAuth credentials were reported as authenticated whenever\na credential record existed. An expired token without a usable refresh\ntoken could therefore appear as `OAuth` even though startup could not\nauthenticate with it, leaving users with a misleading status instead of\na login prompt.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Classify stored OAuth credentials as missing, usable, or requiring\nauthorization.\n- Reuse the existing refresh window so near-expiry credentials without a\nrefresh path are also treated as logged out.\n- Validate required credential fields before reporting OAuth\nauthentication.\n- Add unit coverage for credential usability and integration coverage\nfor expired, unexpired, and refreshable persisted credentials.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client`","tree":{"sha":"72f96d7e26420d49f1c378a305161881dc6199ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/72f96d7e26420d49f1c378a305161881dc6199ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKIMgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyKQQAGLpLPwn30x1UQ17jpaX0vki\n1iS8mWUg3T4H6IBNeYLHrp2I0XKfqc7+h4hwJhyYp9OCPCyU050zJuTGGCC82fjx\nUcLt2+UnP6XvpxEASy6NOLFCEb2Ej+7J5O5nW9Srg+uGZGImYs12A79djA1DvX9+\n5OvyugE5SQ0pv2PBa8ToYtu8gY4RrfhNyCzXp4sSehAJIOC7d33K+BwyZTgTv5B+\nafK1OEwIbgJ5vSG9AOgePFqHHVrOQpJ3lJ8LkPQW/RNssFOFkqGlCJah1pDAFnsa\nnto8OQ1qNaSeK9P1DSlSPwN2SHVAxwmFK2CHeZu2Jb+wzposN696BRMZv8aw2m9f\nyyVahzX52XiBQ406DFcXWxEvvnEPzgAoNMw/T/zcmP+3pGT2IZn0Bx+UErIlUkSN\nim9ZGve82NAT6KHmMrpSvDGNUUh13cXdVg7ewHSsyS+vkVpqqHvi1AcvC704dfKS\n3Y/U2X0dNBpqAgkJaqNRphnqBo4w2Rcf+a4ZOmJRMwwq/4XXpy4n0yuMrWfdHEWy\n3d23FNwp8C0oOe1jVE4eiocfgTUL2BFcRW5OsP2R8fZnfCHGGN0rDH6Tb6uPegTH\nBhiSRqF5YI2mLctF2tI0M66aS8eFutB2aX2iXmwVEKGL/2OYMfJwnyxxPj5awf92\njX6YQrsxGWx/BQIMr4UR\n=hsxD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 72f96d7e26420d49f1c378a305161881dc6199ea\nparent 9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781039904 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781039904 -0700\n\n[codex] Report unusable MCP OAuth credentials as logged out (#26713)\n\n## Why\n\nPersisted MCP OAuth credentials were reported as authenticated whenever\na credential record existed. An expired token without a usable refresh\ntoken could therefore appear as `OAuth` even though startup could not\nauthenticate with it, leaving users with a misleading status instead of\na login prompt.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Classify stored OAuth credentials as missing, usable, or requiring\nauthorization.\n- Reuse the existing refresh window so near-expiry credentials without a\nrefresh path are also treated as logged out.\n- Validate required credential fields before reporting OAuth\nauthentication.\n- Add unit coverage for credential usability and integration coverage\nfor expired, unexpired, and refreshable persisted credentials.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T21:18:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f574946960a4d21e884453ac9963a869153b847d/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839"}]},{"sha":"9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDllMzA4MWJlOTY3MmM2NWY4YTBjZDk1ODcxOTA2NWY0OWY0N2Q4Mzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:51:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:51:57Z"},"message":"[codex] Characterize global instruction lifecycle (#26830)\n\n## Why\n\nGlobal instruction behavior spans thread creation, resume, forks,\nsubagents, and compaction. Characterization coverage is needed before\nchanging those semantics so preserved history can be distinguished from\nnewly loaded configuration.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extends the existing `agents_md` suite with fresh-thread, warning,\nresume, fork, and subagent lifecycle coverage.\n- Extends the existing `compact` suite with manual, mid-turn, and\nremote-v2 compaction coverage.\n- Asserts rendered instruction fragments, reported source paths, and\nstructured request history before and after instruction-file mutations.","tree":{"sha":"03d04514d145e9f440c2a3f465f4e88b713cbea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/03d04514d145e9f440c2a3f465f4e88b713cbea3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHztCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEboQAB4eH2WKkfvlQdjpt6t3BgEb\nZ0/wiM7VlSkyRZH1PqgjwEnssHxMKxTdpNh5YLwxDaNMqndnf630Nx99o1EXCjW8\n3UH3YmcdI7iKPvXG/dy5xLp6BJXPs8oGVMNJLR+dxsCSWGFS9F8JXSSlyWcv60tJ\n7kUC+tqh+rtJdyiEl4dpk8TgROYsQoC8cGd2czp73FCepOym7917UC/tm+821xSE\n1C8alqQQeytFX+c36hKAyNrfnQ9zsFBpfmqLW2tG4k3DBlyUSIXV4KnHgk8BSpLX\nkdyzmh6kr54BE/4mNsqIsGWu+R5ehgt1h0VeUxfH6D2+GHMtncirDrz/UP0vhFUQ\n82mT7ELKdFC4LtnGeN5C47DIkTCZr9ELg0meor46FlNAMN4IYJ5WsRRRZkDxrSOt\nDBj7ebeKHR98xjDwd93oM4PhDp2NQfYG8jGKSba9H/jvdnEcK6E6wr7UR4YVh5Bx\nbstIEyARpVW4lU/ICH1B5NpAQPmPWbgGm4RGP8JmYsW9keXDBeFrntNZ4Wvm3EIS\nnMlB9+YIg/rYb1ZjpBYYLxQPalZCDNpNc2b1cPfZ/4iq/boP1xkQS2wP4sQ1PFHP\nb7crU72k9bzJhzl60SLHVulj3Z9mwRuotIWCEQpUe2oCZ3i9x/BTCU4UerLtK7ty\nWgfTEyWx3wVhRGjC/Du9\n=ZAeF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 03d04514d145e9f440c2a3f465f4e88b713cbea3\nparent 4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781038317 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781038317 +0000\n\n[codex] Characterize global instruction lifecycle (#26830)\n\n## Why\n\nGlobal instruction behavior spans thread creation, resume, forks,\nsubagents, and compaction. Characterization coverage is needed before\nchanging those semantics so preserved history can be distinguished from\nnewly loaded configuration.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extends the existing `agents_md` suite with fresh-thread, warning,\nresume, fork, and subagent lifecycle coverage.\n- Extends the existing `compact` suite with manual, mid-turn, and\nremote-v2 compaction coverage.\n- Asserts rendered instruction fragments, reported source paths, and\nstructured request history before and after instruction-file mutations.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:51:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e3081be9672c65f8a0cd958719065f49f47d839/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717"}]},{"sha":"4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRlYzNiOGVlZWEzOGU5ZjY5MzU2OGU0ZjUxYmI2MDdjYzZjZDk3MTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:44:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:44:16Z"},"message":"Route hosted Apps MCP through extensions (#27191)\n\n## Stack\n\n- Base: #27184\n- This PR is the second vertical and should be reviewed against\n`jif/external-plugins-1`, not `main`.\n\n## Why\n\nCCA is moving toward a split runtime where the orchestrator may have no\nfilesystem or executor, but it still needs to activate remotely hosted\nplugin components. HTTP MCP servers are the simplest complete example:\nthey need configuration and host authentication, but they do not need an\nexecutor process.\n\nThe Apps MCP endpoint is currently synthesized by a special-purpose\nloader inside the MCP runtime. That works locally, but it leaves hosted\nMCP activation outside the extension model being established in #27184.\nIt also makes the Apps path a poor foundation for plugins whose skills,\nMCP servers, connectors, and hooks may come from different sources or\nexecute in different places.\n\nThis PR moves that one behavior behind an extension-owned contribution\nwhile preserving the existing local fallback. It deliberately does not\nintroduce a generic plugin activation framework.\n\n## What changed\n\n### MCP extension contribution\n\n`codex-extension-api` gains an ordered `McpServerContributor` contract.\nA contributor returns typed `Set` or `Remove` overlays for MCP server\nconfiguration; later contributors win for the names they own.\n\nThe contract stays at the existing MCP configuration boundary.\nExtensions do not create a second connection manager or transport\nabstraction.\n\n### Hosted Apps MCP extension\n\nA new `codex-mcp-extension` contributes the reserved `codex_apps` server\nfrom the existing Apps feature, ChatGPT base URL, path override, and\nproduct SKU configuration.\n\nWhen `apps_mcp_path_override` is enabled for `https://chatgpt.com`, the\nresulting streamable HTTP endpoint is\n`https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/ps/mcp`. The existing ChatGPT-auth gate\nremains authoritative, so this server can run in an orchestrator-only\nprocess without being exposed for API-key sessions.\n\n### One resolved runtime view\n\n`McpManager` now distinguishes three views:\n\n- **configured:** config- and plugin-backed servers before extension\noverlays;\n- **runtime:** configured servers plus host-installed extension\ncontributions;\n- **effective:** runtime servers after auth gating and compatibility\nbuilt-ins.\n\nApp-server installs the hosted MCP extension and uses the runtime view\nfor thread startup, refresh, status, threadless resource reads,\nconnector discovery, and MCP OAuth lookup. This keeps\n`mcpServer/oauth/login` consistent with the servers exposed by the other\nMCP APIs. The hosted Apps server itself continues to use existing\nChatGPT host authentication rather than MCP OAuth.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nHosts that do not install the MCP extension retain the existing Apps MCP\nsynthesis path. This preserves current local-only, CLI, and\nstandalone-host behavior while app-server exercises the extension path.\n\nDisabling Apps removes the reserved `codex_apps` entry, and losing\nChatGPT auth removes it from the effective runtime view. Executor\navailability is not consulted for this HTTP transport.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nThe next vertical will resolve a manifest-declared stdio MCP server from\nan executor-selected plugin root and execute it in the environment that\nowns that root. Later verticals can add backend-owned skills, connector\nmetadata, hooks, durable selection semantics, and incremental local\nconvergence without changing the component-specific runtime boundaries\nintroduced here.\n\n## Verification\n\nFocused coverage was added for:\n\n- contributing the hosted Apps MCP at `/backend-api/ps/mcp` without an\nexecutor;\n- requiring ChatGPT auth in the effective runtime view;\n- removing a reserved configured Apps server when the Apps feature is\ndisabled.\n\n`cargo check -p codex-app-server -p codex-mcp-extension -p\ncodex-extension-api -p codex-mcp` passed. Tests and Clippy were not run\nlocally under the current development instruction; CI provides the full\nvalidation pass.","tree":{"sha":"a951088b3284a0d13e4e7af147d9cae905f9c58a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a951088b3284a0d13e4e7af147d9cae905f9c58a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHsgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMJEQAChBZLlSrXDnJIxrgHbStKX0\noX7SXSUBIK1+4dxKoWZIT1EsgvN1fvjG0T/TT357Zj16hREqJjxPdT992hn9Sxzw\nOJeLm6Z8eYirfVA1p53C5Pc2pFA2yb6Toh/qR1V0UKy74QJFBW61LjZF6wxYGOIU\n9MyaLuOJ7O9UqNLwZI0WQ2xgYDrwGT3kusLaQVbw9f4kGiCWYQaXEowv9S4aKwcr\nVgmxP4wCT9H0BAKFjxa3FFcj+uCtov9lLcxBgrx4z/e7/wswkP9qECliWw61uX+e\ndlCPa8GOw/9Ec8M38yj3/HC2mpB5IFy/Yudd6ZmadsU992ok7Oor3PavsHm36P3T\nVTrP5dh5nxJ3SIa8gwRPEaOm6KkJQQ5ak/nYM7Dwukt33hyTgx3YTUBCbfWobgyR\nuxAx2731/J+jORAP+yucCvfAEX35DZTTptr+xJfS3JCfkjWhLi+bA+H7SwDvE0b0\n6DaoJl0I5nxJ9Aa9uyjclqQznlGvzcPoSSQxKrkrmQgFb9FVShIFy83ONh5SKMVj\nhwZF9+IDhWqAoDechSCka2EyoymfRhrBQimAYgUjIb7GW0+ZspN7lr/1e3lV9Skr\nbyNXqy5TqceYaAe2D64BNv7bQG/vawn5Dtmqay86v3cBe021OitE4K3yP2OWKV0z\nt7hhAoHi8akZVrU344JA\n=3cy+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a951088b3284a0d13e4e7af147d9cae905f9c58a\nparent 5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781037856 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781037856 +0200\n\nRoute hosted Apps MCP through extensions (#27191)\n\n## Stack\n\n- Base: #27184\n- This PR is the second vertical and should be reviewed against\n`jif/external-plugins-1`, not `main`.\n\n## Why\n\nCCA is moving toward a split runtime where the orchestrator may have no\nfilesystem or executor, but it still needs to activate remotely hosted\nplugin components. HTTP MCP servers are the simplest complete example:\nthey need configuration and host authentication, but they do not need an\nexecutor process.\n\nThe Apps MCP endpoint is currently synthesized by a special-purpose\nloader inside the MCP runtime. That works locally, but it leaves hosted\nMCP activation outside the extension model being established in #27184.\nIt also makes the Apps path a poor foundation for plugins whose skills,\nMCP servers, connectors, and hooks may come from different sources or\nexecute in different places.\n\nThis PR moves that one behavior behind an extension-owned contribution\nwhile preserving the existing local fallback. It deliberately does not\nintroduce a generic plugin activation framework.\n\n## What changed\n\n### MCP extension contribution\n\n`codex-extension-api` gains an ordered `McpServerContributor` contract.\nA contributor returns typed `Set` or `Remove` overlays for MCP server\nconfiguration; later contributors win for the names they own.\n\nThe contract stays at the existing MCP configuration boundary.\nExtensions do not create a second connection manager or transport\nabstraction.\n\n### Hosted Apps MCP extension\n\nA new `codex-mcp-extension` contributes the reserved `codex_apps` server\nfrom the existing Apps feature, ChatGPT base URL, path override, and\nproduct SKU configuration.\n\nWhen `apps_mcp_path_override` is enabled for `https://chatgpt.com`, the\nresulting streamable HTTP endpoint is\n`https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/ps/mcp`. The existing ChatGPT-auth gate\nremains authoritative, so this server can run in an orchestrator-only\nprocess without being exposed for API-key sessions.\n\n### One resolved runtime view\n\n`McpManager` now distinguishes three views:\n\n- **configured:** config- and plugin-backed servers before extension\noverlays;\n- **runtime:** configured servers plus host-installed extension\ncontributions;\n- **effective:** runtime servers after auth gating and compatibility\nbuilt-ins.\n\nApp-server installs the hosted MCP extension and uses the runtime view\nfor thread startup, refresh, status, threadless resource reads,\nconnector discovery, and MCP OAuth lookup. This keeps\n`mcpServer/oauth/login` consistent with the servers exposed by the other\nMCP APIs. The hosted Apps server itself continues to use existing\nChatGPT host authentication rather than MCP OAuth.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nHosts that do not install the MCP extension retain the existing Apps MCP\nsynthesis path. This preserves current local-only, CLI, and\nstandalone-host behavior while app-server exercises the extension path.\n\nDisabling Apps removes the reserved `codex_apps` entry, and losing\nChatGPT auth removes it from the effective runtime view. Executor\navailability is not consulted for this HTTP transport.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\nThe next vertical will resolve a manifest-declared stdio MCP server from\nan executor-selected plugin root and execute it in the environment that\nowns that root. Later verticals can add backend-owned skills, connector\nmetadata, hooks, durable selection semantics, and incremental local\nconvergence without changing the component-specific runtime boundaries\nintroduced here.\n\n## Verification\n\nFocused coverage was added for:\n\n- contributing the hosted Apps MCP at `/backend-api/ps/mcp` without an\nexecutor;\n- requiring ChatGPT auth in the effective runtime view;\n- removing a reserved configured Apps server when the Apps feature is\ndisabled.\n\n`cargo check -p codex-app-server -p codex-mcp-extension -p\ncodex-extension-api -p codex-mcp` passed. Tests and Clippy were not run\nlocally under the current development instruction; CI provides the full\nvalidation pass.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:44:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ec3b8eeea38e9f693568e4f51bb607cc6cd9717/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e"}]},{"sha":"5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVhMGY5MTM0MjY3ZTBmZWQyNDA2ZmNlMGVhMGYxNGUzMDg5NDUxM2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:35:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:35:29Z"},"message":"[1/4] Add Python goal routing foundation (#27110)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal continuation turns are emitted by the existing runtime as separate\nphysical turns. The Python SDK needs private thread-scoped routing\nbefore it can present those notifications as one logical operation,\nwithout changing ordinary turn routing or the app-server protocol.\n\n## What\n\n- add private goal operation state and thread-scoped notification\nrouting\n- add internal wrappers for the existing `thread/goal/clear` and\n`thread/goal/set` RPCs\n- include existing goal notifications in the SDK notification union\n- preserve ordinary turn-ID routing unchanged\n- add focused routing coverage\n\nThis PR does not expose a public goal API. It is the first PR in the\nPython goal operations stack.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- online CI, including the Python SDK suite\n- focused typed-notification routing coverage","tree":{"sha":"96520921b821892a13d4e5dc31a5ad093e4f7af3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/96520921b821892a13d4e5dc31a5ad093e4f7af3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHkRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIaMQAEf2VU42xjNA9XxgH0C91oTI\nIzFwCsjVCrErKys2MNKChBSLksM//rgOjCivssBoPZaYKgvTk+W2HaGGr5KfVel5\n0fpTzlifQqvpdJFJtaSApqz0Kuva60Zxc+BYqWxEgWF/Xo1hs5/R+eFwQakBUOL4\nLHvOHndUjtgaWBEtniDtvf9CsgK8Ey8sch8fAlCPqSwPOd/19Us3VB8QDv/jGtX5\nMa/AniipoH7tkVlVZ/HfnL/Huuxfd1GWBQwS4WoA9vVAj0QJrNMOCzbmZE6FjwFg\nL8a9dbXBznBcge6PzDHeIHN+NxdLRa/UUARdfGsbiJ2r9FUVktz2rQi6oVvh7h08\niTMZxk4IKTE1bhHwwnm4F1AgfYReNN6UzwF4LqDjS79+XHxLfOWGF7BKDaPJTWRQ\nmXQbQmhnWloBaPjYUaJYedqvWu0F1eJHDUJWB/4Q4IA9FszZAskaZIBnUG/I9MBM\n0T7txxaZkBwpbYSaw9jTztVyM6uCl8dHdDVXOZEcHoxJxA6LuiYzS5gB6tkbWTdA\nAmi5U2U+mstzBYIdG3jzuuFfUMfit0ZPQ48nC0DUjY2oRHoc+Or5Wal0pWOYi52n\nZzYKNrGLcwMTQAcoJDE0y0N5RjoB6DtyutWrZ+bKWsVKp/JsvFn0WnB8lVIhuTUu\n5GwwUaeLKadtpI3R35mG\n=hTPj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96520921b821892a13d4e5dc31a5ad093e4f7af3\nparent 8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1781037329 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781037329 -0700\n\n[1/4] Add Python goal routing foundation (#27110)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal continuation turns are emitted by the existing runtime as separate\nphysical turns. The Python SDK needs private thread-scoped routing\nbefore it can present those notifications as one logical operation,\nwithout changing ordinary turn routing or the app-server protocol.\n\n## What\n\n- add private goal operation state and thread-scoped notification\nrouting\n- add internal wrappers for the existing `thread/goal/clear` and\n`thread/goal/set` RPCs\n- include existing goal notifications in the SDK notification union\n- preserve ordinary turn-ID routing unchanged\n- add focused routing coverage\n\nThis PR does not expose a public goal API. It is the first PR in the\nPython goal operations stack.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- online CI, including the Python SDK suite\n- focused typed-notification routing coverage","verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:35:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a0f9134267e0fed2406fce0ea0f14e30894513e/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354"}]},{"sha":"8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlNjlkMjk1MjE0ODg1MDYxODJkMmI1ODE0ODUxY2RiYjkwYzEzNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:26:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:26:00Z"},"message":"Reduce TUI legacy core dependencies (#26711)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI still reached through `app-server-client::legacy_core` for\nthread-name normalization and project-instruction filename details. In\nparticular, checking the TUI's local filesystem for `/init` is incorrect\nfor remote app-server sessions, where the server owns the working\ndirectory and instruction discovery.\n\n## What changed\n\n- use the instruction source paths supplied by the app server to decide\nwhether `/init` should avoid overwriting project instructions\n- keep the small thread-name normalization helper local to the TUI\n- remove the now-unused instruction filename constants, utility module,\nand other unused `legacy_core` re-exports\n- make status helper tests independent of concrete instruction filenames\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-client`\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nslash_init_skips_when_project_instructions_are_loaded`\n- `just test -p codex-tui` ran 2,799 tests; 2,797 passed and two\nunrelated guardian feature-flag tests failed reproducibly in untouched\ncode\n\n### Manual test\n\nStarted an app server over WebSocket with a remote workspace containing\n`AGENTS.md`, then connected the TUI using `--remote`. After confirming\n`thread/start` returned the file in `instructionSources`, deleted\n`AGENTS.md` and ran `/init` in the existing session.\n\nThe TUI still reported that project instructions already existed and\nskipped `/init`. The trace contained no `turn/start` request, confirming\nthe decision came from app-server session state rather than a new\nclient-local filesystem check.","tree":{"sha":"93a6ddbc6210215fde7c104fbf0f31d46c5ffa91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/93a6ddbc6210215fde7c104fbf0f31d46c5ffa91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHbYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA17gQADcLq1EhMsxghmgHrGSaHDpU\n3sp+q1h27hxMSY/3Cymv5SIoOYlSpAfzJUbsM9Vh+Oap58pP1DkboTONevb3J+Qz\njET2OcXJE6XAoCUYR+dwWR8IbcUamYGNwaZSTr9KUaw3Ukii91FVF3GoJ0pE9cWa\nhgKraQXs71BJujpRV4XVrfGvfOA9BwE/grKSCjIgt94eTWALzIgeFVo+poIAaCz0\npRaPJe+3Uj4/fLOiYInRfwEoh6oBVGVPStOxeF1/pM8lHVnmgxEFGrPKcRD5ryng\nIcBAw7pZEyH69cfXCfYZnOmqA0S0CK8mYiWGplIYtN0WkqN/Hxa7V3IyOJ1hqZvD\n3868WR3R0XUlPYY97rGRoPz2OHiLjtLjJNVOyqigT3WAMbRy4uTOP7Q25lbvrTw8\nfGU+ZdkY0QjO6+wov+LDlLMyvDZO2akt81iprFAQ3QsZJAilN/mFwNhOKgJVoAL+\nq0MP+NKlMF/Ms6RX7n1Q/NMV940qdoVY5IZWCiRTgIYyFyKxBzfiMZmlMhw9g71K\nLxVHhMZio7XpGgwT1SyvXBABmW7rw3kLjYYN/ih3K5TDBdlq9cLtxS6cUTFme6IC\nhuxlOWzMfDUQkHjzquIJ1cn4aWAVwxhXtRXLibuKt2yZ7+qdY9HeuwtEdY7btfoi\nut8HbZGNY2TTfluyMrXZ\n=AL7N\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 93a6ddbc6210215fde7c104fbf0f31d46c5ffa91\nparent 36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781036760 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781036760 -0700\n\nReduce TUI legacy core dependencies (#26711)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI still reached through `app-server-client::legacy_core` for\nthread-name normalization and project-instruction filename details. In\nparticular, checking the TUI's local filesystem for `/init` is incorrect\nfor remote app-server sessions, where the server owns the working\ndirectory and instruction discovery.\n\n## What changed\n\n- use the instruction source paths supplied by the app server to decide\nwhether `/init` should avoid overwriting project instructions\n- keep the small thread-name normalization helper local to the TUI\n- remove the now-unused instruction filename constants, utility module,\nand other unused `legacy_core` re-exports\n- make status helper tests independent of concrete instruction filenames\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-client`\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nslash_init_skips_when_project_instructions_are_loaded`\n- `just test -p codex-tui` ran 2,799 tests; 2,797 passed and two\nunrelated guardian feature-flag tests failed reproducibly in untouched\ncode\n\n### Manual test\n\nStarted an app server over WebSocket with a remote workspace containing\n`AGENTS.md`, then connected the TUI using `--remote`. After confirming\n`thread/start` returned the file in `instructionSources`, deleted\n`AGENTS.md` and ran `/init` in the existing session.\n\nThe TUI still reported that project instructions already existed and\nskipped `/init`. The trace contained no `turn/start` request, confirming\nthe decision came from app-server session state rather than a new\nclient-local filesystem check.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:26:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e69d29521488506182d2b5814851cdbb90c1354/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7"}]},{"sha":"36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM2YmY2M2E1Y2YwMmRhZmIxNTc0YjIzOTY1OTdlZDFlZjE2YmI1ZDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:23:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:23:31Z"},"message":"Allow creating a new goal after completion (#26681)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers have indicated that they want an agent to be able to create a new\ngoal for itself after completing the previous goal. Currently, that's\nnot possible because agents cannot overwrite an existing goal even if\nit's complete. This PR removes this limitation and allows `create_goal`\nto overwrite an existing goal if it is in the `complete` state.\n\n## What changed\n\n`create_goal` now replaces the existing goal only when its status is\n`complete`. The replacement is performed atomically in the goal store,\ncreates a fresh active goal with reset usage, and continues to reject\ncreation while any unfinished goal exists. App server clients see a\nsingle `thread/goal/updated` event when the previous goal is replaced\nwith the new one.\n\nThe tool description and error message now reflect these semantics.\n\n## What didn't change\n\nAgents are not allowed to create a new goal (overwrite their existing\ngoal) if an existing goal is still active, blocked, paused, or in any\nother state other than \"completed\".","tree":{"sha":"e6d21c832567ddf66cb5aca21cc7cae0cede2974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e6d21c832567ddf66cb5aca21cc7cae0cede2974"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHZECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmLkQAAlH0rIGeaHVEUksVXiQt6ug\naLpKqEJPzF293EE+HWIiZQP8MJ8Vr6yw/1MVTfOPfL9cnfnRAFkOZuMK4eE5ype4\nik1H6X5XFDuq4bdaa+Tp9Yq68C6sEbp1FavlPZkjKWoF30rLJozZquM6jeI2y05l\nfx+Pwa9w63y91jhmuZEChRPYxIEc8xyAtV/TY0d0MNNB7b+tal25/5BtcKW57m4g\n+sciBXBuZzD5HUQmK/qagyMQk+mPoSKRbIH7Cw/v9WJIPphYq79kALIUxv8onLog\ndtJhQi5mkRcCW6TMEsaz1Iub3HX2+nlA2dSrSTKsh71YnmGdbqrFO0KDlHPH852+\nykUUo+AQNvjcgtynBp0tcUNCp3Ek0vZUxp7nh+epsCkj04AXBJnjNuZ9MSxYh0Fw\n1LcYd9X9lwen6OGJLwvGV6gzmm18vclGq6LsIvBiKTSBTcOw5TfMRgSRw5D5jlgn\nuZGmI8CqJrCcgxHzvwtf1faoAF9cjUwqmf8Tn+gBv8CcuRap+EFsWSeyj9GMlLqU\n806tIrEtbHFrIOER/89PgnLsy1kDO4l7NH3mSdREi368H7M9hWfz7deOWvnlycsc\n6mLKRw5E8L+8Lp6zk7xIdukuLeOpIbSItOwFMBSK6GYK3OeZBHdFeWYrufKPmQfd\nq3nAsdXHcjiFc9PQc5OA\n=z9KJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e6d21c832567ddf66cb5aca21cc7cae0cede2974\nparent 472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781036611 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781036611 -0700\n\nAllow creating a new goal after completion (#26681)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers have indicated that they want an agent to be able to create a new\ngoal for itself after completing the previous goal. Currently, that's\nnot possible because agents cannot overwrite an existing goal even if\nit's complete. This PR removes this limitation and allows `create_goal`\nto overwrite an existing goal if it is in the `complete` state.\n\n## What changed\n\n`create_goal` now replaces the existing goal only when its status is\n`complete`. The replacement is performed atomically in the goal store,\ncreates a fresh active goal with reset usage, and continues to reject\ncreation while any unfinished goal exists. App server clients see a\nsingle `thread/goal/updated` event when the previous goal is replaced\nwith the new one.\n\nThe tool description and error message now reflect these semantics.\n\n## What didn't change\n\nAgents are not allowed to create a new goal (overwrite their existing\ngoal) if an existing goal is still active, blocked, paused, or in any\nother state other than \"completed\".","verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:23:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36bf63a5cf02dafb1574b2396597ed1ef16bb5d7/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d"}]},{"sha":"472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ3MjYxOWY5ZmM2NzM5ZDVjNGZhNDk5YjNlZjEwMDA3NjU1YjAzMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:08:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T20:08:01Z"},"message":"Add SOCKS5 TCP MITM coverage (#22685)\n\n## Summary\n- reuse the MITM HTTPS serving path for raw SOCKS5 TCP streams\n- route limited-mode and hooked SOCKS5 TCP requests through MITM before\ndialing upstream\n- keep SOCKS5 UDP limited-mode behavior unchanged\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `just fix -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"e4dce444d2cba73d6c6c05fb319fc6d03a0485ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e4dce444d2cba73d6c6c05fb319fc6d03a0485ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKHKhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0mYQAKmzTDODCqI9uP5MQCESpX6O\nSCMUhkKgzscMjc90KrTebwjV1EPWezxk3nuVazhbKUXfpxQj19sPyGB5xYHCFFXI\nOdkVSgZw89EH5sxhrHVgO7f7SVyB105NXuJekh71ThRulhnjmp/vPF0fyCiPL2SQ\nWzGWXQ8hp0Ri6Ks1AqRLFTHAr1VVlTjcm2PlrLYb7I3gD0k4w+HLWseZsv0wdIuW\nqrwlcqkGcvgvMX1qX13FBLlZJ3yo9VLshKedz4Y8IWgWag7rUgeea0BIJSwGxNb9\n7I2A1RibVHouy/UY3LmuvItnYhw6eZQCiJDvlJXkW2wd+Sv25GDT32rYIBw6GrBz\nsgFMQaVMc6n8SyWogCmbGHg/+c3yHLcllX97E4OsyALZaZR+nFxg6L40/tCaZUhQ\n4d8jDKGOVsBK8e1Qt40Z2y1s/TA0V05dJKnDPiQFjxBtqUz1MZgEsqHknSnWIClP\n2kuq2XRfl/l3KQysD6rlfsD6t7/gepB9mpUlRORHubCBI9Y73N4cx7m8Fbf5o6nW\ngj0WSvhajqh8xjMuRWtNu3r1yFkOkKNkvgWTeM/YZ3MGi5i2vLQHMLHafMfv3aEq\nXq1WjUgVH+EpzBdl7oz/227Yfmseh+hvzdilhYBnvKyhHR1dZZ7riSeodUolnm/N\n7tcHYo3umPI8g2LxAhvy\n=MSUQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e4dce444d2cba73d6c6c05fb319fc6d03a0485ef\nparent 7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1781035681 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781035681 -0700\n\nAdd SOCKS5 TCP MITM coverage (#22685)\n\n## Summary\n- reuse the MITM HTTPS serving path for raw SOCKS5 TCP streams\n- route limited-mode and hooked SOCKS5 TCP requests through MITM before\ndialing upstream\n- keep SOCKS5 UDP limited-mode behavior unchanged\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `just fix -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T20:08:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/472619f9fc6739d5c4fa499b3ef10007655b031d/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5"}]},{"sha":"7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdhN2NlZTFiZTRlODI3MzNmMzkzYzk1MTgwMjQyZDExYjUwMDY0ZDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:52:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:52:05Z"},"message":"fix: use plugin service route for remote uninstall (#27223)","tree":{"sha":"6dd7dc74ac81de0150ebb659dba3292d278548fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6dd7dc74ac81de0150ebb659dba3292d278548fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKG7lCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbYwQAFxPIslpyWXiqkAizfD6xgVF\nPMq+CYBQys/TFX7urIORn1Ml8MT4A9pgncrv11EAnAYsV9edy2nAkN5/y7alAecG\n5XE5qPOtZ99QK4dDEU/p4OZ26UM83FTGGD3p87Fu7MiiuiP9Z/JNXaWPE6dLhAU/\n1kgXFiOkuw+4BMt0AJ7Cx7r3C36tqnvbOWI+oK0NLTC/Omw3LiCu84Gvg+LuICMf\nBQTcUvCjGaTlGWJ87jen6/NWfOE6m10HbMKo7NsNIpt0cbItNaonlzLPSQahwwGt\nOe2lN5vvZpH3j+TNT0BLNzo3iSAQOZ3kDxsh+D+eoWKhPf5SgXohUNqIgWoO1kmW\n4MXMLvVfSgzgORy0NhoFk1haADTTjntmwE5eW+RAkZAtodcUWSTvZgSW76suerhE\nRugTyLJ2xHRd9CyILNx70hxJlo2Q/xirPHyu3e59xeFiSrYaH5bYjAfHn9CXhLxs\ncbxPasCEMucLxF8meyN1FjtNjZ3FFlmtTvctip6dtAKqoYSkuShAhM+g1AXWkYie\nztxcoEhW9Fa36WcMOSnzbVYmF5ZS1qjTQYDw9b6T6TgrM2yyGRRATRGyXR9GaIjN\n1BXOIqabYc+gb9IIGd0f9/XT3uKL87yC3qvVJ6Xwruf8wo6HrLVx9HQfs27IVIe0\nPbcC+mu+1hwWQHjKAP5P\n=HgIV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6dd7dc74ac81de0150ebb659dba3292d278548fa\nparent 6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1781034725 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781034725 -0700\n\nfix: use plugin service route for remote uninstall (#27223)","verified_at":"2026-06-09T19:52:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7a7cee1be4e82733f393c95180242d11b50064d5/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef"}]},{"sha":"6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZlN2FiNTI5Mjk3YWMzZThlZjkxMTA3MThlMWVhYjY4OGQ0MzkxZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:48:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:48:04Z"},"message":"[codex] Speed up local nextest runs (#26479)\n\n## Why\n\n`just test` currently uses the CI-oriented nextest profile, which\nserializes app-server integration tests even on developer machines that\ncan run several safely. Bounded local parallelism substantially shortens\nthis common iteration loop without changing CI behavior.\n\nEight-worker experiments were faster, but keeping them reliable required\nrelaxing several test deadlines. Four workers for integration tests is a\nsolid tradeoff that speeds up local testing without needing to change\ntest logic.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a `local` nextest profile that inherits the existing defaults.\n- Allow up to four app-server integration tests to run concurrently\nunder that profile.\n- Make `just test` select the local profile on Unix and Windows.\n- Keep the default CI profile serialized and leave all test deadlines\nunchanged.\n\nThe tests use separate processes, randomized temporary `CODEX_HOME`\ndirectories, and ephemeral ports. The remaining shared constraints are\nsystem resources; each app-server also uses a multi-thread Tokio\nruntime, and fuzzy-search tests can create additional worker threads, so\nthe local cap remains intentionally conservative.\n\n## Performance and validation\n\nAll measurements below are warm, execution-only app-server runs with\nnextest retries disabled.\n\nOn the current rebased branch, an AMD EPYC 7763 machine with 16 logical\nCPUs and 62 GiB RAM completed three consecutive runs:\n\n| Run | Nextest time | Wall time | Result |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | 142.941s | 145.17s | 836/836 passed |\n| 2 | 143.402s | 145.59s | 836/836 passed |\n| 3 | 142.870s | 145.08s | 836/836 passed |\n\nThe mean wall time was 145.28s. The slow-inventory, approval replay, and\nzsh-fork tests all passed with their original deadlines.\n\nEarlier measurements on the same Linux machine, before the suite grew,\nshowed the scaling that motivated the change:\n\n| App-server concurrency | Nextest time | Result |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | 369.5s | 572/572 passed |\n| 2 | 194.5s | 572/572 passed |\n| 4 | 111.0s mean over 3 runs | 3/3 clean |\n\nFour workers reduced that execution time by about 70%, a roughly 3.3x\nspeedup over serialization.","tree":{"sha":"c9dc444871186c5415c0644c507536b9bbf3459b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c9dc444871186c5415c0644c507536b9bbf3459b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKG30CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlbsQAJArk+Sg3PzvEy/1eDmgM8Y+\nKB9WF/9h9/NonE9mvSL9qrhA+icBrlEfhfmTNj3NJE6aeW5KzVi9QgIEndugP9i3\nkYcGgNxCFzw3xKgm666M396UYOizRkto1lgnbuxer1psvDpA+IhFal/tX2PM3AJ/\nz/vhS4Wz/Spixf8TEIRP/PFFj6hRJgCYvnNcG4tv9CTQsaBNmX7Et+ywn4o4cJCm\n4MkZt3McKkBFTHdwvD42XD1upO4mHd1cWeuJ+xVOHkU594L8+63L9GKNz0uzl31i\nIuab8svd7M28LclTSalC25sJy2ySsnyvsnsL12vuX048lnCHTi4R1NqguB0+mqqJ\nAyKDMEoEJF5oZMgIAQvc6flq98CkyZ1vmXDOW14Uky1iVGyxto0ZRet45QtQOd9a\nP27rZi69WM6FtdOz6brjsFsXo7hQt85Yt3ejcBL7osUTSSXug46UmXaDsv2czORJ\ngqDc2NVMXT0ZaGEBtQ/RlXWH8gMqw2f3Utpej0O56j/kWr4Yhn8yfrXD5A6qYVGT\nhYvwT79gj30akUVM/Kz96PIowp4WjpwYOjIq45lcJM2/LymorXz8P5ykBMwr2dlb\nPtYncFdvwAZL1pt2BqAhQvHm/Am+W9Tv56MxGEeSYWb2RQmTmLdIcyjAU2GT9EWV\nZgutNie64goJH2f1KNug\n=0eDz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c9dc444871186c5415c0644c507536b9bbf3459b\nparent a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781034484 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781034484 -0700\n\n[codex] Speed up local nextest runs (#26479)\n\n## Why\n\n`just test` currently uses the CI-oriented nextest profile, which\nserializes app-server integration tests even on developer machines that\ncan run several safely. Bounded local parallelism substantially shortens\nthis common iteration loop without changing CI behavior.\n\nEight-worker experiments were faster, but keeping them reliable required\nrelaxing several test deadlines. Four workers for integration tests is a\nsolid tradeoff that speeds up local testing without needing to change\ntest logic.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a `local` nextest profile that inherits the existing defaults.\n- Allow up to four app-server integration tests to run concurrently\nunder that profile.\n- Make `just test` select the local profile on Unix and Windows.\n- Keep the default CI profile serialized and leave all test deadlines\nunchanged.\n\nThe tests use separate processes, randomized temporary `CODEX_HOME`\ndirectories, and ephemeral ports. The remaining shared constraints are\nsystem resources; each app-server also uses a multi-thread Tokio\nruntime, and fuzzy-search tests can create additional worker threads, so\nthe local cap remains intentionally conservative.\n\n## Performance and validation\n\nAll measurements below are warm, execution-only app-server runs with\nnextest retries disabled.\n\nOn the current rebased branch, an AMD EPYC 7763 machine with 16 logical\nCPUs and 62 GiB RAM completed three consecutive runs:\n\n| Run | Nextest time | Wall time | Result |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | 142.941s | 145.17s | 836/836 passed |\n| 2 | 143.402s | 145.59s | 836/836 passed |\n| 3 | 142.870s | 145.08s | 836/836 passed |\n\nThe mean wall time was 145.28s. The slow-inventory, approval replay, and\nzsh-fork tests all passed with their original deadlines.\n\nEarlier measurements on the same Linux machine, before the suite grew,\nshowed the scaling that motivated the change:\n\n| App-server concurrency | Nextest time | Result |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 1 | 369.5s | 572/572 passed |\n| 2 | 194.5s | 572/572 passed |\n| 4 | 111.0s mean over 3 runs | 3/3 clean |\n\nFour workers reduced that execution time by about 70%, a roughly 3.3x\nspeedup over serialization.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T19:48:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e7ab529297ac3e8ef9110718e1eab688d4391ef/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128"}]},{"sha":"a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE3MWUwNDBkZjUxZWMwZTFmNTUyM2JmMGZmNWYxYmVmMzk4NTgxMjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"marksteinbrick-oai","email":"mark.steinbrick@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:27:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T19:27:10Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] add extensible feature thread sources (#27063)\n\n## Why\n- `ThreadSource` currently defines a closed set of core-owned values\n- Product features also create threads for background or scheduled work\n- Adding every product-specific value to the core enum would require\nrepeated `codex-rs` protocol changes\n- Feature-backed values let product callers provide precise attribution\nwhile preserving the existing core classifications\n\n## What Changed\n- Adds `ThreadSource::Feature(String)` for app-owned thread source\nvalues\n- Represents all app-server v2 thread sources as scalar strings, so a\nfeature source is supplied as `\"automation\"`\n- Persists and emits the feature's plain string label, so `\"automation\"`\nproduces `thread_source=\"automation\"` in analytics\n- Keeps `user`, `subagent`, and `memory_consolidation` as explicit\ncore-owned values and regenerates the app-server schemas and TypeScript\nbindings\n\n## Verification\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo check --workspace`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol\nfeature_thread_source_serializes_as_its_app_owned_label`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol\nthread_sources_round_trip_as_scalar_labels`\n- `cargo test -p codex-analytics\nthread_initialized_event_serializes_expected_shape`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"013a16a6b9778a29ef6545663d9508b254918b26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/013a16a6b9778a29ef6545663d9508b254918b26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKGkOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+Z8QAJsEdms1SGDsKkIoIkVfKU6r\nVPzTZwv+HyDBf4jlXeh+3rzmBou14wJGf3YJvZmY4d+zUS3PQKi5G/ErSjtycThG\natHHhZHF/3jx0jGv/Mzp1L0zjkLK+a8qhU8SRQ8pjSVvYE4gCt8oISd7DXpAa5US\nmgsOUZn43aNQyB32MQ8KsX5FH0hGMHrxZ1KejgLkI1I39j0X4I9TCMXBVrCVlwIt\n/iXIcJRqREIyqT0eEZl/Q5vj55+bjRgdNlq6r24A81gRpdTxtxPaNbWHNuczqeZT\nLIsXYyKekpx1YgtvWt0LT2GyBDZ4XMtfD/sNtKv2e8c+CXMs6pBfvIUOYO35OodT\nAOlG8KaqSsaARVakgbZrk05Z42tAuI+ICRr4I6bEXKXbWe9EiDgVC3aBGhOdbOFW\nxv8r59VO6MyHMktZIM2CaoqY2BPC+rjCQ8BzOB3Uw3tN/K4BZUiDiFardczKy46G\n5ANIJHtxJ5y9/9fxupLCrlKyJpi+1E0lMLrPeHMlb+inTjBE/ntosLG/CSPXoO1Z\nvk7CfWOUHBpaaFvC+QN9yUrVx1HAJBeiOy1ZsJTrSVWq7C09D5SzQbqtL/4H6Yqi\nFGPX/RaKyPDc0L0+U7jERv9aSLlMbEDraNrgSX4/fgu0fcmrs3me0J0/dsGugF1k\nW8VvpYQ5hHcw99Wpwc7d\n=Po49\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 013a16a6b9778a29ef6545663d9508b254918b26\nparent 99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83\nauthor marksteinbrick-oai <mark.steinbrick@openai.com> 1781033230 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781033230 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] add extensible feature thread sources (#27063)\n\n## Why\n- `ThreadSource` currently defines a closed set of core-owned values\n- Product features also create threads for background or scheduled work\n- Adding every product-specific value to the core enum would require\nrepeated `codex-rs` protocol changes\n- Feature-backed values let product callers provide precise attribution\nwhile preserving the existing core classifications\n\n## What Changed\n- Adds `ThreadSource::Feature(String)` for app-owned thread source\nvalues\n- Represents all app-server v2 thread sources as scalar strings, so a\nfeature source is supplied as `\"automation\"`\n- Persists and emits the feature's plain string label, so `\"automation\"`\nproduces `thread_source=\"automation\"` in analytics\n- Keeps `user`, `subagent`, and `memory_consolidation` as explicit\ncore-owned values and regenerates the app-server schemas and TypeScript\nbindings\n\n## Verification\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo check --workspace`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol\nfeature_thread_source_serializes_as_its_app_owned_label`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol\nthread_sources_round_trip_as_scalar_labels`\n- `cargo test -p codex-analytics\nthread_initialized_event_serializes_expected_shape`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T19:27:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a71e040df51ec0e1f5523bf0ff5f1bef39858128/comments","author":{"login":"marksteinbrick-oai","id":219906558,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuB_g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/marksteinbrick-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83"}]},{"sha":"99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk5ZGE2OTdlNGM1YzFmYzkwODczMmE1OGI2NTQ4YmY5Y2MyMjdmODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T18:30:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T18:30:24Z"},"message":"[codex] Test extension API contracts (#26835)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-extension-api` defines contracts shared by extension crates and\ntheir hosts, but it had no direct test suite. Host and feature tests\ncover downstream behavior, while regressions in the API crate's own\ntyped state, registry ordering, and capability adapters could go\nunnoticed.\n\n## What\n\n- Add public-surface integration tests for `ExtensionData`, including\nconcurrent initialization and poison recovery.\n- Cover contributor registration order, approval short-circuiting, event\nsink retention, no-op response injection, and closure-based agent\nspawning.\n- Add the test-only dependencies used by the suite.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-extension-api`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-extension-api`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"6b57dd28d5781132b5a01f36b215e45bba456db0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6b57dd28d5781132b5a01f36b215e45bba456db0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKFvACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqlsQAHdlXppoU8z+5D71ZerHcM6q\n+XgarBijOVTp4qZ7SkyyiUt51zxKZLHctnRGSG5n3F9uYCezQhF2xqELXM/4KZig\nFwSxA8Gbq5s9DCNihtyfuDZNBHys1u2gFqxrHvwQlPpU9CpxQJrMDiSCIKL3GCb6\nLRQfoifdw+BsFoIVSVVIsh6+OVxb79/T2xavN6yarb6TWXofIkFgdrT697BCSRZT\ny4J/Wtff7jlSqK8xj/ehUDjwQNhu6mXiS37i0M1L1ej8wzqTez7TqMhRD22AHJ8w\npe0q3Dqp5lt3mHTYBmX1qNZm8bXXrOlgZQ/ogk9VHAbECJiVmC7V0/hMaNn9tURx\nxbzTQTchXTZ1ycA4WV+gT+6fhrdu7lQ42axzyvRYHJkq0a+lsVX68iIxXLtfWJNk\n18/oWkfVM7yZhB6UMIdyAp5axsZnSvK+IytEkInWKr6DXcRAqOSLMtsVu4ENA8f8\nvs4w21K7ebwOcIILXtxjdnuDnfCmruLg6pyXfGKgeSGXFjdxMKt9gD7+cqNuD4da\nIBNWDVMqBWul7PtQ80fNoPc9EcgmTcFUkaTdHZLoFRTMn4jZaA727tBFWx/h2OAX\ncUeYsTSdyHlasNrUq2YG4kPfG9JcJulLOPonzg9ENi9uT+lM5uLr0Ab6sThtOdEb\n20oHiFl9CUtZczl20YaD\n=RJ8+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6b57dd28d5781132b5a01f36b215e45bba456db0\nparent 89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781029824 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781029824 +0000\n\n[codex] Test extension API contracts (#26835)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-extension-api` defines contracts shared by extension crates and\ntheir hosts, but it had no direct test suite. Host and feature tests\ncover downstream behavior, while regressions in the API crate's own\ntyped state, registry ordering, and capability adapters could go\nunnoticed.\n\n## What\n\n- Add public-surface integration tests for `ExtensionData`, including\nconcurrent initialization and poison recovery.\n- Cover contributor registration order, approval short-circuiting, event\nsink retention, no-op response injection, and closure-based agent\nspawning.\n- Add the test-only dependencies used by the suite.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-extension-api`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-extension-api`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T18:30:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/99da697e4c5c1fc908732a58b6548bf9cc227f83/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb"}]},{"sha":"89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg5YWMzZWMyN2NhZTAwMDBkYTE0ZmJlNDE2MGE3OWVkNDY1ODQzZmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:51:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:51:54Z"},"message":"Load selected executor skills through extensions (#27184)\n\n## Why\n\nCCA is moving toward a split runtime where the orchestrator may not have\na filesystem, while executors can expose preinstalled plugins and\nskills. A thread therefore needs to select capabilities without asking\napp-server or core to interpret executor-owned paths through the\norchestrator's filesystem.\n\nThe longer-term model is broader than executor skills:\n\n- A plugin is a bundle of skills, MCP servers, connectors/apps, and\nhooks.\n- A plugin root can be local, executor-owned, or hosted by a backend.\n- Components inside one plugin can use different access and execution\nmechanisms. A skill may be read from a filesystem or through backend\ntools; an HTTP MCP server can run without an executor; a stdio MCP\nserver or hook needs an execution environment.\n- Core should carry generic extension initialization data. The extension\nthat owns a component should discover it, expose it to the model, and\ninvoke it through the appropriate runtime.\n\nThis PR establishes that architecture through one complete vertical:\nselecting a root on an executor, discovering the skills beneath it,\nexposing those skills to the model, and reading an explicitly invoked\n`SKILL.md` through the same executor.\n\n## Contract\n\n`thread/start` gains an experimental `selectedCapabilityRoots` field:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"selectedCapabilityRoots\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"deploy-plugin@1\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"type\": \"environment\",\n        \"environmentId\": \"workspace\",\n        \"path\": \"/opt/codex/plugins/deploy\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe root is intentionally not classified as a \"plugin\" or \"skill\" in the\nAPI. It can point at a standalone skill, a directory containing several\nskills, or a plugin containing skills and other components. This PR only\nteaches the skills extension how to consume it; later extensions can\nresolve MCP, connector, and hook components from the same selection.\n\nThe platform-supplied `id` is stable selection identity. The location\nsays which runtime owns the root and gives that runtime an opaque path.\nApp-server does not inspect or canonicalize the path.\n\n## What changed\n\n### Generic thread extension initialization\n\nApp-server converts selected roots into `ExtensionDataInit`. Core\ncarries that generic initialization value until the final thread ID is\nknown, then creates thread-scoped `ExtensionData` before lifecycle\ncontributors run.\n\nThis keeps `Session` and core independent of the capability-selection\ncontract. The initialization value is consumed during construction; it\nis not retained as another long-lived `Session` field.\n\n### Executor-backed skills\n\nThe skills extension now owns an `ExecutorSkillProvider` that:\n\n- resolves the selected environment through `EnvironmentManager`\n- discovers, canonicalizes, and reads skills through that environment's\n`ExecutorFileSystem`\n- contributes the bounded selected-skill catalog as stable developer\ncontext\n- reads an explicitly invoked skill body through the authority that\nlisted it\n- warns when an environment or root is unavailable\n- never falls back to the orchestrator filesystem for an executor-owned\nroot\n\nSkill catalog and instruction fragments have hard byte bounds, which\nalso bound them below the 10K-token per-item context limit. If a\nselected executor skill has the same name as a legacy local skill, the\nexecutor selection owns that invocation and the local body is not\ninjected a second time.\n\nExisting local and bundled skill loading remains in place. Omitting\n`selectedCapabilityRoots` therefore preserves current local-only\nbehavior.\n\n## Current semantics\n\n- Only environment-owned locations are represented in this first\ncontract.\n- Roots are resolved by the destination extension, not by app-server or\ncore.\n- An unavailable executor or invalid root produces a warning and no\ncapabilities from that root; it does not trigger a local-filesystem\nfallback.\n- Selection applies to a newly started active thread.\n- MCP servers, connectors, and hooks beneath a selected plugin root are\nnot activated yet.\n- Selection is not yet persisted or inherited across resume, fork, or\nsubagent creation. Existing local capabilities continue to behave as\nthey do today in those flows.\n\n## Planned vertical follow-ups\n\n1. **Hosted HTTP MCP:** add an extension-backed HTTP MCP source that\nworks without an executor, then replace the special-purpose MCP plugins\nloader with that implementation.\n2. **Executor MCP:** register and execute stdio MCP servers through the\nenvironment that owns the selected plugin root.\n3. **Backend skills:** add a hosted skill source whose catalog and\nbodies are accessed through extension tools rather than a filesystem.\n4. **Connectors and hooks:** activate those components through their\nowning extensions, using the same selected-root boundary and\ncomponent-specific runtime.\n5. **Durable selection:** define the desired-selection lifecycle,\npersist it, and make resume, fork, and subagent inheritance explicit\nrather than accidental.\n6. **Local convergence:** incrementally route existing local plugin,\nskill, and MCP loading through the same extension model while preserving\ncurrent local behavior.\n\nEach follow-up remains reviewable as an end-to-end capability. The\nplatform selects roots, generic thread extension data carries the\nselection, and the owning extension resolves and operates its component.\n\n## Verification\n\nCoverage added for:\n\n- app-server end-to-end discovery and explicit invocation of a skill\ninside an executor-selected plugin root\n- exclusive invocation when a selected executor skill collides with a\nlocal skill name\n- executor filesystem authority for discovery, canonicalization, and\nreads\n- thread extension initialization before lifecycle contributors run\n- stable executor catalog context, explicit invocation, context\nrebuilding, hidden skills, and preserved host/remote catalog behavior\n\nTargeted protocol, core-skills, skills-extension, core lifecycle, and\napp-server executor-skill tests were run during development.","tree":{"sha":"64c0878cc6275d6424f62618c3799c9b59a1c88d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/64c0878cc6275d6424f62618c3799c9b59a1c88d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKFK6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm14QADnybahvd1IUzGvfmrY32bjO\nvzzuwTu5DC2ynxtrgE5TtQ8yc8+siU1Ihm2YkstxMwhA08QRGplBU4IJqxEGefL0\nE/o0L+gpMboMdhTuDSwt6npWl5g7z6gkv2kcQDyS63nF/+RvZ8qVCDcJTDYsIKtD\nhwaGHDUn0b50UHoQ82zBO2YV9pC1sPQ6T0Wo7pljoI/TBY/yQBkZSk+72cBoi5Ga\nEHq0yINr46XpsSvQs3eQ5rvB7y9mJqcZhrk/abEM+ZPREDxGJIwyqD8SWU9bkeVP\nKkKO4VJyC9zR1+tnvtGmbwf+nNKn6UIyFr8OWYE8wshvudBeezRM/rgYXfWHSHVD\nXGqFTdmcRx3Ths+1Tjg3RNDHkUwriLZ6wkmJWwA6GJkUJHu+CuNusT3xOqbPVzdV\nec79qDqbMlfR7mtdjt0o5ZZ5S9UVSXFR7w/Qlh84vO5j6aAsqtR6LMnso1Q/otx2\ntSySqUlDvpEw1JtDlGJccdsVR+Pwz2NWqWvWZepYw7WoYx7xAhYHZz6tpeyGJlPN\nYs+Stu5w8sehbkZjokOJI+despBAO6eNuJvzSOV/O4ONQ9nMrILkBsajN7uaSSr+\nSTXs2dEd4GrREMOkLAWPnTpUEz97e0jGbX81mZTK74eFnqgJtDAN1fvkkUS2kDWe\nKJ/Z3KxLvrkXrvNRmPvu\n=20f4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 64c0878cc6275d6424f62618c3799c9b59a1c88d\nparent 1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781027514 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781027514 +0200\n\nLoad selected executor skills through extensions (#27184)\n\n## Why\n\nCCA is moving toward a split runtime where the orchestrator may not have\na filesystem, while executors can expose preinstalled plugins and\nskills. A thread therefore needs to select capabilities without asking\napp-server or core to interpret executor-owned paths through the\norchestrator's filesystem.\n\nThe longer-term model is broader than executor skills:\n\n- A plugin is a bundle of skills, MCP servers, connectors/apps, and\nhooks.\n- A plugin root can be local, executor-owned, or hosted by a backend.\n- Components inside one plugin can use different access and execution\nmechanisms. A skill may be read from a filesystem or through backend\ntools; an HTTP MCP server can run without an executor; a stdio MCP\nserver or hook needs an execution environment.\n- Core should carry generic extension initialization data. The extension\nthat owns a component should discover it, expose it to the model, and\ninvoke it through the appropriate runtime.\n\nThis PR establishes that architecture through one complete vertical:\nselecting a root on an executor, discovering the skills beneath it,\nexposing those skills to the model, and reading an explicitly invoked\n`SKILL.md` through the same executor.\n\n## Contract\n\n`thread/start` gains an experimental `selectedCapabilityRoots` field:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"selectedCapabilityRoots\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"deploy-plugin@1\",\n      \"location\": {\n        \"type\": \"environment\",\n        \"environmentId\": \"workspace\",\n        \"path\": \"/opt/codex/plugins/deploy\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe root is intentionally not classified as a \"plugin\" or \"skill\" in the\nAPI. It can point at a standalone skill, a directory containing several\nskills, or a plugin containing skills and other components. This PR only\nteaches the skills extension how to consume it; later extensions can\nresolve MCP, connector, and hook components from the same selection.\n\nThe platform-supplied `id` is stable selection identity. The location\nsays which runtime owns the root and gives that runtime an opaque path.\nApp-server does not inspect or canonicalize the path.\n\n## What changed\n\n### Generic thread extension initialization\n\nApp-server converts selected roots into `ExtensionDataInit`. Core\ncarries that generic initialization value until the final thread ID is\nknown, then creates thread-scoped `ExtensionData` before lifecycle\ncontributors run.\n\nThis keeps `Session` and core independent of the capability-selection\ncontract. The initialization value is consumed during construction; it\nis not retained as another long-lived `Session` field.\n\n### Executor-backed skills\n\nThe skills extension now owns an `ExecutorSkillProvider` that:\n\n- resolves the selected environment through `EnvironmentManager`\n- discovers, canonicalizes, and reads skills through that environment's\n`ExecutorFileSystem`\n- contributes the bounded selected-skill catalog as stable developer\ncontext\n- reads an explicitly invoked skill body through the authority that\nlisted it\n- warns when an environment or root is unavailable\n- never falls back to the orchestrator filesystem for an executor-owned\nroot\n\nSkill catalog and instruction fragments have hard byte bounds, which\nalso bound them below the 10K-token per-item context limit. If a\nselected executor skill has the same name as a legacy local skill, the\nexecutor selection owns that invocation and the local body is not\ninjected a second time.\n\nExisting local and bundled skill loading remains in place. Omitting\n`selectedCapabilityRoots` therefore preserves current local-only\nbehavior.\n\n## Current semantics\n\n- Only environment-owned locations are represented in this first\ncontract.\n- Roots are resolved by the destination extension, not by app-server or\ncore.\n- An unavailable executor or invalid root produces a warning and no\ncapabilities from that root; it does not trigger a local-filesystem\nfallback.\n- Selection applies to a newly started active thread.\n- MCP servers, connectors, and hooks beneath a selected plugin root are\nnot activated yet.\n- Selection is not yet persisted or inherited across resume, fork, or\nsubagent creation. Existing local capabilities continue to behave as\nthey do today in those flows.\n\n## Planned vertical follow-ups\n\n1. **Hosted HTTP MCP:** add an extension-backed HTTP MCP source that\nworks without an executor, then replace the special-purpose MCP plugins\nloader with that implementation.\n2. **Executor MCP:** register and execute stdio MCP servers through the\nenvironment that owns the selected plugin root.\n3. **Backend skills:** add a hosted skill source whose catalog and\nbodies are accessed through extension tools rather than a filesystem.\n4. **Connectors and hooks:** activate those components through their\nowning extensions, using the same selected-root boundary and\ncomponent-specific runtime.\n5. **Durable selection:** define the desired-selection lifecycle,\npersist it, and make resume, fork, and subagent inheritance explicit\nrather than accidental.\n6. **Local convergence:** incrementally route existing local plugin,\nskill, and MCP loading through the same extension model while preserving\ncurrent local behavior.\n\nEach follow-up remains reviewable as an end-to-end capability. The\nplatform selects roots, generic thread extension data carries the\nselection, and the owning extension resolves and operates its component.\n\n## Verification\n\nCoverage added for:\n\n- app-server end-to-end discovery and explicit invocation of a skill\ninside an executor-selected plugin root\n- exclusive invocation when a selected executor skill collides with a\nlocal skill name\n- executor filesystem authority for discovery, canonicalization, and\nreads\n- thread extension initialization before lifecycle contributors run\n- stable executor catalog context, explicit invocation, context\nrebuilding, hidden skills, and preserved host/remote catalog behavior\n\nTargeted protocol, core-skills, skills-extension, core lifecycle, and\napp-server executor-skill tests were run during development.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T17:51:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/89ac3ec27cae0000da14fbe4160a79ed465843fb/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a"}]},{"sha":"1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEwMjZlOWRlMWJlMjkyZWJiMDE1NzlkZmNjZTVhMzRhYjIyNDkxN2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:40:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T17:40:40Z"},"message":"app-server: reject direct input to multi-agent v2 sub-agents (#27173)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 sub-agents are owned and coordinated by their parent\nagent. Allowing an app-server client to start or steer turns on a\nspawned child bypasses the multi-agent messaging path and creates a\nsecond, conflicting source of work for that sub-agent.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Reject direct `turn/start` and `turn/steer` requests targeting\nmulti-agent v2 thread-spawn sub-agents.\n- Identify these targets using both the thread's resolved multi-agent\nversion and its `SubAgentSource::ThreadSpawn` session source, leaving\nroot threads, v1 agents, and other sub-agent types unchanged.\n- Return a consistent invalid-request error before validating or\napplying the submitted input.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added an app-server integration test that spawns a real multi-agent v2\nchild and verifies that direct `turn/start` and `turn/steer` requests\nare rejected.","tree":{"sha":"e47493145584af2a6f77226e1f03282f11415422","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e47493145584af2a6f77226e1f03282f11415422"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKFAYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASBwQABgmQh06VIiXsKpvYJsYdZlY\nauqDBNssJHuCWjd/keHGcd6RyCYZEhVSYxmoMYAWMx/B0VTyL2TzZBQF522AyD4u\nVzsjfinKGbHfZFOxXdKpzVk3J+LSyej/Di2xR9/eshlpPfadw1/bfjv05TUD9nHn\n+8tFLfaeYPGj1872jvk14J8LGD3ekHI8F69AbZBiPZvbgT3ZNTBcdBlb1LQE4ntK\nrQmMj9Zq8wYSf4/y/ohPNP+BDjEvnWWCUUYmu314YRe/X6+gixSOCsbIhZXeHmQA\nFFuekRYJlp8XxVs5G+T0suMWwe/sJSP11N5f3aV+5Fo111mg2XDrXNYkppVJbIOR\npFh2A3EI4/wvNQi/sg8SYTk8vjzfOzOFxqrDGf4MNl585EoJV7AuleYbMdk/BwwJ\nVnyQUNxImTNcoEfMzdx8pz8KMeLVB8wwd7wiUlrRPjFxkUPjznrzVijjfdlKZAot\n7LHB7XwZW9IykSoLrc4D2LuHHQPzHGk4AjtLgcgWgTuL0XPWPzVLL+T9gZoVAvGH\nueYXx15d79+HpQQG/XsCxv6om0LINcl4ZR4LhGazaEqZcotz6IIaB/RUL99Uqhwl\n30N718HOLCTiiI2Hq2QJaxynAKIgJyl10MmRVkHy6r6gGFYiA8BzxsdztRYsygQB\nSr7zSbjprbaZTaZDlXxj\n=6NKh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e47493145584af2a6f77226e1f03282f11415422\nparent 8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781026840 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781026840 +0200\n\napp-server: reject direct input to multi-agent v2 sub-agents (#27173)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 sub-agents are owned and coordinated by their parent\nagent. Allowing an app-server client to start or steer turns on a\nspawned child bypasses the multi-agent messaging path and creates a\nsecond, conflicting source of work for that sub-agent.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Reject direct `turn/start` and `turn/steer` requests targeting\nmulti-agent v2 thread-spawn sub-agents.\n- Identify these targets using both the thread's resolved multi-agent\nversion and its `SubAgentSource::ThreadSpawn` session source, leaving\nroot threads, v1 agents, and other sub-agent types unchanged.\n- Return a consistent invalid-request error before validating or\napplying the submitted input.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added an app-server integration test that spawns a real multi-agent v2\nchild and verifies that direct `turn/start` and `turn/steer` requests\nare rejected.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T17:40:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1026e9de1be292ebb01579dfcce5a34ab224917a/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7"}]},{"sha":"8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhhMjk5ZmI3MDQzYjY0NWNlY2I1MGIyMzliZWI3ZDBlOWU0YWM3ZTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T16:41:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T16:41:58Z"},"message":"fix: Prevent /review crash when entering Esc on steer message (#22879)\n\nThis changes the `/review` escape path so `Esc` no longer behaves like\nthe normal queued-follow-up interrupt flow while a review is running.\nSteering is not currently supported in `/review` mode, without this\nchange users are able to attempt a steer but it leads to a crash (see\n#22815). If the user has already tried to send additional guidance\nduring `/review`, the TUI now keeps the review running and shows a\nwarning that steer messages are not supported in that mode, while still\npointing users to `Ctrl+C` if they actually want to cancel. It also adds\nregression coverage for the review-specific warning behavior. When users\ndo cancel with Ctrl+C during /review, the TUI now tolerates the\nactive-turn race that can happen during review handoff, and any queued\nsteer messages are restored to the composer instead of being discarded.\n\n- Special-case `Esc` during an active `/review` when follow-up steer\ninput is pending or has already been deferred.\n- Show a clear warning instead of interrupting the running review.\n- Make the Ctrl+C cancel path during /review resilient to active-turn\nraces, while preserving any queued steer text by restoring it to the\ncomposer.\n- Add review-mode test coverage for the warning path.\n\n## Testing\n\n1. Start a `/review` with a diff large enough that the review stays\nactive for more than a few seconds.\n\n2. While the review is still running, type a follow-up / steer message,\nsubmit it, and then press `Esc`.\n   Before: `Esc` causes the TUI to close abruptly.  \nAfter: the review keeps running and the transcript shows a warning that\nsteer messages are not supported during `/review`, with guidance to use\n`Ctrl+C` if you want to cancel.\n\n3. Press `Ctrl+C` if you actually want to stop the review.  \nBefore: (after restarting the test since Pt. 2 crashed) this is the\nintentional cancellation path.\nAfter: this remains the intentional cancellation path, and any queued\nfollow-up steer text is restored to the composer instead of being lost.\n   \n## Note:\n`/review` mode explicitly does not support steering at this time (as\nnoted in `turn_processer.rs`, if we want to explore that in the future\nthis code will need to be modified). This change keeps unsupported steer\nattempts from crashing the TUI and preserves queued follow-up text if\nthe user cancels with Ctrl+C.","tree":{"sha":"d06408b79beb52ee97e2fab570d3303f3a1d29ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d06408b79beb52ee97e2fab570d3303f3a1d29ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKEJWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVpwQAJPSBcuDgnZ3qFrSAGneF3DL\npmM3lY5/LVUAp6yosGMlRuz7Y+ITzH3O5ZYO7PJq2tPC/K+COsuyUuMbbk/O2KDi\njUgkdGz4Un7pyPWVt0OBQryLRfX+DStqS/lMJu3K3DuBWpgKx60QeKeOlMyYqckA\nL5MvjSLGIjY4xBKqDjAE8VKn+rWCyZ8rhlTagzoAzO5ht4+OBLXvJ/u+FXNilMME\nvHx+tU0h7agxeMEVKgrk2Js/WnR9Bc69P/g4sxzdJ1Ll/L67a2IVoq1eRakzmRIt\nnpTEAyZhftTJR7Od36KR9x3QmWBRfYez3zMvwE5aQg5ASCo5juGc6wSa8jjEoL5K\n8qVhnQHk7Pyuvb4F3zE8/BKVHVJSRaASsalI3hekIRPf6p4JbYsVC2JUFwvMDwBA\ntSEfzXnuCb8tUU2DepQ5UoX6pj7g5LGqFBLLQEQMk9tjwr/PLXf+vOycZQvDGS1x\nHJjDknYGbgfuc1wCcFhKejWTlj3Ale/KVFmx5kwc5c+ZiPatXDrvsZeBq//A2k6/\nwBmhYwnC9atI5P4vgrrkjiRdWaI8w6HFpiOZxavfZWRkPWZ++NgYPfjW1sSewd/Q\n+P6Z7KJPQY5uDWlNSRQq0T7zDoCQudOTofbj3IdorDNeSPu3h5WnJsmMlrbHGyQM\nnfe3Alxe4eGgCFqfOeeH\n=vD6L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d06408b79beb52ee97e2fab570d3303f3a1d29ac\nparent 6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1781023318 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781023318 -0700\n\nfix: Prevent /review crash when entering Esc on steer message (#22879)\n\nThis changes the `/review` escape path so `Esc` no longer behaves like\nthe normal queued-follow-up interrupt flow while a review is running.\nSteering is not currently supported in `/review` mode, without this\nchange users are able to attempt a steer but it leads to a crash (see\n#22815). If the user has already tried to send additional guidance\nduring `/review`, the TUI now keeps the review running and shows a\nwarning that steer messages are not supported in that mode, while still\npointing users to `Ctrl+C` if they actually want to cancel. It also adds\nregression coverage for the review-specific warning behavior. When users\ndo cancel with Ctrl+C during /review, the TUI now tolerates the\nactive-turn race that can happen during review handoff, and any queued\nsteer messages are restored to the composer instead of being discarded.\n\n- Special-case `Esc` during an active `/review` when follow-up steer\ninput is pending or has already been deferred.\n- Show a clear warning instead of interrupting the running review.\n- Make the Ctrl+C cancel path during /review resilient to active-turn\nraces, while preserving any queued steer text by restoring it to the\ncomposer.\n- Add review-mode test coverage for the warning path.\n\n## Testing\n\n1. Start a `/review` with a diff large enough that the review stays\nactive for more than a few seconds.\n\n2. While the review is still running, type a follow-up / steer message,\nsubmit it, and then press `Esc`.\n   Before: `Esc` causes the TUI to close abruptly.  \nAfter: the review keeps running and the transcript shows a warning that\nsteer messages are not supported during `/review`, with guidance to use\n`Ctrl+C` if you want to cancel.\n\n3. Press `Ctrl+C` if you actually want to stop the review.  \nBefore: (after restarting the test since Pt. 2 crashed) this is the\nintentional cancellation path.\nAfter: this remains the intentional cancellation path, and any queued\nfollow-up steer text is restored to the composer instead of being lost.\n   \n## Note:\n`/review` mode explicitly does not support steering at this time (as\nnoted in `turn_processer.rs`, if we want to explore that in the future\nthis code will need to be modified). This change keeps unsupported steer\nattempts from crashing the TUI and preserves queued follow-up text if\nthe user cancels with Ctrl+C.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T16:41:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a299fb7043b645cecb50b239beb7d0e9e4ac7e7/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7"}]},{"sha":"6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZhOWE0OWIzMzRlODA4MTc1NjkzNGIwY2U3ZDkwOTIzNGI1M2FhYzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Zanie Blue","email":"zanie@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T16:16:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T16:16:27Z"},"message":"Avoid rereading rollout history during cold resume (#27031)\n\n## Summary\n\n- reuse the history-bearing `StoredThread` loaded while probing for a\nrunning thread\n- avoid rereading and reparsing the rollout when that probe finds no\nactive process\n- reload after shutting down a loaded thread because shutdown may flush\nnewer rollout items\n- add a regression test that verifies cold resume performs one\nhistory-bearing store read\n\n## Problem\n\n`thread/resume` first reads the persisted thread with history while\nchecking whether the thread is\nalready running. When no running process exists, cold resume currently\nfalls through to\n`resume_thread_from_rollout`, which reads and parses the same history\nagain.\n\nThat duplicate work grows with rollout size and remains on the\nsynchronous resume path even when\nthe caller requests `excludeTurns`.\n\n## Background\n\nThe duplicate read was introduced by #24528, which fixed resume\noverrides for idle cached\nthreads. To support resumes specified by rollout path,\n`resume_running_thread` began loading the\nstored thread with history so it could resolve the canonical thread ID\nand determine whether a\ncached `CodexThread` was already loaded.\n\nThat history is needed when the loaded-thread path handles the request.\nOn a cold miss, however,\nthe function's boolean result could only report that no loaded thread\nhandled the request. It\ndiscarded the history-bearing `StoredThread`, and the normal cold-resume\npath immediately loaded\nand parsed the same rollout again.\n\nThis change preserves the idle cached-thread behavior from #24528 while\nallowing the cold-resume\npath to reuse the probe result.\n\n## Performance\n\nI benchmarked real retained rollouts using isolated `CODEX_HOME`\ndirectories, explicit rollout\npaths, debug builds of the commit and its exact parent, and alternating\nparent/patch order. The\ntable below uses `thread/resume` with `excludeTurns: true`; response\npayload sizes were identical.\n\n| Rollout size | Records | Parent median | Patch median | Median paired\nsaving |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 6 MB | 3,574 | 541 ms | 441 ms | 132 ms |\n| 30 MB | 15,220 | 1.505 s | 1.041 s | 701 ms |\n| 60 MB | 31,453 | 2.644 s | 1.742 s | 970 ms |\n| 149 MB | 100,874 | 10.506 s | 7.156 s | 3.350 s |\n| 559 MB | 259,734 | 27.759 s | 16.725 s | 9.836 s |\n\nThe absolute saving increases with thread size, as expected when\nremoving one complete JSONL\nhistory read and parse. Total resume time is also content-dependent, so\nthe relationship is not\nperfectly linear.\n\nI also tested full-history resume with `excludeTurns: false`. The\nresponse payload was\nbyte-identical between variants, and the same size-dependent improvement\nremained visible:\n\n| Rollout size | Parent median | Patch median | Median paired saving |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 6 MB | 1.052 s | 904 ms | 270 ms |\n| 30 MB | 2.667 s | 1.762 s | 924 ms |\n| 60 MB | 8.464 s | 6.272 s | 3.680 s |\n| 149 MB | 26.719 s | 12.118 s | 14.601 s |\n| 559 MB | 40.359 s | 25.475 s | 16.590 s |\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\ncold_thread_resume_reuses_non_local_history_probe`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"164b426e9087442537b1eab2244ec7286f83fae6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/164b426e9087442537b1eab2244ec7286f83fae6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKDxbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyGwQAHxK8Ffe/Vxq+D9EgVZqYZC9\nOvBzPtlyTBkIAAcPBTKjfbDbLLH1JcaweGBFmpshhF2Mu4Cng4LShPonMfQR4H+K\n5pRJ91anB1vDB43X9+LrWjJidClR7ScXhe6y8Ot1sAt9V8GrrgVH562NcPjMIvhw\nPHfPxQS60T0CAdQTMfldsKFTIYpevF3WekSG/JC8MqzbS3k6KyPK+HI4yU/1pXfu\nTPf/XNzdQw/9gqA5TRaWLyQ9qiCV2QdHGCjYQB4Js9akQXA6txDPgLFzQvSL/CYx\nViwZNeWSOKMdOl2xbtVP8IU6zsgSwH7GNvfXhXOGRjwN/tnB3hURWCxugnuhOX0p\nLxrYaerEp5aH/RF/i5NKOQh3DPW+WW32eeGyKVkW2Kp54oCXnJLv+GYNt5io12pT\nWsZJ1+h8iF0JPx7Dfic59g/ExjzD0EgIIr2fbuvRKNDTKVvw+mrRvbS9CPoyPL7L\nox+vkJhqwTOcsR7o+WHYn088clgrJEZotNPwbtmHGcO9Xw64oU95C1qyvGOrRQgR\nVXglHreKTub1tw3iR+6nE0rKrY7anOx3xiXNeCQkqmA6sgJO0svtP5sKSGvb8M4V\nY3/lF2l8kKpQez+qfbsgNU+Qviw4SY8ti2onhMSpZYGL0RSNLwO0neYYDVYT5eI8\nCxrcocKPGwiNF+Wy7xvL\n=myZs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 164b426e9087442537b1eab2244ec7286f83fae6\nparent 18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4\nauthor Zanie Blue <zanie@openai.com> 1781021787 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781021787 -0500\n\nAvoid rereading rollout history during cold resume (#27031)\n\n## Summary\n\n- reuse the history-bearing `StoredThread` loaded while probing for a\nrunning thread\n- avoid rereading and reparsing the rollout when that probe finds no\nactive process\n- reload after shutting down a loaded thread because shutdown may flush\nnewer rollout items\n- add a regression test that verifies cold resume performs one\nhistory-bearing store read\n\n## Problem\n\n`thread/resume` first reads the persisted thread with history while\nchecking whether the thread is\nalready running. When no running process exists, cold resume currently\nfalls through to\n`resume_thread_from_rollout`, which reads and parses the same history\nagain.\n\nThat duplicate work grows with rollout size and remains on the\nsynchronous resume path even when\nthe caller requests `excludeTurns`.\n\n## Background\n\nThe duplicate read was introduced by #24528, which fixed resume\noverrides for idle cached\nthreads. To support resumes specified by rollout path,\n`resume_running_thread` began loading the\nstored thread with history so it could resolve the canonical thread ID\nand determine whether a\ncached `CodexThread` was already loaded.\n\nThat history is needed when the loaded-thread path handles the request.\nOn a cold miss, however,\nthe function's boolean result could only report that no loaded thread\nhandled the request. It\ndiscarded the history-bearing `StoredThread`, and the normal cold-resume\npath immediately loaded\nand parsed the same rollout again.\n\nThis change preserves the idle cached-thread behavior from #24528 while\nallowing the cold-resume\npath to reuse the probe result.\n\n## Performance\n\nI benchmarked real retained rollouts using isolated `CODEX_HOME`\ndirectories, explicit rollout\npaths, debug builds of the commit and its exact parent, and alternating\nparent/patch order. The\ntable below uses `thread/resume` with `excludeTurns: true`; response\npayload sizes were identical.\n\n| Rollout size | Records | Parent median | Patch median | Median paired\nsaving |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 6 MB | 3,574 | 541 ms | 441 ms | 132 ms |\n| 30 MB | 15,220 | 1.505 s | 1.041 s | 701 ms |\n| 60 MB | 31,453 | 2.644 s | 1.742 s | 970 ms |\n| 149 MB | 100,874 | 10.506 s | 7.156 s | 3.350 s |\n| 559 MB | 259,734 | 27.759 s | 16.725 s | 9.836 s |\n\nThe absolute saving increases with thread size, as expected when\nremoving one complete JSONL\nhistory read and parse. Total resume time is also content-dependent, so\nthe relationship is not\nperfectly linear.\n\nI also tested full-history resume with `excludeTurns: false`. The\nresponse payload was\nbyte-identical between variants, and the same size-dependent improvement\nremained visible:\n\n| Rollout size | Parent median | Patch median | Median paired saving |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 6 MB | 1.052 s | 904 ms | 270 ms |\n| 30 MB | 2.667 s | 1.762 s | 924 ms |\n| 60 MB | 8.464 s | 6.272 s | 3.680 s |\n| 149 MB | 26.719 s | 12.118 s | 14.601 s |\n| 559 MB | 40.359 s | 25.475 s | 16.590 s |\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\ncold_thread_resume_reuses_non_local_history_probe`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T16:16:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6a9a49b334e8081756934b0ce7d909234b53aac7/comments","author":{"login":"zanie-oai","id":282067757,"node_id":"U_kgDOENADLQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282067757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/zanie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4"}]},{"sha":"18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE4Y2U2NzFmZWQ1MjZiZTkwMzM5MDdiZDg4YTNhNjNjNjg4OGJiZjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Zanie Blue","email":"zanie@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T15:50:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T15:50:13Z"},"message":"Avoid no-op backfill state writes (#26420)\n\n## Summary\n\n- avoid acquiring SQLite's writer slot when the singleton backfill row\nalready exists\n- preserve race-safe repair when the row is missing\n- add regressions for writer contention and missing-row repair\n\n## Why\n\nState runtime initialization and backfill-state reads previously\nexecuted\n`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` even in the steady state. SQLite\nstill\nenters the writer path for that statement, so TUI and app-server startup\ncould\nwait behind another writer for up to the configured five-second busy\ntimeout.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-state` (134 tests passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-state`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"25af4b96af0003b3e2361d022afb259997762995","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/25af4b96af0003b3e2361d022afb259997762995"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKDY1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9yMQAKmlq2SY12Y6TsYs0icbGpkW\nFunesVJEHO9P/EjkcTh1Qwltw1m+YrkrajYTzp1kYAynVNnTmHvQxafQK5EZL1zE\npi2oYxzTBAa21XfpyzalJbHe6xrKcEbDl3MIfBQtPOJogetPHM9sqmzi9nVNNHvB\n7H3ZlmSlx11T1+8mJF4nOpvoCFXnAIVkwca1jna8v5DWloJuDvAU1TnssPyQj8sZ\nSp94Up7Qmr9r23QanOJMslWj5qXwIQQzTH++GEddpF/vuHj3KrKqXymHmzAuK0Hb\nQifYqxzA7sNY3Gw3/vPyCmVTsI8/fAV9Br+Tz5Kae7UEJKq/mApuvjrqInmIBNng\n1jjqvJXVGGUQ94AlCV7gBx3Nt8hwyHsJWV9LHO2ZYaxObrKRgEhM262NiQz0GaK4\n+Jigy7iP3vt9x6XWebUGy00vFHGcjpwxaUMqlAHawfsqTqsHPPqYNd7vVb7iMC8s\nSf27LYiFCj+j7HrUOPdJCKKfLpxqt05kyuLHiKPBztJzilKcR2vO1tVpQ40ytB1z\nWeGzRdK9v7T18olhpVjGI0rBUEzMFIIp20jzZojg+cRq+ofRmoYBb8Vzbi0dS+Kq\nPmq7e1Yv/AnbBOw538HdBb6dsh9Nxdy2k4lWGGbLxI3ugIYQFMvdsnT1+FO/JJ6C\no6eid10CVl2/os+G9hig\n=oKIE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 25af4b96af0003b3e2361d022afb259997762995\nparent a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59\nauthor Zanie Blue <zanie@openai.com> 1781020213 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781020213 -0500\n\nAvoid no-op backfill state writes (#26420)\n\n## Summary\n\n- avoid acquiring SQLite's writer slot when the singleton backfill row\nalready exists\n- preserve race-safe repair when the row is missing\n- add regressions for writer contention and missing-row repair\n\n## Why\n\nState runtime initialization and backfill-state reads previously\nexecuted\n`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` even in the steady state. SQLite\nstill\nenters the writer path for that statement, so TUI and app-server startup\ncould\nwait behind another writer for up to the configured five-second busy\ntimeout.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-state` (134 tests passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-state`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T15:50:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18ce671fed526be9033907bd88a3a63c6888bbf4/comments","author":{"login":"zanie-oai","id":282067757,"node_id":"U_kgDOENADLQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282067757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/zanie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59"}]},{"sha":"a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE3NzBlNWI4NDcwZDMzMjBlYjUzYTU2YTI4NmVhNGEwYTcwYTFmNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T15:29:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T15:29:32Z"},"message":"[codex] Ignore pending PR review comments (#27080)\n\n## Why\n\nThe PR babysitter could surface inline comments from a GitHub review\nthat was still in the `PENDING` state. That allowed Codex to start\nacting on feedback before the reviewer submitted it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Correlate inline comments with their parent review and ignore pending\nreviews and their comments.\n- Remove pending review IDs from saved watcher state so the feedback\nsurfaces normally after publication.\n- Update the skill instructions and add regression coverage for the\ndraft-to-published transition.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python3 -m pytest\n.codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/test_gh_pr_watch.py`\n- Skill package validation with `quick_validate.py`\n- Live verification on #26835: the draft comment stayed hidden and\nsurfaced after the review was submitted.","tree":{"sha":"4e213d98445b4cda7e7b28aed6abe2d05d9c7b41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4e213d98445b4cda7e7b28aed6abe2d05d9c7b41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKDFcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsKwQAF55SPCWVmuIsQd9a4OnJDvU\nO2Yj6du56EoeCUOdo9hROYvBOD2Db+18vr5777WcU74bJqFbz7jaEK89rfcoy7a9\nhYDaLhBiNkAOg9wlQ9N6mX+6YXk8HMfNg/d4UZM1fzUSTcldCp1589AHjaJLw5XO\n9EgmHMMYhPkauA4Q9+QNP9vd2z8f1rsUpvTgVl0nMVfM5AQmT+enO2tuF8S1LsmW\nHi2Geb7mRNiqhR2/34k7UwKHT1E7AJSwug67dWBadOKFBpCg+i5crfQ/M/v+xqN4\neTfcD7ceRc2ZMK7fDwtRyyx9CtrM/3PUyS9lGju98LosbLppRX6yj2KdKk8twmMe\nCivDpfuSqgQAGAf02gv+ULLC60L9cwInEuWBn/OBvEzM/+7j4AUpnlKAIz7oN1yf\nhlE1oCvqpLaHGW0Tg5Za7waWj7NspO6bteZ4+efmvL9YVQ7tUFwljUqCOIaOzSEv\n9OXToi+pPrdMqyl8tZ9VRZeywwpykl1azwwD79SpwP9Uqz3uZG+U0Mlru2NriqYU\nfm0kS6GgE/Rc2KiFh7Yzg39h91+HIxwYHIVkHV6kCDqMu4Pii+0Qt4mzltyI+yB3\nTZ+rVNPl9sxiyc0skYPSUTPaooRiPdG6g/eq8CruQivS090sOrOeMcSRXJhnSD8R\nxF6eoc8tTIt33TocMPTl\n=pg3V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4e213d98445b4cda7e7b28aed6abe2d05d9c7b41\nparent 1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781018972 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781018972 -0700\n\n[codex] Ignore pending PR review comments (#27080)\n\n## Why\n\nThe PR babysitter could surface inline comments from a GitHub review\nthat was still in the `PENDING` state. That allowed Codex to start\nacting on feedback before the reviewer submitted it.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Correlate inline comments with their parent review and ignore pending\nreviews and their comments.\n- Remove pending review IDs from saved watcher state so the feedback\nsurfaces normally after publication.\n- Update the skill instructions and add regression coverage for the\ndraft-to-published transition.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python3 -m pytest\n.codex/skills/babysit-pr/scripts/test_gh_pr_watch.py`\n- Skill package validation with `quick_validate.py`\n- Live verification on #26835: the draft comment stayed hidden and\nsurfaced after the review was submitted.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T15:29:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a770e5b8470d3320eb53a56a286ea4a0a70a1f59/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0"}]},{"sha":"1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE1NDc3ODU2NTc2MDcwNDMzMDlmYmUxOWQ4MjZhZWE4ZWU2ZTQwZTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T11:27:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T11:27:53Z"},"message":"app-server: clear stale thread watches after v2 agent interruption (#27166)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #27007 moved MultiAgentV2 interruption reporting from the legacy\ncollaboration close event to `SubAgentActivity::Interrupted`.\nApp-server's missing-thread cleanup still ran only for the legacy event,\nso an interrupted child that had already been unloaded could remain\nmarked as loaded and running in `ThreadWatchManager`. That leaves thread\nstatus and running-turn accounting stale, including the count used\nduring graceful shutdown.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Handle `SubAgentActivity::Interrupted` separately in app-server event\nprocessing.\n- Remove the child's thread watch when `ThreadManager` no longer has\nthat thread.\n- Continue forwarding the same completed sub-agent activity notification\nto clients.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added a regression test that starts with a running watch for an\nunloaded child, applies the interrupted activity event, and verifies the\nwatch is removed, the running count returns to zero, and the client\nnotification is still emitted.","tree":{"sha":"c41a3ebd0de50f19697cbcf52a293859ad0e99f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c41a3ebd0de50f19697cbcf52a293859ad0e99f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ/i5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJawQAFH8C2/lcDY31Czdnn/4iiHr\neLfZrkNgM8Zb2roGV50rtuRC6dOzbvmcB0xjnF4ASulsab2+yYeqWTcBX+/scozr\nJzyps+F/OCczL4WG5dkzGjzzqx8nuY6hTwUt7kS82OeLSEGBfLCBX0DzSWxR9ZuF\n5Li2zSYBav/zmYlGmqh/VWKI8DO6aXB2hINOnHW43P1ghs7KRRKwzU2gMtwNmbY6\nUqOXAVzf/IAovno6p3smD6EnJqIdyc++5K5op4eaQjHk50vihASS7G9fiaxPknA0\nl+ddKkx6VH3oZLegTSV7Hefd88zQzo3Cuy+/djCTiIkUFSfZaUWCbu6bFIppKKiL\nGGyoqScn36pv6XerJmiVBbS7YMaOhxMT83D9pkoH9iMrGVahG/FU1mBXk68YpmLd\nbstJjZmRlkRSgyFMKp8yhB4gL13y2u7pB9nEy4ysuovCafLeqV2jQLDVpS1NDXC0\npYVafcI80ozwvvJEpSGzMT2gz4aDleGXyf2czZFOtuXgeCbihbD9Pn1dusRLH7Mg\nQAdLZDjg+ZBTnx2frsJgbS3M8XENeLldkmUtcTBVxrSO9b+83lelLKqmBhzIYRT9\ne5b8uzMdiNlAopyH2Gc6zT+ShIVPEB1UOxAhIpOz2AL+ZrKztsJbH+gQt5QnClEC\n7MbVK1x8dt1wkT2C3h8A\n=mfLY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c41a3ebd0de50f19697cbcf52a293859ad0e99f5\nparent fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781004473 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781004473 +0200\n\napp-server: clear stale thread watches after v2 agent interruption (#27166)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #27007 moved MultiAgentV2 interruption reporting from the legacy\ncollaboration close event to `SubAgentActivity::Interrupted`.\nApp-server's missing-thread cleanup still ran only for the legacy event,\nso an interrupted child that had already been unloaded could remain\nmarked as loaded and running in `ThreadWatchManager`. That leaves thread\nstatus and running-turn accounting stale, including the count used\nduring graceful shutdown.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Handle `SubAgentActivity::Interrupted` separately in app-server event\nprocessing.\n- Remove the child's thread watch when `ThreadManager` no longer has\nthat thread.\n- Continue forwarding the same completed sub-agent activity notification\nto clients.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added a regression test that starts with a running watch for an\nunloaded child, applies the interrupted activity event, and verifies the\nwatch is removed, the running count returns to zero, and the client\nnotification is still emitted.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T11:27:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1547785657607043309fbe19d826aea8ee6e40e0/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b"}]},{"sha":"fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZhZTI3MDkzMjA2NTM1NWI1ZDdmMTk3YjNmMWM3MjkxMjU4ODM2OWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T10:14:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T10:14:48Z"},"message":"multi-agent: add path-based v2 activity tracking (#27007)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 identifies agents by canonical paths, but its tool\nhandlers still emitted the larger legacy collaboration begin/end events\nbuilt around nickname and role metadata. App-server, rollout-trace,\nanalytics, and TUI consumers therefore lacked one compact path-based\ncompletion signal that behaved consistently across live events and\nreplay.\n\nThe TUI also needs a bounded `/agent` status surface for v2 agents. It\nshould use recent local activity for previews, refresh liveness without\nloading full histories, and keep the legacy picker available when no\npath-backed v2 agent is known.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the v2 `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, and\n`interrupt_agent` legacy lifecycle emissions with a success-only\n`SubAgentActivity` event. The event records the tool call ID, occurrence\ntime, affected thread, canonical agent path, and `started`,\n`interacted`, or `interrupted` kind.\n- Expose the activity as a completion-only app-server v2\n`subAgentActivity` thread item in live notifications and reconstructed\nhistory, regenerate the protocol schemas, and count it in sub-agent tool\nanalytics.\n- Track canonical paths from live activity and loaded-thread metadata in\nthe TUI, and render the activity in live and replayed transcripts.\n- Make `/agent` list running path-backed agents with summaries from\nbounded local event buffers. Each summary is capped at 240 graphemes,\nthe scan is capped at six recent items, only the last three wrapped\nlines are shown, and command output is omitted. Liveness falls back to\nmetadata-only `thread/read` when local turn state is unavailable.\n- Persist the activity as a terminal rollout-trace runtime payload and\nreduce it to the corresponding spawn, send, follow-up, or close\ninteraction edge. `interrupt_agent` is classified as a close-edge\noperation.\n- Preserve the legacy picker when no path-backed v2 agent is known.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nApp-server v2 clients that consumed `collabAgentToolCall` begin/end\npairs for these tools must handle the new completion-only\n`subAgentActivity` item. Legacy v1 collaboration behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Screenshot\n\n<img width=\"684\" height=\"288\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-08 at 15 40 47\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/194b3cd0-619d-45fb-b587-cf3e2b1b8a1d\"\n/>\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace`\n- Added focused coverage for activity analytics, terminal trace\nserialization, spawn-edge reduction, `interrupt_agent` classification,\nTUI status rendering without aggregated command output, and clearing\nstale running state after a completed turn.","tree":{"sha":"596ffba2b27988889fa263ba989dad40d831a883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/596ffba2b27988889fa263ba989dad40d831a883"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ+eYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKGkQAElUTfg4US8P0bWE/k9UXQ0N\n4xmyV/yWaQRGxuKfaRnLpINX4ZL7GGcvf7q/Iwl1K0ZRgsXMXVe0MhYAXfSu9I1f\nf/T4MxT95p3TbAzavFrTZAR87CykiMMkxi0euoWEM8GCT3t5SAkoNKgEdv6n8aJ3\nYPM/J1W7/zBfgNXv9xIF8tJw4VwmaXdPf3XniyWpRzu1bcoaDyJ1IDDGLyIsQsaj\nBJcu47MIgeHBC+y7IGYma8nwFJe4UQHqzV0YPX424rxqblsCQ7IrL82vy0tmWlSv\nazsZ/pkIX/YS96zmrAtuvJUNB7oLlY6TNX3YOGfQKrVthgh1hPBlVj5eTEKusDVF\nhu0C5Pu53FukYGY9C7vSk0QIVaa2EURFaPl7ZYI5CpqfYPyMNIBy7EvVCeKnCkRO\nGo4K68hsW2zMr6jsj9HHKC+wBdSXI7gWgTjS5hY0nrxJzMW1UZ6cvkTwY9RQUFX4\nMZ2lMaga7vIpf4e+6UUd/sRu5+IRYHAdwinEPnOCPq1xTayg7hofNrHyr+b/nIOC\n/xP0xQA5t2FdsLSP8a8Fz5/o3nz4cAz41lckaUR5DVyekwwysh9lDlJSBbljWRrG\nLRlym5LNmVEVt+315aeoQEEjo5jcOFbAUd+aJnFfDo/az0W1RqGot3R+Rh9URtVn\n9f2JHUWV7+BFyKehxUqm\n=TZzf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 596ffba2b27988889fa263ba989dad40d831a883\nparent a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781000088 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781000088 +0200\n\nmulti-agent: add path-based v2 activity tracking (#27007)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 identifies agents by canonical paths, but its tool\nhandlers still emitted the larger legacy collaboration begin/end events\nbuilt around nickname and role metadata. App-server, rollout-trace,\nanalytics, and TUI consumers therefore lacked one compact path-based\ncompletion signal that behaved consistently across live events and\nreplay.\n\nThe TUI also needs a bounded `/agent` status surface for v2 agents. It\nshould use recent local activity for previews, refresh liveness without\nloading full histories, and keep the legacy picker available when no\npath-backed v2 agent is known.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the v2 `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, and\n`interrupt_agent` legacy lifecycle emissions with a success-only\n`SubAgentActivity` event. The event records the tool call ID, occurrence\ntime, affected thread, canonical agent path, and `started`,\n`interacted`, or `interrupted` kind.\n- Expose the activity as a completion-only app-server v2\n`subAgentActivity` thread item in live notifications and reconstructed\nhistory, regenerate the protocol schemas, and count it in sub-agent tool\nanalytics.\n- Track canonical paths from live activity and loaded-thread metadata in\nthe TUI, and render the activity in live and replayed transcripts.\n- Make `/agent` list running path-backed agents with summaries from\nbounded local event buffers. Each summary is capped at 240 graphemes,\nthe scan is capped at six recent items, only the last three wrapped\nlines are shown, and command output is omitted. Liveness falls back to\nmetadata-only `thread/read` when local turn state is unavailable.\n- Persist the activity as a terminal rollout-trace runtime payload and\nreduce it to the corresponding spawn, send, follow-up, or close\ninteraction edge. `interrupt_agent` is classified as a close-edge\noperation.\n- Preserve the legacy picker when no path-backed v2 agent is known.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nApp-server v2 clients that consumed `collabAgentToolCall` begin/end\npairs for these tools must handle the new completion-only\n`subAgentActivity` item. Legacy v1 collaboration behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Screenshot\n\n<img width=\"684\" height=\"288\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-08 at 15 40 47\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/194b3cd0-619d-45fb-b587-cf3e2b1b8a1d\"\n/>\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace`\n- Added focused coverage for activity analytics, terminal trace\nserialization, spawn-edge reduction, `interrupt_agent` classification,\nTUI status rendering without aggregated command output, and clearing\nstale running state after a completed turn.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T10:14:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fae270932065355b5d7f197b3f1c72912588369b/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0"}]},{"sha":"a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEzMDQ1NjljNzk2YTBhY2VlYjkyMjFlNGJkOGRhYmEwMTAyZDM5YTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T08:23:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T08:23:16Z"},"message":"[codex] Return workspace directory installed plugins (#27098)\n\n## Summary\n\n- return installed `workspace-directory` remote plugins by default in\n`plugin/installed`\n- keep shared-with-me installed plugins gated behind `plugin_sharing`\n- filter remote installed plugin marketplaces by canonical marketplace\nname instead of coarse workspace scope\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `$xin-build` targeted verification:\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nbuild_remote_installed_plugin_marketplaces_from_cache_filters_by_marketplace_name`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_installed_includes_workspace_directory_without_plugin_sharing`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_installed_includes_remote_shared_with_me_plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_list_omits_shared_with_me_kind_when_plugin_sharing_disabled`","tree":{"sha":"35e5e4d7d18255c12482994ed361a7727fee4356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/35e5e4d7d18255c12482994ed361a7727fee4356"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ810CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWFcQAIwRFnjBXYriuD80B7s2rxW7\nXGc3Z2mfcXvfGBPYBaibYdquZr2uwRuioZax9kBUwr/aOOmSTiwJGhcReWu8VeAY\nn6t+unwtjSaarPv7mdgjoGoY0e4gwZWa7gXpJkjnTnbS1daSWSXLpzIzIOAxxKdQ\nQrfqgh2XS5oPVbmqWIoMKoPDeFPd2PXFQN6F84aVse9T8E3PMHvwEzSaWAbTXgZH\nj2hHFvr9NuPjVsoJo69dod6Hdkwc2M47EWVo8msNgqCHhHoJr6Cnyb03zEnHcyDf\n27HFkWBYCpevfohnJyC+vz3iwEhTqXLw++bl4b5tZ7bVLDSjxEGNvmJsCCEDBozr\nTlBVQG/CnbFAe/w/oJ9IC2wJXrlFNurMOTELdro6LTTxN2MuB8SQOUwqH0cDoaL3\nMntpqOLPsrXMyjH9XV7fhLIUtDsP15MyvT7Pnn8c0ex84F70krA6SZqkXL8fS2wR\neH2fY2h/I2sf7/sBq2D5XOm2SP6lH6pqRF8Cafi0jAZ/KsPeZxAtyeNbolrLlIBb\ndgeLCiybwyW+nF0LJvIuwgXPX/LhwVgIVQ2YimIyrD9FAgCVhkDTt9cSPXaGytFo\nfZsKP0prRT8978yGijrICeMeCY8+MqzwRUA9ef5SLYu24IbwN3XVlyUF/qmPXzi2\nsRMcQUhpAbJh55O4quir\n=W+7Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 35e5e4d7d18255c12482994ed361a7727fee4356\nparent 14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780993396 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780993396 -0700\n\n[codex] Return workspace directory installed plugins (#27098)\n\n## Summary\n\n- return installed `workspace-directory` remote plugins by default in\n`plugin/installed`\n- keep shared-with-me installed plugins gated behind `plugin_sharing`\n- filter remote installed plugin marketplaces by canonical marketplace\nname instead of coarse workspace scope\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `$xin-build` targeted verification:\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nbuild_remote_installed_plugin_marketplaces_from_cache_filters_by_marketplace_name`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_installed_includes_workspace_directory_without_plugin_sharing`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_installed_includes_remote_shared_with_me_plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_list_omits_shared_with_me_kind_when_plugin_sharing_disabled`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T08:23:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a304569c796a0aceeb9221e4bd8daba0102d39a0/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26"}]},{"sha":"14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE0NjYwYzIyZDE0MzEyYzI4YTUwYzUyOTU0ZGQ3N2RkODhmMDNjMjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T04:39:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T04:39:35Z"},"message":"Use server app auth requirements for remote plugin install (#27085)\n\n## Summary\n- request `includeAppsNeedingAuth=true` when installing remote plugins\n- return backend-provided `app_ids_needing_auth` from the remote install\nclient\n- use those app IDs to populate `appsNeedingAuth` without refetching\naccessible apps, with fallback for older responses\n\n## Testing\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- real app-server install/uninstall check with Notion remote plugin\n- subagent review found no blocking issues","tree":{"sha":"02c222bd6cd2d57de7565bad38040b8abc1b205b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/02c222bd6cd2d57de7565bad38040b8abc1b205b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ5kHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYz0QAIPVe1T3vFxK//va9pRMnCFh\nNbzkuCW26e7y2/1R35vLkHtuEifzIUgwrP8CUemGDEAvYGjJeqz9k+KStGqg18GU\neDfe6a6pPFiot+Vr3fyimcXp3FbrV1Lc+m8GZdoibcZw7ZNLvTQAVifsJVk1h8bM\nPbciLRNp5PXCOKnOciIUwSIulCOyPVVFxbGrV6alZsg3qvoYnDWrXPw94fYkekSb\nb8dftFTLQBv2KH1DRx3Tog3II9xkIEss2r3tk8H9vsRwBhlOgi5Gh+daLMdfvWcC\nzWgSfBPjL16DyQ+HOxjiPQP0524SS+YWCz+aRr6pt95shzaMJCfGzJgBsk1WAZHP\nFA/FL/3sYA5EEVIIWo9IAQM5A4brk5G/Z+GfyqmEIsFxZRdCV1rsKe/fUHZUQGzF\nBZ52ZyTU+8nav9M9aOfTP7AsabQePSncSShkfree0yG9gl2f3eShntJT7xjhId5C\nzp8o0yqAP4sQNM4D8bG6SHbjEeGzgMVU2+rgycA/LoYjqGTYlHCmPJObjwfWa87t\nrSPkeejObeH7zgS4XDV7PCzXNvvhZ5MgXSo0dInrp8mwHccagHvHAiNW4jEcrtDv\nLZRwJ8HiRH7zEKmlaceoNIFLmpdTUdqp9wr1m08/Ne/EliyXd3hsuQx3uIkFiw6u\nSIZBYwMEEbCsT/XLR57U\n=wZ/d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 02c222bd6cd2d57de7565bad38040b8abc1b205b\nparent dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780979975 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780979975 -0700\n\nUse server app auth requirements for remote plugin install (#27085)\n\n## Summary\n- request `includeAppsNeedingAuth=true` when installing remote plugins\n- return backend-provided `app_ids_needing_auth` from the remote install\nclient\n- use those app IDs to populate `appsNeedingAuth` without refetching\naccessible apps, with fallback for older responses\n\n## Testing\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- real app-server install/uninstall check with Notion remote plugin\n- subagent review found no blocking issues","verified_at":"2026-06-09T04:39:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/14660c22d14312c28a50c52954dd77dd88f03c26/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d"}]},{"sha":"dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRmZmM0YmY3NWRjOWVlYjA3MjdmNjY4Yzk1YmI3YmQ3MjMxNTU4MWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T04:32:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T04:32:46Z"},"message":"[codex] preserve fsmonitor for worktree Git reads (#26880)\n\nCodex forces `core.fsmonitor=false` on internal Git commands so a\nrepository cannot select an executable fsmonitor helper. This also\ndisables Git's built-in daemon for `status`, `diff`, and `ls-files`,\nturning those worktree reads into full scans in large repositories.\n\nRead the raw effective `core.fsmonitor` value and preserve it only when\nGit interprets it as true and advertises built-in daemon support through\n`git version --build-options`. Query uncommon boolean spellings back\nthrough Git using the exact effective value. Unset, false, helper paths,\nmalformed values, probe failures, and unsupported Git builds continue to\nforce `core.fsmonitor=false`.\n\nCentralize this policy in `git-utils` while keeping process execution in\nthe existing local and workspace-command adapters. Probe once per\nworktree workflow and reuse the result for its Git commands, including\nthe TUI `/diff` path. Metadata-only commands and repository discovery\nremain disabled without probing. Each probe and requested Git process\nkeeps its own existing timeout, and the decision is not cached because\nlayered and conditional Git configuration can change while Codex runs.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Chris Bookholt <bookholt@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbbce21603aef1e825cb65d380f6790b3ab50575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bbbce21603aef1e825cb65d380f6790b3ab50575"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ5duCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk7IQAHZ6HwPM8PgOuVGwvSacVfr5\n9pvJUsJbMXDsxseve+HUpc/l2TQnvsVjRlBYESC4wEYCsQtDflEwLVibefKRjMCo\nFnhZu20o89jL0BhoAiFTUHGhJiUcYge2oQZWNBW2F3772XXOu+818KRF9efPDQLJ\nna9UoEoEnvN5UV1Ugv1Yu1fUuepKini+FdbXzC/dVTAtz1TXK4RW3x/9a6xFok8V\n6XVQ/P2yZYjvrvBIm00thX6dUg/W4Z9K32nj/6XqM36VN5SoSarUxXdpm9W0PZrZ\n4oIyHdihlkx5XlSIu46umvbtEdecJcBQAmChyV1stHk+olrKWEN5AhYWobVIP4Sw\nea52UU+1Zg/f7837IFMJs3sZsihYL/dIznGAewInh78yNPisXEOgNNUwqiiWcL2I\noDjZ8rjwtYcb+UTlEIh4UMLBPqBu5QBsz1bsjTgqDJRUdKRinLEZnKzBqg9bq8rz\nXMm+EXrDNMtA3mEuN5Kn0+qEsYrSN8B5tvBfcQbAf/b+L8ZoGWcHGHSNUNaX21Lo\nZiFkAynXFR8mQPEdW61Cy/UlZ6/r+K/eP1Ys4WFXBatqcc2M5MDLLON0UWkZcvTy\nodMTwuVZUGc68d7wnH5lxJV/7JId9zkP6SEpXxzQaYnVx2o0oiNPd/NUdK6GbZEb\n99A9O8rFm1Dh/X7wCuSO\n=94if\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bbbce21603aef1e825cb65d380f6790b3ab50575\nparent 08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653\nauthor Tamir Duberstein <tamird@openai.com> 1780979566 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780979566 -0700\n\n[codex] preserve fsmonitor for worktree Git reads (#26880)\n\nCodex forces `core.fsmonitor=false` on internal Git commands so a\nrepository cannot select an executable fsmonitor helper. This also\ndisables Git's built-in daemon for `status`, `diff`, and `ls-files`,\nturning those worktree reads into full scans in large repositories.\n\nRead the raw effective `core.fsmonitor` value and preserve it only when\nGit interprets it as true and advertises built-in daemon support through\n`git version --build-options`. Query uncommon boolean spellings back\nthrough Git using the exact effective value. Unset, false, helper paths,\nmalformed values, probe failures, and unsupported Git builds continue to\nforce `core.fsmonitor=false`.\n\nCentralize this policy in `git-utils` while keeping process execution in\nthe existing local and workspace-command adapters. Probe once per\nworktree workflow and reuse the result for its Git commands, including\nthe TUI `/diff` path. Metadata-only commands and repository discovery\nremain disabled without probing. Each probe and requested Git process\nkeeps its own existing timeout, and the decision is not cached because\nlayered and conditional Git configuration can change while Codex runs.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Chris Bookholt <bookholt@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-09T04:32:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dffc4bf75dc9eeb0727f668c95bb7bd72315581d/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653"}]},{"sha":"08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA4Y2I2MzNjMDZhMjdkMjU4NzJkMDEzMmZiZDljNzQ5NTU2ZDc2NTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T02:23:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T02:23:35Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove remote compaction failure log (#27106)\n\n## Why\n\n`log_remote_compact_failure` was the only consumer of the\ncompact-request logging payload and most of the token-usage breakdown\nfields. Once that failure log is removed, keeping the surrounding\ncarrier types leaves dead plumbing in the compaction path and context\nmanager.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove `log_remote_compact_failure`, `CompactRequestLogData`, and the\nv2 wrapper that only fed that log.\n- Let both remote compaction implementations return the original\ncompaction error directly.\n- Replace `TotalTokenUsageBreakdown` with a narrow helper that returns\nonly the remaining value needed by compaction analytics.\n- Keep `estimate_response_item_model_visible_bytes` private to the\ncontext manager implementation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core`","tree":{"sha":"bf51fe333d2d002f4fdf3913d4d517be0b9d5538","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bf51fe333d2d002f4fdf3913d4d517be0b9d5538"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ3knCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhJIQAJgFowQ37Z8gqg2QepJk36iw\nZLO2+ncsknnlXIGWIix7vuks2ANG86rziOq/Ai7WYT/1KKtMP7j/KDhjxlV4qG7U\ncsUmNGO/WpqUgJXOTjmtRs//M0BCQ64Aycb15RLNF3OrVDgEW9J3/8kRynXSbSE2\n+DmDptqDlzE3XbKlR6oV4p4KD8VaeCeNIBgSGN8RZ76xaimlb3pyoA4yMxNkhSVn\nvJ/n6NoNSHK1r5bmjRIxANTMxot2Zhi9rHvoG3JxNA7Sqf6IbAV4e0CK489Hq823\nGHLdWgyUPedldHRvgI2EyiClpoLCwyKA7obJ4xq8hxunmEM+tVmuiqKAqoT6/uOE\nCC+epYugXtqBhReAZI7C8SnMT0BhISTPkDfB/j7j9c8PKQaVOSeGUGLEoaPbkK7Y\nflbbVn3pQ+0trr3P3eR8iePFeWXcjHVr02sj0BFc5tlCQVDHKf6aShys84Ol9JW/\n7GOYNx6AqYfVHVigF5ZeilyVyhYeHK2EqQ7nGv3MsGsk9vCZjIzjLYepHf+IK2vA\nGoHmOthTxNRo9sqR/32lbuqiDZQQBscgiyB/FfE4uuxqwctBccEZgUVuNtwJ5O/w\nS3wMNBpdjTI0azXwzoheL/AzfjJOOyPNZrWxDK/zEMqmZnStDeuw0UZ2q9OFxHg5\nhcd+GPQSD5WoTd+lnHD1\n=ULf6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bf51fe333d2d002f4fdf3913d4d517be0b9d5538\nparent 0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780971815 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780971815 -0700\n\n[codex] Remove remote compaction failure log (#27106)\n\n## Why\n\n`log_remote_compact_failure` was the only consumer of the\ncompact-request logging payload and most of the token-usage breakdown\nfields. Once that failure log is removed, keeping the surrounding\ncarrier types leaves dead plumbing in the compaction path and context\nmanager.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove `log_remote_compact_failure`, `CompactRequestLogData`, and the\nv2 wrapper that only fed that log.\n- Let both remote compaction implementations return the original\ncompaction error directly.\n- Replace `TotalTokenUsageBreakdown` with a narrow helper that returns\nonly the remaining value needed by compaction analytics.\n- Keep `estimate_response_item_model_visible_bytes` private to the\ncontext manager implementation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T02:23:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/08cb633c06a27d25872d0132fbd9c749556d7653/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854"}]},{"sha":"0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBiZWI1YzdmMzJjZjU0NTlhNTFlM2Y2YmMwMWU2NTA5ZDc5NTE4NTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T01:08:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T01:08:48Z"},"message":"Preserve cloud requirements across TUI thread resets (#25177)\n\nFixes a TUI regression where thread transitions such as `/new` and\n`/clear` could rebuild config without the cloud requirements loader,\nallowing users to fall back to non-cloud-managed settings. The config\nrefresh path now preserves cloud requirements during thread\nreinitialization, and config loading is moved off the deep TUI event\nstack to avoid stack-overflow crashes during those reloads.\n\n- Passes the cloud requirements loader through TUI config rebuild paths.\n- Keeps cloud requirements applied for `/new`, `/clear`, `/fork`, side\nconversations, and session picker transitions.\n- Runs config building on a Tokio task so reloads do not occur on the\ndeep TUI caller stack.\n- Adds regression coverage that cloud requirements survive\nthread-transition config refreshes.\n\n## Test/Repro:\n  - Start Codex with a cloud requirement applied.\n  - Use `/new` or `/clear`.\n- The refreshed/fresh-session config should still include the cloud\nrequirements\n  \nThis can be tested with any config item, at this moment for oai staff\nthe easiest item to test is the `mentions_v2` feature. This is currently\nenabled in cloud requirements, but is not enabled by default. As a\nresult, prior to these changes that feature is disabled after `/new` or\n`/clear`. Testing the same steps with a binary from this branch should\nnot drop the feature enablement.","tree":{"sha":"c4c5e0d812d3fbfc5893c7475fdd64535560e7d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c4c5e0d812d3fbfc5893c7475fdd64535560e7d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ2egCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuUcQABs9CEvDGIYQ5ZlKaNfttqCD\n2VlcmS67wUC+g/bbiXh2vLZ6Y7119KZoQrGOglNMqEDjeX5XpwBQujQNnwG2NfuL\neVdzTCCOYhZMbgxHYIj85DNHulqx7O6tiIfv4s71WgOU39FCxd5kwMxfHECq7Z44\n8/TEYO0BlayGbKJhPX73V+zN/Ee5HbzxY8Rwn4xMMlfTOQi8aJmjwUgN8iRhdxW9\nehHJns4x3SoS26GaRMEI8/OKkwwiyzZ/VPZJ8/rYxJnsMMDug9qp0Nd3+uVIsYG4\nYBRVRa0gCwL6QXnDkF7hEerLpGAEZzQ4uM/aWVTNtzOrOnF02uJ6ipq0kxsTLCPQ\nrXnLKf2zo/zC9dsjknqEM3ubgT3b9HQazEAbuGYKaz9QGikRX8pmeCPepdfyf8Vf\not18090xmF4SLdNWAtSOqcmacRAVWW/AlqBeL2rIBk20+uh6PidzYoVt9A04uyBK\na4TLS0Bn41QwlN/bEqsDDXJqEZ3GRiDRG9T77glSJDEv5kA+f7UtZX7uijXiwF4v\nTI4Evx2KnMtT1ETfo9vsNFG/49M0xKu/nVjFLKOvz49dXLktncjuQikO3/Z8vchO\n51/eit2SS2NNMhJHMVrG9qB4DpQFLbSj9mlL9/FqRsbr8ayAoDaSNco/BtdWs32Z\nHxSa7LhHHx6PjnZVBFCQ\n=a6u4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c4c5e0d812d3fbfc5893c7475fdd64535560e7d7\nparent c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1780967328 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780967328 -0700\n\nPreserve cloud requirements across TUI thread resets (#25177)\n\nFixes a TUI regression where thread transitions such as `/new` and\n`/clear` could rebuild config without the cloud requirements loader,\nallowing users to fall back to non-cloud-managed settings. The config\nrefresh path now preserves cloud requirements during thread\nreinitialization, and config loading is moved off the deep TUI event\nstack to avoid stack-overflow crashes during those reloads.\n\n- Passes the cloud requirements loader through TUI config rebuild paths.\n- Keeps cloud requirements applied for `/new`, `/clear`, `/fork`, side\nconversations, and session picker transitions.\n- Runs config building on a Tokio task so reloads do not occur on the\ndeep TUI caller stack.\n- Adds regression coverage that cloud requirements survive\nthread-transition config refreshes.\n\n## Test/Repro:\n  - Start Codex with a cloud requirement applied.\n  - Use `/new` or `/clear`.\n- The refreshed/fresh-session config should still include the cloud\nrequirements\n  \nThis can be tested with any config item, at this moment for oai staff\nthe easiest item to test is the `mentions_v2` feature. This is currently\nenabled in cloud requirements, but is not enabled by default. As a\nresult, prior to these changes that feature is disabled after `/new` or\n`/clear`. Testing the same steps with a binary from this branch should\nnot drop the feature enablement.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T01:08:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0beb5c7f32cf5459a51e3f6bc01e6509d7951854/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b"}]},{"sha":"c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM2NTZjYzRhODNlYWViMTI4OWM4YzhjNjZlYTcyYjM1ZGJjNmUyOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"yuning-oai","email":"yuning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T00:55:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T00:55:00Z"},"message":"Update web search citation prompt (#27096)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Update the web search tool prompt to require Markdown links for cited\nsources.\n- Explicitly tell the model not to use `turnX`-style citations in\nresponses.\n\n## Context\n\n\nhttps://openai.slack.com/archives/C0AU83S0ZQU/p1780964147777649?thread_ts=1780352049.512299&cid=C0AU83S0ZQU\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `python3 scripts/format.py --check` (fails only on Rust formatter\nsetup: rustup cannot create temp files under `/home/dev-user/.rustup`;\nJust and Python formatter checks pass when using temp cache dirs)","tree":{"sha":"6697e657d0abb719f3707543fa7d3c88c049968d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6697e657d0abb719f3707543fa7d3c88c049968d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ2RkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhtkQACc7neMA5vl+lpXphxt49Bwx\nCctOReinGaF0996xf2CmeNiO/n5Hz6UaCLEvPzmSrlUA+Xs8SvaOthwo9DRLn7kR\n38OMKi+LvOlwB7X+PMJFozsEirR6SZTtFr4u1mB/l4K3n2PB0DQX+ZlUaDX4Cl2W\n5kAxlSlkScS3bA8yvBYxAcVtynB+ZwWoFARWAhgmzAyfZGItWDIVAuA/iZtjY2Yf\nd7YeArn0Vlyk8+/MFhH+dAYSiIJH6oiUk+UhXbSAwlAtVXtgAzKHepxWjuI3Jgyv\nmdpGiMr/05jDcq880IsN2s0OwFg5Er3KLUturYb1jTPHRZzrFKAkDQTZELfIttdM\nehXoQOTjAjZJ+hevFWeqcrywXWUiGcTNjV2sUohmD/hi/zK86BIvYgVwBusMJlRZ\nNoO59MkJDo+z+VD38M7ED1qxrJA6AnVrMWkog2sSsXUUe54A6SVkgssVhHrkcoT7\ns7kPEPTaG0oUE83rAikVq2nPPFjuoIXJVgOmuqzT5/VaX+yzLiFc6zUlaDr0yvt9\nRyLY2KBfXfXJWJoldCWsUxF+MgVzrGePXvyIY9JAQa9I1bhaiTXquOfof743bFfH\nIrvgcAptUAgX5nTto3QZrBR+Edjdhh7RmgZEpwMScKuHY2aL2+3OtK9m7lQ2m9/b\nH3Na9OKVipiZ0vb/kUcs\n=iWIK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6697e657d0abb719f3707543fa7d3c88c049968d\nparent e127a0cf99195e94e8762c40c6ba17fd6158ac29\nauthor yuning-oai <yuning@openai.com> 1780966500 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780966500 +0000\n\nUpdate web search citation prompt (#27096)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Update the web search tool prompt to require Markdown links for cited\nsources.\n- Explicitly tell the model not to use `turnX`-style citations in\nresponses.\n\n## Context\n\n\nhttps://openai.slack.com/archives/C0AU83S0ZQU/p1780964147777649?thread_ts=1780352049.512299&cid=C0AU83S0ZQU\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `python3 scripts/format.py --check` (fails only on Rust formatter\nsetup: rustup cannot create temp files under `/home/dev-user/.rustup`;\nJust and Python formatter checks pass when using temp cache dirs)","verified_at":"2026-06-09T00:55:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c656cc4a83eaeb1289c8c8c66ea72b35dbc6e28b/comments","author":{"login":"yuning-oai","id":257628876,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1sazA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257628876?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/yuning-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.