:"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53"}]},{"sha":"8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg1MzQ5MTJkZjkzMDcwMDc4OGVhNjk4MTJkZTY1ZTcyMjJlYWVhNTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T00:03:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T00:03:52Z"},"message":"Show effective sandbox modes in /debug-config (#27068)\n\n## Summary\n- Render `/debug-config`'s `allowed_sandbox_modes` from the finalized\npermission constraints instead of the raw requirements list.\n- Add regression coverage for configured full-access and external\nsandbox modes being omitted when effective permissions reject them.\n\n## Details\n`allowed_sandbox_modes` comes from managed requirements, but the final\npermissions can be further constrained by derived validation rules. For\nexample, `permissions.filesystem.deny_read` requires sandbox\nenforcement, so modes that disable or externalize Codex's sandbox are\nnot actually usable even if they were present in the raw requirements\nTOML.\n\nThe debug renderer now enumerates the configured sandbox-mode labels and\nkeeps only those accepted by `Config.permissions`. That makes\n`/debug-config` reflect the same effective permission-profile constraint\npath used by runtime config validation, while preserving the existing\nsource/provenance display.\n\n## Validation\n- Added a regression test for effective sandbox-mode filtering in\n`/debug-config`.","tree":{"sha":"dde2140b3b4e1b84af4dc06333c64878de2611aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dde2140b3b4e1b84af4dc06333c64878de2611aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ1hoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABLkQAB1DsVHekzH667wY7VhTHGgn\nyuxRBbD95TVk8dBrBES/JadSTpWbySlIpjfrwOCnV7ybofcrUAnAzl4IcYcdx9fN\n6FaA1twDDzZ44Zhdboxg3ivnGI658ST4GA/19KSrlTWGmduvwGyYkByBiNyuSUxl\nKZU9jwrOJZzOapk7RoPcW+/1UbtHsg+B8Do5asZ7tEXa9Klh+XtBuzCXpyqqIkiw\nSbYl8zHmVW0XJIKeGQSrNM4+0LBmJSRK8hOfG5M199kMWl4u67q21p1Cd6qcW9UQ\nIr8wzLQ+x0IpI9QPhOfsHH53LTH4KmiiettWyGpm9O+VtqgFQAtlodw9VIeiHQ04\nv01k9HT0nLDcyew5gpSkuOAxg5K11/pwFq0C1hiaWgQu124Pxkli3toG0SPhgMEe\ntPCdlfCJuIKrfdCv7TCDc7jzVMVohVyXugUTJ48JSpTZnSBhYoU1wG9ZMuOCmEke\n+wdZLmIZ2q/hzTEwwVLTsiljyQ+eXjf29DHKK/aswjLYe8WxaYr0FF+T02pPX7GA\nhpK59uvF6RP0EMP0g6QQz3CXliKjJo7Cc8PDEH6jOZALzVjPY/gR+1EycNsjTlql\nH0HdwWNXapsxYR+6kui+p3/i+2AO6Ic/UIv2SMv7uCaynaBZh/Lcfe1/tHRYcGbH\nPFxGUysCH9lRwSfqefv4\n=SbRZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dde2140b3b4e1b84af4dc06333c64878de2611aa\nparent 4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1780963432 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780963432 -0700\n\nShow effective sandbox modes in /debug-config (#27068)\n\n## Summary\n- Render `/debug-config`'s `allowed_sandbox_modes` from the finalized\npermission constraints instead of the raw requirements list.\n- Add regression coverage for configured full-access and external\nsandbox modes being omitted when effective permissions reject them.\n\n## Details\n`allowed_sandbox_modes` comes from managed requirements, but the final\npermissions can be further constrained by derived validation rules. For\nexample, `permissions.filesystem.deny_read` requires sandbox\nenforcement, so modes that disable or externalize Codex's sandbox are\nnot actually usable even if they were present in the raw requirements\nTOML.\n\nThe debug renderer now enumerates the configured sandbox-mode labels and\nkeeps only those accepted by `Config.permissions`. That makes\n`/debug-config` reflect the same effective permission-profile constraint\npath used by runtime config validation, while preserving the existing\nsource/provenance display.\n\n## Validation\n- Added a regression test for effective sandbox-mode filtering in\n`/debug-config`.","verified_at":"2026-06-09T00:03:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8534912df930700788ea69812de65e7222eaea53/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a"}]},{"sha":"4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRjYTJlNDM2ZTUwOTUxYmFhMWVhNzQyNDZmZTA5YmJiZmYxZmRhNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-09T00:02:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-09T00:02:36Z"},"message":"fix(tui): linkify complete bare URLs with tildes (#27088)\n\n## Background\n\nBare URLs containing `~` in their path are currently only clickable up\nto the tilde in the interactive TUI. For example, Codex renders the\nvisible text for:\n\n\n`https://www.cs.tufts.edu/~nr/cs257/archive/olin-shivers/dissertation.pdf`\n\nbut the OSC 8 destination stops at `https://www.cs.tufts.edu/`. This\nmakes Cmd-click open the wrong location even though the terminal\nrecognizes the complete URL outside Codex.\n\nFixes #26774.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe URL scanner already accepts `~`. The truncation happens earlier:\nwith strikethrough parsing enabled, `pulldown-cmark` splits this URL\ninto adjacent decoded `Event::Text` values around the tilde. The\nMarkdown renderer annotated each text event independently, so only the\nfirst event still looked like a complete URL with a supported scheme.\n\nThe renderer now merges adjacent decoded text events before URL\nannotation. It preserves the combined source range while retaining\nparser-decoded contents, which avoids regressing entities such as\n`&amp;`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add a small iterator that merges adjacent decoded Markdown text events\nand their source ranges.\n- Apply it at the Markdown renderer boundary before hyperlink detection.\n- Add regression coverage for the reported URL in prose, wrapped table\noutput, and entity-decoded URLs.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Run Codex with `just c`.\n2. Ask the assistant to output this exact bare URL with no Markdown link\nsyntax:\n\n`https://www.cs.tufts.edu/~nr/cs257/archive/olin-shivers/dissertation.pdf`\n3. Hold Cmd and hover or click the URL.\n4. Confirm the complete URL, including the suffix after `~`, is one\ndestination.\n5. Repeat with the URL inside a Markdown table and confirm wrapped\nportions retain the same complete destination.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui url_with_tilde`\n- `just test -p codex-tui merged_text_events_preserve_entity_decoding`\n\nThe full `codex-tui` test run was also executed. Its only failures were\nthe two existing Guardian feature-flag tests:\n\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`","tree":{"sha":"8023df7a95a4940d53f6f7a028d96005f43d2c3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8023df7a95a4940d53f6f7a028d96005f43d2c3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ1gcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALMUQAB55/x6+nwISbQ6KsoWyGrs9\nS3JSf0YDmncCyAb5SrPRxrJx+xyGgLfar2BHheJZOVR7QLGvRiG5LhI8CEuHfp09\nv4wL2eUjF/Oz12O98cEixx0NsXaLNFE5vv1Hl2vv3twKX+Iop2Ln8d0cMUB0ne79\n4di97UDikbLpL1YuPgX5lTRIbasy8SGVbuqpOIwjAgy6VIosa7sRSZgDePQRmRNi\nE7BNRXydKOtJ6Vl9SH89BoJASUtlxRAJQlowTbBQaLgSLu7C1TbJP3ggueHGNwt9\nGQL0aGQwXVutNiyZubtpQ5FIhvLhxY9A7OvuuhsQkGNx04/irbkV4E/+M1DINVMO\n3S6WaUwnzJWhG1PJVtg7H5YVxp1IBlCp8VgWD2drwhqdltEieNeSig0hVTys5KW9\nqdwhAzr+H3NPGC1QqYvX0uAFNVVHeTO1n0Ldjo4UsV1wa/gcrWpZap9PdqM0R/I+\nLZ8jZr9q2cQ8Ng0oJaxQhvy/jc/0UG9MWHMjSdYvkkOElNOLfMBXV7kIjutkzmdc\nveoL/c0+oJTS4rCO3SxVOaLeQEOh5nC0faSJLp4/EkOFXTA7pIFFkz5w9RCjYB1q\n4/s1zj5sBkfEHHKFsC4NVYKt+mCqKxgiMz4gvuCpEqINO/SSmlsjpleO0YH+qAQE\nOeScEGzBcB1ryZMzFCgJ\n=hgil\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8023df7a95a4940d53f6f7a028d96005f43d2c3c\nparent ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780963356 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780963356 -0700\n\nfix(tui): linkify complete bare URLs with tildes (#27088)\n\n## Background\n\nBare URLs containing `~` in their path are currently only clickable up\nto the tilde in the interactive TUI. For example, Codex renders the\nvisible text for:\n\n\n`https://www.cs.tufts.edu/~nr/cs257/archive/olin-shivers/dissertation.pdf`\n\nbut the OSC 8 destination stops at `https://www.cs.tufts.edu/`. This\nmakes Cmd-click open the wrong location even though the terminal\nrecognizes the complete URL outside Codex.\n\nFixes #26774.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe URL scanner already accepts `~`. The truncation happens earlier:\nwith strikethrough parsing enabled, `pulldown-cmark` splits this URL\ninto adjacent decoded `Event::Text` values around the tilde. The\nMarkdown renderer annotated each text event independently, so only the\nfirst event still looked like a complete URL with a supported scheme.\n\nThe renderer now merges adjacent decoded text events before URL\nannotation. It preserves the combined source range while retaining\nparser-decoded contents, which avoids regressing entities such as\n`&amp;`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Add a small iterator that merges adjacent decoded Markdown text events\nand their source ranges.\n- Apply it at the Markdown renderer boundary before hyperlink detection.\n- Add regression coverage for the reported URL in prose, wrapped table\noutput, and entity-decoded URLs.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Run Codex with `just c`.\n2. Ask the assistant to output this exact bare URL with no Markdown link\nsyntax:\n\n`https://www.cs.tufts.edu/~nr/cs257/archive/olin-shivers/dissertation.pdf`\n3. Hold Cmd and hover or click the URL.\n4. Confirm the complete URL, including the suffix after `~`, is one\ndestination.\n5. Repeat with the URL inside a Markdown table and confirm wrapped\nportions retain the same complete destination.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui url_with_tilde`\n- `just test -p codex-tui merged_text_events_preserve_entity_decoding`\n\nThe full `codex-tui` test run was also executed. Its only failures were\nthe two existing Guardian feature-flag tests:\n\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`","verified_at":"2026-06-09T00:02:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ca2e436e50951baa1ea74246fe09bbbff1fda4a/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03"}]},{"sha":"ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZmZWM3YzA5MzM2NWVhY2IyYjVlZjU4ZGFmZDUzYWJhZWVhNzJlMDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T23:33:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T23:33:41Z"},"message":"Add typed file URIs (#26840)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex needs stable `file:` URI identifiers that can cross process and\noperating-system boundaries without eagerly interpreting them as native\npaths. Existing fields also need to keep accepting absolute path strings\nduring migration.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `codex-utils-path-uri` with a validated, immutable `PathUri`\nwrapper that currently accepts only `file:` URLs.\n- Expose URI-level `basename`, `parent`, and `join` operations that\npreserve authorities and percent encoding without guessing the source\noperating system.\n- Keep native conversion explicit through `AbsolutePathBuf` and the\ncurrent host rules.\n- Serialize as canonical URI text while accepting both URI text and\nlegacy absolute native paths during deserialization.\n- Add adversarial coverage for Windows-looking and POSIX paths, UNC\nauthorities, encoded metadata characters, non-UTF-8 POSIX paths, URI\nhierarchy operations, and legacy serde round trips.","tree":{"sha":"f51af9e7f66e18c14d860a8e99e048345e2e48c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f51af9e7f66e18c14d860a8e99e048345e2e48c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ1FVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlSMQAFsfW52I37dBD1yqgFRGVrml\nRfxoD3ApSQ3g/GYfDaqP1xHtI8qu9f2cYYMfQgybrtD7b69vB2Yq01gnquMELj+w\nPrnziUZweQAvuyWUx/zb6u7dkTFYm6RA+j25Gqzc9ct9EhKf7hZ7BaYl5L/eZY2S\n7SKtPGEyr4FYBNba/hFDLgrwrpUxzw3w0/Wswnc9Y4s02UTOXjtrRcqbB4xT+GoZ\n0xLxTpyqUYv2Ynuxnz4vtGOWZ1HCyLs8qMqDi0UZq8wFnpFW15ZUfdAM4N+bc/s6\nj9TjYCAuPqKxRV8cJrqz0QriOPVKaumPVRPs228tj1iSbxCitJssfhb2GGzMBGeX\niKOuKQdhJDauNreUE2/TiOUbEkx1//i7Df6A7afwZBGBZyHS5j2r6Qk/cZewi411\nefyZmTura/aWx8lbUgkTweIxkpz/5dyZ0EmXR6Ei6UpC1lAWvYUmWkUrHub/d95h\nk3qA1VdsWfTYszKdIMe/8frepfFBqkKakRg1z5r3Y8o4ZLddJxZNE9zpN6XL2Wj1\nir6h2pgKd/HKfh97ddETW80DDZNnd8yJyVHfj4+bX7Yp5cafc1DQEzUSyF+5BVZE\nvT9SSxNpHuKsWiUSRsuzaKGjAnnbdhpGLW1UPq/qkoe8t5trdujg+y5dhoBt6kTi\nnlfM602ucXX3y7m0QbRs\n=27rG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f51af9e7f66e18c14d860a8e99e048345e2e48c4\nparent 6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780961621 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780961621 -0700\n\nAdd typed file URIs (#26840)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex needs stable `file:` URI identifiers that can cross process and\noperating-system boundaries without eagerly interpreting them as native\npaths. Existing fields also need to keep accepting absolute path strings\nduring migration.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `codex-utils-path-uri` with a validated, immutable `PathUri`\nwrapper that currently accepts only `file:` URLs.\n- Expose URI-level `basename`, `parent`, and `join` operations that\npreserve authorities and percent encoding without guessing the source\noperating system.\n- Keep native conversion explicit through `AbsolutePathBuf` and the\ncurrent host rules.\n- Serialize as canonical URI text while accepting both URI text and\nlegacy absolute native paths during deserialization.\n- Add adversarial coverage for Windows-looking and POSIX paths, UNC\nauthorities, encoded metadata characters, non-UTF-8 POSIX paths, URI\nhierarchy operations, and legacy serde round trips.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T23:33:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffec7c093365eacb2b5ef58dafd53abaeea72e03/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4"}]},{"sha":"6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYwNDJlNTgxMGU3MDYyY2M5MzdiYjAzOTdhZmFhNWJlYTQzMWZiYzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T23:07:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T23:07:56Z"},"message":"chore: preserve one more schema layer during large tool compaction (#27084)\n\n## Summary\n\nSome customer MCP tools expose large input schemas that exceed Codex's\ncompact schema budget even after description stripping. Today, the final\ncompaction pass collapses complex schemas starting at depth 2, which can\nerase important shallow call structure such as small `anyOf` branches,\nrequired fields, and help-mode entry points. In one reported case, this\ndegraded a tool schema into `query: any | any`, leaving the model\nwithout enough structure to discover the required help call.\n\nThis change raises the deep-schema collapse boundary from depth 2 to\ndepth 3. That preserves one additional layer of the tool contract while\nstill collapsing deeper expensive subtrees to `{}` when a schema remains\nover budget.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Increased `MAX_COMPACT_TOOL_SCHEMA_DEPTH` from `2` to `3`.\n- Updated the schema compaction traversal test to assert the new\ncollapse boundary.\n- The resulting compacted shape keeps useful shallow structure, for\nexample:\n  - top-level argument names\n  - shallow `anyOf` branches\n  - required object fields\n  - nested property names one level deeper than before\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just test -p codex-tools`: 81 tests passed.\n- Ran a golden schema corpus comparison over 214 discovered tool input\nschemas under `golden_schemas/*/mcp_tools/*/input_schema.json`.\n- Depth 2 and depth 3 had identical percentile token counts across the\ncorpus.\n  - Both ended with `0 / 214` schemas over 1k tokens.\n- Both ended with `0 / 214` schemas over the 4,000-byte compact JSON\nbudget.\n- Only one golden schema changed, increasing from 49 to 56 tokens, so\nthis does not appear to introduce a meaningful corpus-wide regression.\n\nCorpus percentile results:\n\n| Percentile | Depth 2 | Depth 3 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| p0 | 9 | 9 |\n| p10 | 31 | 31 |\n| p25 | 54 | 54 |\n| p50 | 81 | 81 |\n| p75 | 143 | 143 |\n| p90 | 290 | 290 |\n| p95 | 431 | 431 |\n| p99 | 600 | 600 |\n| max | 832 | 832 |","tree":{"sha":"45b57ebd9a10243e49f344aa082dbb4912f62045","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/45b57ebd9a10243e49f344aa082dbb4912f62045"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ0tMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/RMQAChyB8q6bvgJTqbUPeIwV2BM\na8uAdlZqZhSz7zmZSHugP15u6eLQwGsRCluT8Q3z7IvbIlKM76Fx2NfTHAc80lD+\niJIAverBHfPB80GozRa4SXGTpIsLimgQyaMOkYkuFk+HYZie9xbl2X6IdfH6KBxA\nvaxKCvz7YyiCYLtaxa4bLzItJK8o5dXyrVZ+zPbm+iCjZM28tNZJK+7gKeemeBBw\n2lwbDD5ZIvdo5gdeSjeMFuTDGMDGlgGwxtfNEwfwQdgbLk/mZan7puq4VhpFLUVY\n5Uh1ZK9BKiEBR2g1mRVFhEBCteLFhUFQNV/+AtM6yYTuVYSZ+c8xaW7mrFLQLPOV\neJ3StWsQocmHBjQN2nzQlBrwsxt5sHAOoduHeemwmkxHbjCdn+PvgGaax9jXBsdu\nubCF6wdeFS6g6uABSNaeVGQDOucAdtT+q3+sunw002aC6stTvUFG9qOg+9xjeqhq\n5FlBCRrLrPYd9qhyIsPEbUiLPYWXR0Duq4/pP4gHtGO43ZcWcO9rcnBjSeBp2vH4\nY90KPsQI3kh01RfJWRKvopVmXqFePZ1DbuIKE262BmqExAEM11bnv43YlKhnUCSV\nSSKg44dgKZRdlZUCpvpxS/Q814zLKj3tk0UE3/cvbqXMbi9Klg+n2QT0i3xFesua\nzOldBQuRjdur0xxJQjIF\n=EvUX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 45b57ebd9a10243e49f344aa082dbb4912f62045\nparent 0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1780960076 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780960076 +0000\n\nchore: preserve one more schema layer during large tool compaction (#27084)\n\n## Summary\n\nSome customer MCP tools expose large input schemas that exceed Codex's\ncompact schema budget even after description stripping. Today, the final\ncompaction pass collapses complex schemas starting at depth 2, which can\nerase important shallow call structure such as small `anyOf` branches,\nrequired fields, and help-mode entry points. In one reported case, this\ndegraded a tool schema into `query: any | any`, leaving the model\nwithout enough structure to discover the required help call.\n\nThis change raises the deep-schema collapse boundary from depth 2 to\ndepth 3. That preserves one additional layer of the tool contract while\nstill collapsing deeper expensive subtrees to `{}` when a schema remains\nover budget.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Increased `MAX_COMPACT_TOOL_SCHEMA_DEPTH` from `2` to `3`.\n- Updated the schema compaction traversal test to assert the new\ncollapse boundary.\n- The resulting compacted shape keeps useful shallow structure, for\nexample:\n  - top-level argument names\n  - shallow `anyOf` branches\n  - required object fields\n  - nested property names one level deeper than before\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just test -p codex-tools`: 81 tests passed.\n- Ran a golden schema corpus comparison over 214 discovered tool input\nschemas under `golden_schemas/*/mcp_tools/*/input_schema.json`.\n- Depth 2 and depth 3 had identical percentile token counts across the\ncorpus.\n  - Both ended with `0 / 214` schemas over 1k tokens.\n- Both ended with `0 / 214` schemas over the 4,000-byte compact JSON\nbudget.\n- Only one golden schema changed, increasing from 49 to 56 tokens, so\nthis does not appear to introduce a meaningful corpus-wide regression.\n\nCorpus percentile results:\n\n| Percentile | Depth 2 | Depth 3 |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| p0 | 9 | 9 |\n| p10 | 31 | 31 |\n| p25 | 54 | 54 |\n| p50 | 81 | 81 |\n| p75 | 143 | 143 |\n| p90 | 290 | 290 |\n| p95 | 431 | 431 |\n| p99 | 600 | 600 |\n| max | 832 | 832 |","verified_at":"2026-06-08T23:07:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6042e5810e7062cc937bb0397afaa5bea431fbc4/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab"}]},{"sha":"0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA0NzNhNWNjNTIyY2Q4ZDBhNzk4NTk1YzBhMDhjZTY2MWViMmEwYWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T22:43:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T22:43:08Z"},"message":"feat(doctor): report editor and pager environment (#27081)\n\n## Background\n\nThis was prompted by\n[#26858](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/26858), where the\nattached doctor report did not include the editor selection and I had to\n[ask which editor was in\nuse](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/26858#issuecomment-4653829891)\nbefore investigating the external-editor newline issue. Capturing these\nvariables in doctor makes that context available up front in future\nreports.\n\n`codex doctor` is intended to capture enough local context to diagnose\nstartup and terminal behavior, but it did not report the environment\nvariables that select an external editor or configure command pagers.\n\nThe TUI [prefers `VISUAL` over\n`EDITOR`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c/codex-rs/tui/src/external_editor.rs#L31-L38),\nso missing or unexpected values can explain why the external-editor\nshortcut fails or launches the wrong command. Pager values are also\nuseful inherited-shell context even though [unified exec normalizes its\neffective pager variables to\n`cat`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c/codex-rs/core/src/unified_exec/process_manager.rs#L60-L70).\n\nThese variables can contain arbitrary command arguments or inline\nenvironment assignments. The human report is local, but `codex doctor\n--json` may be attached to feedback, so the machine-readable report\nshould not include their raw contents.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Report `VISUAL` and `EDITOR` in the system environment details, using\n`not set` when either variable is absent.\n- Report inherited `PAGER`, `GIT_PAGER`, `GH_PAGER`, and `LESS` values\nwhen present.\n- Preserve full values in local human output while reducing these fields\nto `set` or `not set` in redacted JSON output.\n- Add structured check, JSON-redaction, rendered-output, and snapshot\ncoverage.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. From `codex-rs`, run Codex with explicit editor and pager variables:\n\n   ```sh\nenv VISUAL='code --wait' EDITOR=vim PAGER='less -R' GIT_PAGER=delta\nGH_PAGER=less LESS=-FRX \\\n     cargo run -p codex-cli --bin codex -- doctor --no-color\n   ```\n\n2. Confirm the `system` details show the full values for all six\nvariables.\n3. Unset the pager variables and rerun the command. Confirm pager rows\nare omitted while missing editor variables are shown as `not set`.\n4. Run the same configured environment with `doctor --json`. Confirm\neach configured editor or pager field is reported as `set` and none of\nthe raw commands or arguments appear in the JSON.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli` (279 tests passed)","tree":{"sha":"83f6f7cffd1758253d5d872fe21f7d5243fd632b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/83f6f7cffd1758253d5d872fe21f7d5243fd632b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ0V9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuWMQADgA6ZmihsQfDK3EJyjb5e2m\ng09jvUwI/g2MfU2aQWRqPQUpmTNppK4ox58hPVjcex23bF9KUefP0xgSoGJtI7Fq\n37sauwzh2fvQdIYvAPYrl/Sg3YOOAtxDjo82+37pwx97lcyenx+ODa0Rw1mu+C80\n+OxVCUaMP8auWDQQpXpokTQDfthHvu1hI/n3OqKxKqG95MbGp3b6MTAuQHIVjE9Q\ngo76atjeurahT5JFr1/8nLXftKwiQCAjD4bnf++kcbnGThexFn/YNp5CKO0ked7U\n51HNZt05aADYEWTobEH5PP8xZAGG8II74dqbtr7DBlu6pH5ZMglwhEBqxugJsXhD\nju+GsOnozInYO3MkJcXXexrST/n5Rgmqi0uH9C00X4GyEVhqndHxrAB5MhdAGGnC\n2PzzffzOyCYgTmm3gnmPoDe91mtGAVxaZ8CatFxKWfRGfQltElPU+j8FzMow9h0d\nsUZM+KpjXWB8SHPueyA6/ojI1FDriXSETzlT505ogPunPHPHE0s3nzJ4gspdg/ZQ\nkmpU9VL9Dfr6okr99hJNju3bXAv5P9qEWi2RTw4C79GLPMpPpUldcHJr6Xh5T+bT\nFj4KK+gPyWlY73ltLN40Jg2d95BzBq3Iz1ypuEGvjJT3Woi1JlcTNLvT5BCgooNQ\nEeMnEdToXZwVNZVaGrCr\n=jsiz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 83f6f7cffd1758253d5d872fe21f7d5243fd632b\nparent feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780958588 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780958588 -0700\n\nfeat(doctor): report editor and pager environment (#27081)\n\n## Background\n\nThis was prompted by\n[#26858](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/26858), where the\nattached doctor report did not include the editor selection and I had to\n[ask which editor was in\nuse](https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/26858#issuecomment-4653829891)\nbefore investigating the external-editor newline issue. Capturing these\nvariables in doctor makes that context available up front in future\nreports.\n\n`codex doctor` is intended to capture enough local context to diagnose\nstartup and terminal behavior, but it did not report the environment\nvariables that select an external editor or configure command pagers.\n\nThe TUI [prefers `VISUAL` over\n`EDITOR`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c/codex-rs/tui/src/external_editor.rs#L31-L38),\nso missing or unexpected values can explain why the external-editor\nshortcut fails or launches the wrong command. Pager values are also\nuseful inherited-shell context even though [unified exec normalizes its\neffective pager variables to\n`cat`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c/codex-rs/core/src/unified_exec/process_manager.rs#L60-L70).\n\nThese variables can contain arbitrary command arguments or inline\nenvironment assignments. The human report is local, but `codex doctor\n--json` may be attached to feedback, so the machine-readable report\nshould not include their raw contents.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Report `VISUAL` and `EDITOR` in the system environment details, using\n`not set` when either variable is absent.\n- Report inherited `PAGER`, `GIT_PAGER`, `GH_PAGER`, and `LESS` values\nwhen present.\n- Preserve full values in local human output while reducing these fields\nto `set` or `not set` in redacted JSON output.\n- Add structured check, JSON-redaction, rendered-output, and snapshot\ncoverage.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. From `codex-rs`, run Codex with explicit editor and pager variables:\n\n   ```sh\nenv VISUAL='code --wait' EDITOR=vim PAGER='less -R' GIT_PAGER=delta\nGH_PAGER=less LESS=-FRX \\\n     cargo run -p codex-cli --bin codex -- doctor --no-color\n   ```\n\n2. Confirm the `system` details show the full values for all six\nvariables.\n3. Unset the pager variables and rerun the command. Confirm pager rows\nare omitted while missing editor variables are shown as `not set`.\n4. Run the same configured environment with `doctor --json`. Confirm\neach configured editor or pager field is reported as `set` and none of\nthe raw commands or arguments appear in the JSON.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli` (279 tests passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-08T22:43:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0473a5cc522cd8d0a798595c0a08ce661eb2a0ab/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786"}]},{"sha":"feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZlY2ExNjBkYTQ3YjY3OGI3M2IzM2RkOGEwOGUwMTBlODZiODE3ODY","commit":{"author":{"name":"richardopenai","email":"richardlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T22:29:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T22:29:51Z"},"message":"[codex] Add OTEL counter descriptions (#26091)\n\n## Why\n\nMetric descriptions should be declared with reusable OTEL instruments\ninstead of being coupled to individual consumers. Counter descriptions\nare the smallest API primitive needed by the exec-server observability\nwork.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `counter_with_description` while preserving the existing counter\nAPI.\n- Caches counters by name and description so instrument metadata remains\npart of the declaration identity.\n- Covers the exported description together with the existing value and\nattribute contract.\n\nThis PR only adds counter descriptions. It does not add gauges,\nsecond-based durations, or exec-server adoption.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **#26091: counter descriptions**\n2. #27057: gauge instruments\n3. #27058: second-based duration histograms\n\nRelated independent coverage: #27059 tests OTLP HTTP log and trace event\nexport.\n\nThe `codex-exec-server` bounded service tag now stays with the\nexec-server adoption change instead of this reusable infrastructure\nstack.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-otel`\n- `just fix -p codex-otel`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"bd951ac2a340e39cf9eeaa175c0756c62fe08f18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bd951ac2a340e39cf9eeaa175c0756c62fe08f18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJ0JfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZl0QAChhpa2DPlwU1cDtfr23qE4p\nsr+YaXP+WpXH9/9uxlHIHk4KkocQw3c45QXZ5gJ82ShVjZC+CA/yJgpgLtUppLBD\nnZyxd4O/isHUMp4Y5DiXMcQhK/G4EZh4vPxaQv9jgp+21Q/dFHJ2Y0kGgOeQGHAC\nlmnlj6uT3At0B3SE4TRpYEpyhK/W9hc5texzBycN/CL9WazsNEmDqXLwBBAp94SC\nON2cHmd6VTlbVZA/I/ci/Lt+nrXZYkeL4PRrKvd4sae4gJvYEnIXcv79WISYRkkf\nrj0MoN76fyDvRvWv5xKPGVIbBbwW9/eQEWGh8I4txrWpvTDVsZ3jog0kRTBlFEia\nLx2ZDx+yU5PcjJTlnngj95hZp9inK4OaVmiiPDnRnUl0FSEuLtVJHk0Z87jEy7eb\nSba9vE9a4DOtp0+t1y8cDV8nKVSY4Y+YTtHIFUP7tReHsDWIBTnYchoPkffkYqYW\nc7hWLzJxgv/8TEB8zZfcx8DXdN0FwV/TpQBj/i+3vIrk3JOPNtLDEKdZcQgcdxd3\nPp9jWpCr7PX2BSelh/E2+CRVcecaeqxM3xhrGdkrqxPWiSHVz53b2RHvV4aJYKe/\nTR6ZdcLNPN/hq1zjLvads42h7b1tXUCflDPQJ3x3szMD1SMwp4l5T73623U06ZrS\nETANyo7AowG8c+qrJEpo\n=gLeO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bd951ac2a340e39cf9eeaa175c0756c62fe08f18\nparent 381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf\nauthor richardopenai <richardlee@openai.com> 1780957791 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780957791 +0000\n\n[codex] Add OTEL counter descriptions (#26091)\n\n## Why\n\nMetric descriptions should be declared with reusable OTEL instruments\ninstead of being coupled to individual consumers. Counter descriptions\nare the smallest API primitive needed by the exec-server observability\nwork.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `counter_with_description` while preserving the existing counter\nAPI.\n- Caches counters by name and description so instrument metadata remains\npart of the declaration identity.\n- Covers the exported description together with the existing value and\nattribute contract.\n\nThis PR only adds counter descriptions. It does not add gauges,\nsecond-based durations, or exec-server adoption.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **#26091: counter descriptions**\n2. #27057: gauge instruments\n3. #27058: second-based duration histograms\n\nRelated independent coverage: #27059 tests OTLP HTTP log and trace event\nexport.\n\nThe `codex-exec-server` bounded service tag now stays with the\nexec-server adoption change instead of this reusable infrastructure\nstack.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-otel`\n- `just fix -p codex-otel`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T22:29:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/feca160da47b678b73b33dd8a08e010e86b81786/comments","author":{"login":"richardopenai","id":272641442,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAtog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272641442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai","html_url":"https://github.com/richardopenai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf"}]},{"sha":"381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM4MWYwZGU1MzFlMGJjNzc1OTg2MzI5NWZjMzMzZGQwMDg3YjRmYWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:47:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:47:09Z"},"message":"Use cached remote plugin catalog for plugin list (#26932)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis changes the default remote plugin marketplace listing to use the\ncached global remote catalog when it is already present on disk. The\nforeground `plugin/list` response can then return from the local catalog\ncache instead of waiting on `/ps/plugins/list`.\n\nWhen a cached global catalog was present at the start of the request,\n`plugin/list` still schedules a background refresh through the existing\nplugin-list background task path so the disk cache is updated for future\nrequests. Cache misses keep the existing synchronous remote fetch path\nand write the cache, and they do not schedule an extra duplicate\nbackground `/ps/plugins/list` refresh.\n\nInstalled/enabled state continues to come from the existing remote\ninstalled overlay path. This change only affects the global remote\ncatalog directory data used by `plugin/list`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_list_uses_cached_global_remote_catalog_and_refreshes_it`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"4890179a982e7a2fd27e60f1b930d32d5997ed31","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4890179a982e7a2fd27e60f1b930d32d5997ed31"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJzhdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQakQABlMEc17PiZFnkv2W0w5qGdo\nZIxtEDoigVNChfJ08FXMpksNEIMsWZ4NEkRILkkJhlTRMUJUQBxrgRacLJxzKv9X\nKOQKdtBYMq8HOHJFHI3nvm0F3ZV7pCuCrWGVWhXcEIVITeZTwcHGn1xw4+WKV45a\ny9HH7Q8Ga9nRHQm7rQmq+QMPOfOhsuYKm1dl2AnSnzEg0U9M3zTMlrOhe8RTtjp0\nHJ8te7fpahpsKZv8Leo09hdqbO9RfSlmyajngdvkKlcVTXCvNEPI70XWQmjNpMdp\nncc4KSTYO/RBgZ7+is3sc3vbIkcB6awrlwebEPmUXqF2wuzMuM/dhA/LydHxXGyK\n6bm0GXE7bdWab4TpqC4xHBnCs2N5eHJf4dQlGAFkAEQaQNXuxfRFjVM3JoC67OWn\nWwCZhPCxOl5s/Q2sjdx0rPLr3mB3vTlLn+St5zo4ii8S0ua9/s4fkwfVjz0lJQEn\niJBCQmtpcY1zDmG2LWT1T87piT1f7kHTef6KlZGH8CacLyoV8uO+AMVcigPbWBWy\nK7yidsbWdulvWnYnJlcLxYd8++VZDpx893++yMmvskeApI+IWgZ8Pc+8Amb2tdCc\nhiegmNIC9yEdy3SC1BMKJZcJNMvYxWTLcQIJJjWIE0CPYlpTPnEKE6XMEgx9SJRw\nr/MtS/jfE9cLu75MiznB\n=kRZL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4890179a982e7a2fd27e60f1b930d32d5997ed31\nparent daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780955229 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780955229 -0700\n\nUse cached remote plugin catalog for plugin list (#26932)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis changes the default remote plugin marketplace listing to use the\ncached global remote catalog when it is already present on disk. The\nforeground `plugin/list` response can then return from the local catalog\ncache instead of waiting on `/ps/plugins/list`.\n\nWhen a cached global catalog was present at the start of the request,\n`plugin/list` still schedules a background refresh through the existing\nplugin-list background task path so the disk cache is updated for future\nrequests. Cache misses keep the existing synchronous remote fetch path\nand write the cache, and they do not schedule an extra duplicate\nbackground `/ps/plugins/list` refresh.\n\nInstalled/enabled state continues to come from the existing remote\ninstalled overlay path. This change only affects the global remote\ncatalog directory data used by `plugin/list`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_list_uses_cached_global_remote_catalog_and_refreshes_it`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:47:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/381f0de531e0bc7759863295fc333dd0087b4faf/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4"}]},{"sha":"daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRhZjc2YTU3ZDI1NjRiZTg1YjZlMzRjMjVhMjkzODBiM2Q0MzE1YjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:46:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:46:59Z"},"message":"[codex] Prune stale curated plugin caches (#26934)\n\nCurated plugin startup refresh now removes cached plugins whose names no\nlonger appear in the raw openai-curated marketplace. This prevents users\nwith the old standalone Google Sheets plugin selected locally from\ncontinuing to load its stale cache after the curated repo drops it.\n\nExisting config is left untouched, and plugins still present in the\nmarketplace continue to refresh from local curated sources.\n\nValidation:\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"d97d82800c1fecd8338ce096fccd9469cd93fc14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d97d82800c1fecd8338ce096fccd9469cd93fc14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJzhTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApbQQADzRA+zepKH44GXYZuz+uCPN\nRg+pNeU7Kdkm/92MwfAehT4Cz0V5kPI1O3qpOduME0UHkaex9QhxEUF3sF25c9hs\nNL24JTWphiroWeKZZ/9KpwcKByrpPkrt1vQuZGTCXpR3mT5JVw181ylbrypfGv34\nkv1+l7z/3lXzMxqQghCv2K+bo9JZkdPBmy17r2i/0rYfSX7nRHGknGxrCrTghoHN\n6rO/ngW+B5C6GqREsPd2Fc3V7pDVes0tD4R+8xzPg7Ab94aL+g3z6s1MY5L3c8pW\nNhPSnMwdG+l89UdOnqkOVIFWn1B0YSnqVNQhcMAX51axCFn5ThWExuHM9nPeib26\nbPXzUMq6AgJAUCcgAgEtRT7dyO2uSmiXtRAzznOA8DJrjOEyiFP/68jy4s4XP7wT\ngJfaeuru2tgFYv98cYw1c5V6PUvIehGg2Hoj2+A5kjr/4wvKyQ3532NMDnvVAn+1\n1wTzBJb+Bh6qd/04mvBsXhiGzR0WcxCfUBIjtFsAtYs/AsXEUqJn/5Mx7RD4QCYt\nGZu+CT1uDQ/vjilFzx0/gH6ZlOI0Py6WisTFzzgcPAkZrJy0pFBOvFwC9NABUrT4\nDLzHQR7SmrY0BrlCiMZy0vHuwJFKilNd19+qp4nKhCUHpYXYcgSQ+rEQ/bDDkTwm\nJQec2jPOzaIYKCs/wa/G\n=tP14\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d97d82800c1fecd8338ce096fccd9469cd93fc14\nparent b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780955219 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780955219 -0700\n\n[codex] Prune stale curated plugin caches (#26934)\n\nCurated plugin startup refresh now removes cached plugins whose names no\nlonger appear in the raw openai-curated marketplace. This prevents users\nwith the old standalone Google Sheets plugin selected locally from\ncontinuing to load its stale cache after the curated repo drops it.\n\nExisting config is left untouched, and plugins still present in the\nmarketplace continue to refresh from local curated sources.\n\nValidation:\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:46:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/daf76a57d2564be85b6e34c25a29380b3d4315b4/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5"}]},{"sha":"b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI4OWQ5MWY2ZmZlZTU0NzRmMjNhOTdiMjNiNDAxNjQ0YzRlMDg3ZDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:41:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:41:05Z"},"message":"feat: support oneOf and allOf in tool input schemas (#24118)\n\n## Why\n\nSome connector golden schemas use JSON Schema composition keywords\nbeyond `anyOf`, specifically top-level or nested `oneOf` and `allOf`.\nCodex currently needs to preserve those shapes when parsing MCP tool\ninput schemas so connector tools do not lose valid schema structure\nduring normalization.\n\nTo prevent an increased Responses API error rate, this PR will be merged\nafter the Responses API supports top-level `oneOf`/`allOf`.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds `oneOf` and `allOf` support to `JsonSchema`, matching the\nexisting `anyOf` handling.\n- Traverses `oneOf` and `allOf` anywhere schema children are visited,\nincluding sanitization, definition reachability, description stripping,\nand deep schema compaction.\n- Adds a final large-schema compaction pass that prunes schema objects\ncontaining `anyOf`, `oneOf`, or `allOf` to `{}` if earlier compaction\npasses still leave the schema over budget.\n\n## Validation\nGolden schema token validation over `2,025` schemas under\n`golden_schemas`, all parsed successfully. Token count is `o200k_base`\nover compact JSON from `parse_tool_input_schema`.\n\n| Percentile | Before PR | After oneOf/allOf | After pruning |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| p0 | 9 | 9 | 9 |\n| p10 | 63 | 64 | 64 |\n| p25 | 86 | 87 | 87 |\n| p50 | 125 | 128 | 128 |\n| p75 | 203 | 206 | 206 |\n| p90 | 327 | 333 | 333 |\n| p95 | 460 | 473 | 473 |\n| p99 | 763 | 779 | 779 |\n| max | 891 | 955 | 955 |\n\nTotals:\n\n| Parser state | Total tokens |\n|---|---:|\n| Before PR | 345,713 |\n| After oneOf/allOf | 352,686 |\n| After pruning | 352,686 |\n\nThe pruning column matches the oneOf/allOf column for this corpus\nbecause no parsed compact golden schema remains over the `4,000`\ncompact-byte budget after the earlier compaction passes.","tree":{"sha":"271b9cd47362885e8c4eb53cd2c4ac7a3d685bc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/271b9cd47362885e8c4eb53cd2c4ac7a3d685bc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJzbxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAONoQAKh/fLmNyA4C49bwQ/vXbR5j\ny8nvg6AX/7uPM9SmiqOQKMg8RMnX29McS1hws2E3y0S26aQVFWMGjTXs79eOF7Uq\nuNw+lC3cLCIgae4Gv8XPuqH93fusHJr6JJ8GepD2hfhY2OfNZNFYskQuv8RJRgxB\n57Mb79wvwHalyOC8b2NNKYBI9T44izNQmMmPCrnUir5GfVmIyLj1D8L/HflrXOpR\n/jqbzA4aQE4bA5Efum+r9IlbFvpPVuOESyT4G4pB42Z7DI6tHa9KacE9N1ktyM+a\nYqnMOemiQND32AI37pVVDzm32xmMun1/ZP2PGqHQhFAMelOZj2hEpdRLsGS7m/j+\nHiyLd1fzPbsgPqbro9et0IEduoKTkZ+9fVZwtMbWCK17/u0Ugmdw0wghnfrHtpc5\nAiuoCF3F2877d4nYstYRkHgSLzXLJvbLrLKvcx5gej6LwCcd917pZXUsb/RokSnZ\nfYgyh3+t31wTvfa5L8utwRGPbaji7E46VpkPS1GfNfjb2ISkcPP7JtklJXn9YR7Z\n8rt1H5tcRsMQBk6TAUkW1+sRXXKBSDW8nEiV1+/TKCDMFBFiQicq6Ikus0HlzGKg\nFarGKtBWz7+NZjnLEJNABMMRVDEYtVQ0j/TCsYqZvU74gxbS2Z2wEM8xOKw4GY8O\n3TFqyOSXCct0cj17MnpD\n=CHQX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 271b9cd47362885e8c4eb53cd2c4ac7a3d685bc0\nparent 56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1780954865 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780954865 +0000\n\nfeat: support oneOf and allOf in tool input schemas (#24118)\n\n## Why\n\nSome connector golden schemas use JSON Schema composition keywords\nbeyond `anyOf`, specifically top-level or nested `oneOf` and `allOf`.\nCodex currently needs to preserve those shapes when parsing MCP tool\ninput schemas so connector tools do not lose valid schema structure\nduring normalization.\n\nTo prevent an increased Responses API error rate, this PR will be merged\nafter the Responses API supports top-level `oneOf`/`allOf`.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds `oneOf` and `allOf` support to `JsonSchema`, matching the\nexisting `anyOf` handling.\n- Traverses `oneOf` and `allOf` anywhere schema children are visited,\nincluding sanitization, definition reachability, description stripping,\nand deep schema compaction.\n- Adds a final large-schema compaction pass that prunes schema objects\ncontaining `anyOf`, `oneOf`, or `allOf` to `{}` if earlier compaction\npasses still leave the schema over budget.\n\n## Validation\nGolden schema token validation over `2,025` schemas under\n`golden_schemas`, all parsed successfully. Token count is `o200k_base`\nover compact JSON from `parse_tool_input_schema`.\n\n| Percentile | Before PR | After oneOf/allOf | After pruning |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| p0 | 9 | 9 | 9 |\n| p10 | 63 | 64 | 64 |\n| p25 | 86 | 87 | 87 |\n| p50 | 125 | 128 | 128 |\n| p75 | 203 | 206 | 206 |\n| p90 | 327 | 333 | 333 |\n| p95 | 460 | 473 | 473 |\n| p99 | 763 | 779 | 779 |\n| max | 891 | 955 | 955 |\n\nTotals:\n\n| Parser state | Total tokens |\n|---|---:|\n| Before PR | 345,713 |\n| After oneOf/allOf | 352,686 |\n| After pruning | 352,686 |\n\nThe pruning column matches the oneOf/allOf column for this corpus\nbecause no parsed compact golden schema remains over the `4,000`\ncompact-byte budget after the earlier compaction passes.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:41:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b89d91f6ffee5474f23a97b23b401644c4e087d5/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c"}]},{"sha":"56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU2NTU0OTA0YmFiY2FhY2Y0NDQ0YTJjYzkwNzE2ODgwODM3ZGZmN2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"fchen-oai","email":"fchen@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:33:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:33:57Z"},"message":"[codex] Require complete main-agent skill reads (#27044)\n\n## Summary\n- require the main agent to read selected `SKILL.md` files completely,\ncontinuing truncated or paginated reads through EOF\n- require the main agent to personally read task-required instruction\nreferences instead of delegating their interpretation\n- clarify that progressive disclosure selects relevant files without\npermitting partial reads\n- preserve subagent use for task work when the selected skill allows it\n- cover both absolute-path and aliased-root prompt variants\n\n## Why\nPartial reads can skip routing and verification requirements later in\nskill instructions. Delegated summaries can also omit constraints the\nmain agent needs to follow. The existing \"Read only enough\" wording made\nboth behaviors appear acceptable.\n\n## Impact\nAgents should follow complete selected skill instructions while\ncontinuing to avoid unrelated references, scripts, and assets. Subagents\nremain available for task execution where permitted.\n\n## Test plan\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills` (101 passed)\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"2af41b2927f927279053e5f2ce91534d6effe45b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2af41b2927f927279053e5f2ce91534d6effe45b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJzVFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/DkQAIT7jVndkKKx/eUKHESGCX/9\nK9QIQV0/0+RIT3BroiDVDEZ/Nh0tUw4mqJtgjFABgSzY+J+kdtFMbOBC6pRMSmPT\n51TacxsLvAaJ3jDUNrKnmMTRAMXAJzS8cHxCpxhMDobtolFQgcuzN0WqRMQxPDqb\nhcI78cSNPgEWW8O74x6JvGItpAO/tvn3YwdQxU3uAhaIhg/4U69Vdz97r/LrlcOS\nQwKeRaNPBkM7WIHMgATBmzditKzrDVk4e3DdoIpkxK5ipksRsBKEO51l/iBr6feF\nJZJPLhWfG1A+d7+noF9p3uesH+FQlRh8buvE3a3Db3dc0IVn8Rs5JkmCgdXVbD3k\nlaC7QdGv5GWpuR9yneXVbD+vmpfeAxvbezp0vWFFy4Co8zs3uiGlU0qOPl3tZq7M\noCUNHrx58NlEuDrEn+VpC8+kf5QzV1ofnGIrPK5fyfaCQGBZcNHOLB8D/EZspwW1\nezY3WlIXLn0KBaI7L91Nbt/esl4ibAx78oc6elTJ27EtYlW2pPehFiigJk5QQZFT\nL5VNC5CPUddhzCrFhnUD7MJy5fuYN/CRuACBg6wZLXv1zdJZb2JuUkK3XVRXI5Op\nPsEiWIAohX0E8/1ztANRJdrBZlURxrFu+wXhn7Va/gS69mPRpf9Ghsc0a3xVUtPe\nrWG4+RyUks6Cu12dyjsi\n=bTS5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2af41b2927f927279053e5f2ce91534d6effe45b\nparent ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688\nauthor fchen-oai <fchen@openai.com> 1780954437 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780954437 -0700\n\n[codex] Require complete main-agent skill reads (#27044)\n\n## Summary\n- require the main agent to read selected `SKILL.md` files completely,\ncontinuing truncated or paginated reads through EOF\n- require the main agent to personally read task-required instruction\nreferences instead of delegating their interpretation\n- clarify that progressive disclosure selects relevant files without\npermitting partial reads\n- preserve subagent use for task work when the selected skill allows it\n- cover both absolute-path and aliased-root prompt variants\n\n## Why\nPartial reads can skip routing and verification requirements later in\nskill instructions. Delegated summaries can also omit constraints the\nmain agent needs to follow. The existing \"Read only enough\" wording made\nboth behaviors appear acceptable.\n\n## Impact\nAgents should follow complete selected skill instructions while\ncontinuing to avoid unrelated references, scripts, and assets. Subagents\nremain available for task execution where permitted.\n\n## Test plan\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills` (101 passed)\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:33:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56554904babcaacf4444a2cc90716880837dff7c/comments","author":{"login":"fchen-oai","id":288173853,"node_id":"U_kgDOES0vHQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288173853?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fchen-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fchen-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688"}]},{"sha":"ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVlNmM5MWQ1Y2ZkMGU2MzIzOWM3NWI0MWY0YTJkYzE0MTMwZDU2ODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:29:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:29:06Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] stop sending codex error subreason (#27060)\n\n## Summary\n- stop emitting `codex_error_subreason` on `codex_turn_event`\n- remove the transient analytics fact plumbing that copied\n`CodexErr::InvalidRequest(String)` into the event\n- update analytics serialization coverage accordingly\n\n## Why\n`codex_error_subreason` is a free-form copy of `InvalidRequest(String)`,\nincluding raw provider 400 bodies in some paths. That makes it unsafe as\nan analytics field because it can carry user-derived or sensitive text.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`","tree":{"sha":"08a2fa68bd0bce341cde59c28219b21ae3ddf809","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/08a2fa68bd0bce341cde59c28219b21ae3ddf809"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJzQiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3lcQAIDq6SO1dTsBFw8w15gea1We\nfnr7FpbF04OrkFsM54cBtsgW05UP8xU/yCGnQckriKogcSdyXaQ8/weS7eXujRD2\n9OL716yQ0q2zcWj6mdDMQugxQKc0LYEGbsEkcUdrvhmheLA5Fpg2rqLjSiHKo8r9\nH/1TYqKgaiAY3LE4WjOGjZ1zBrZwCPUXzGT4QpWFl5LXfOodRR6+SpM1EgOqLCq4\nLIXI69M6MbC8NnrTsD2OPn3ngR0L5VydU3M5broMXdxRWKGcOI0jfpma0YtX7FSM\n/G4aqgpprmruAIiJMmtuDDgOhvPj1PGF03avntP3ImRbX5JwJ/EG1GRKWQ839nL0\nEw78HlZCM/cQ0oOv/2Y6soyTG5vG22pYzYtx/+uqbTJr3FnIe5LwHrzr1iPMwSYG\nVYyjVnKHv7RE2lki1OgGeLpX9x+rIlpQyvfx9Fc6MOj/537uF/a6SOJ4mSN9ikP0\ngfAy7qw+aLRzO/rXEAK25nz4jkNHDoKlWEN1pf0GHtnit2zUnYgJONoxSTjgk/qY\nfsrLVv2r45QxAjJQHgUxUV/TAcbJuglaGusTsXqfiLxiQi++du1PA70RtBKdx9sS\n4q08snWPOKJQ0fLTsloSxuTx5JMSEQ0VwRZcyjmOBwQP07q1SuWeWvr7HBJCkc0E\n0+oq/dC8WVAW0MMiDtMk\n=zjmQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 08a2fa68bd0bce341cde59c28219b21ae3ddf809\nparent 123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1780954146 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780954146 +0000\n\n[codex-analytics] stop sending codex error subreason (#27060)\n\n## Summary\n- stop emitting `codex_error_subreason` on `codex_turn_event`\n- remove the transient analytics fact plumbing that copied\n`CodexErr::InvalidRequest(String)` into the event\n- update analytics serialization coverage accordingly\n\n## Why\n`codex_error_subreason` is a free-form copy of `InvalidRequest(String)`,\nincluding raw provider 400 bodies in some paths. That makes it unsafe as\nan analytics field because it can carry user-derived or sensitive text.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:29:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ee6c91d5cfd0e63239c75b41f4a2dc14130d5688/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5"}]},{"sha":"123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEyM2NmNjJhNDg1ZGUyM2E4OTYwMjYwZjViYjAwYjg2YWY2Nzc4YzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:23:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:23:55Z"},"message":"Route image edits through referenced file paths (#26486)\n\n## Why\n\nImage edits should use the exact images selected by the model instead of\ninferring edit inputs from conversation history.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replaced the image tool's `action` argument with optional\n`referenced_image_paths`.\n- Treats omitted or empty references as generation and populated\nreferences as editing.\n- Reads referenced absolute image paths and packages them as image data\nURLs for the edit request.\n- Removed the previous history-selection and image-count heuristics.\n- Updated direct and code-mode tool instructions and calls.\n- Added an app-server integration test covering an attached image routed\nto the image edit endpoint.\n\n## Validation\n- Tested end-to-end on local `just codex` with copy pasted image,\nattached image, etc.\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_edit_uses_attached_model_visible_image`\n- `just fix -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"4e2f5f0fb2ea1e6761e01dfe2c0e817265dcca81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4e2f5f0fb2ea1e6761e01dfe2c0e817265dcca81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJzLrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIwAQAFvco5oHFBkxkL3QvtsHA4BU\n/SSj37xCSw1YjK8IpTWgvwpWhK99Syz1kqEGgVRj6F5smdkpocsKi7TqgotlHyGR\nh11LNNBaZdXKMPZejltBVKE4xNQDBK1ZuD/Am0hCNJiFQhZiyqErGwGUmtREyq6b\n/q0G/BVV3Oe9qmwAd6lVQYtWACfVDMxMILu7d6gGO72gTGqydbIm5z9HQSD6DF2p\n8tUQ9yJjyuAblJ01Pi4cPnQaC3KePJ7XWEw7H3cTJL6HrLOd+S9YcAzplZdBFcal\nZ1Vagho1bwFBujy1NPNFDtNx/813UkjYfQ3dxQ8LF0ap2Tnr9BoXc/OR8h9WR8si\nVbGdmwGkBo/xVxVG0PUX3yMutqj7EnH+RGbdtsZyg7mUZlyFtJxe2H70pjAFO3dw\ns9eej8gyYrvaX8hW3A0LS4OMIxFS9m58hTYak3Za6EBfLohAdOHN/FrX4MfeYIDL\nWPITSgazMavlXc0qenbS0cgXymF2eBpLxuYxo/XNH5lCquEarrlRT7EqQG4HrY/p\nUgsRHTACcvEeFIVoGuJO4rLtlv6fnYw7UWtQH0b1NPVum8yM3i0dkOpliXtnYYNr\ngYrnld/+lNAmIYuCH7kG9hx14r4yAsNigR9rorJysquWYUpWgntRYGuN1qUsObwB\n2vY3aDvVGTEoCLi+7Ucl\n=Jyti\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4e2f5f0fb2ea1e6761e01dfe2c0e817265dcca81\nparent 85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780953835 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780953835 -0700\n\nRoute image edits through referenced file paths (#26486)\n\n## Why\n\nImage edits should use the exact images selected by the model instead of\ninferring edit inputs from conversation history.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replaced the image tool's `action` argument with optional\n`referenced_image_paths`.\n- Treats omitted or empty references as generation and populated\nreferences as editing.\n- Reads referenced absolute image paths and packages them as image data\nURLs for the edit request.\n- Removed the previous history-selection and image-count heuristics.\n- Updated direct and code-mode tool instructions and calls.\n- Added an app-server integration test covering an attached image routed\nto the image edit endpoint.\n\n## Validation\n- Tested end-to-end on local `just codex` with copy pasted image,\nattached image, etc.\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_edit_uses_attached_model_visible_image`\n- `just fix -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:23:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/123cf62a485de23a8960260f5bb00b86af6778c5/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343"}]},{"sha":"85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg1ZmQ1MmY3ZTRhZWJmYzM5MjI5YjUwZTZmMGMwOTJkZDAwY2EzNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:03:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T21:03:37Z"},"message":"Enforce configured network proxy in codex sandbox (#27035)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex sandbox` can start a network proxy from a configured permission\nprofile. Previously, sandbox-level containment was tied to managed\nnetwork requirements rather than whether a proxy was actually active.\nThis meant config-driven proxy policies were not consistently enforced\nas the sandbox's only network path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Enable proxy-only network containment whenever `codex sandbox` starts\na network proxy.\n- Apply the same active-proxy check to the macOS and Linux sandbox\npaths.\n- Add a Linux regression test that verifies a sandboxed command cannot\nestablish a direct connection while the configured proxy is active.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli debug_sandbox::tests`\n- `sandbox_with_network_proxy_blocks_direct_loopback_access` runs on\nLinux to cover the config-driven proxy path end to end.","tree":{"sha":"a63ff8df7878ac3fc6a55f9aee8a3ade8b35ae97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a63ff8df7878ac3fc6a55f9aee8a3ade8b35ae97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJy4pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/WoQAI+oTzGr5XLL5uZn5NpF6dMv\nLRY1nUmKXc1hwxHnHEDSANIzN5BeIRYeCQWFDbwMKwJdENxkV8Fekg6L4Q80GWEv\n0RXo4MgIatYWjm+kCtQ3UCHfLEv1ywyRuyKGPCTUsiCCmJ/Oy58GN3Vp5RO9g9OS\nfhY3IRoHSjsFYSJ29XF1BxBA8AykCnF3PL/+nGZ86p36k0ihsXQvjcDlT5ymP+c7\nWNkxoEfS2/EcgYeknGN/PNZdl8DgU6forxUqBJNjHMOSY5MhLzZr61kkh1xj92y/\nuVj6AoXg4YCQ9VnAxpl2FtG8NS3sKlsrs3VRIR2y+LCFaK/UM7+a6/WXtccgTdSt\noeFVp0UcGlpylNXkHyIfLu+DQfZn1C/zTIgW+DA01+NqtFEJgCSD/iyhFrM+41fj\nWq/EQ+iMx60+S+k1w7lVUM4GzjgPLYmzRyD3ZwoELnqOIsAxTc8/BSh576BtSjme\nI2rypDnaq37IXhK+lCaOOMCSubQ71pjNA94Ml0RWat0aQ1j9FQ8L40DFhTlXuo16\nt8erOXcjeIKqGFFKYe8KyT8BwxOCC8r4C7pTEoWU2YGxSbCinbC68laTlbxfb461\noD2fnOkvECVQDih28WA2rNQRsApM9bEqFHy0dEOUSzbFjTh0oVYsCrIAoBtcN+Fi\nrpizFYdltBB97+yQw8Hn\n=ybeH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a63ff8df7878ac3fc6a55f9aee8a3ade8b35ae97\nparent e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780952617 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780952617 -0700\n\nEnforce configured network proxy in codex sandbox (#27035)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex sandbox` can start a network proxy from a configured permission\nprofile. Previously, sandbox-level containment was tied to managed\nnetwork requirements rather than whether a proxy was actually active.\nThis meant config-driven proxy policies were not consistently enforced\nas the sandbox's only network path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Enable proxy-only network containment whenever `codex sandbox` starts\na network proxy.\n- Apply the same active-proxy check to the macOS and Linux sandbox\npaths.\n- Add a Linux regression test that verifies a sandboxed command cannot\nestablish a direct connection while the configured proxy is active.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli debug_sandbox::tests`\n- `sandbox_with_network_proxy_blocks_direct_loopback_access` runs on\nLinux to cover the config-driven proxy path end to end.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T21:03:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/85fd52f7e4aebfc39229b50e6f0c092dd00ca343/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f"}]},{"sha":"e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUwZWU0OTFkZjM1MWFkODVkMzVmODc5ZDJlMmI4YjMwYzg2NjgxNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:59:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:59:23Z"},"message":"cli: add -P sandbox permissions profile alias (#27054)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex sandbox --permissions-profile` is useful when running commands\nunder a named permissions profile, but the long option is cumbersome for\na debugging-oriented command. `-p` is already used for the config\nprofile selector, so `-P` gives the permissions profile selector a\ncompact, non-conflicting alias.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `short = 'P'` to the `permissions_profile` option for the macOS,\nLinux, and Windows sandbox command structs in\n[`codex-rs/cli/src/lib.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/6d9f9c5cdcaa0a156aa2dabbde259ae5e9e8bc0b/codex-rs/cli/src/lib.rs#L29-L112).\n- Added parser coverage for `codex sandbox -P :workspace -- echo` in\n[`codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/6d9f9c5cdcaa0a156aa2dabbde259ae5e9e8bc0b/codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs#L2883-L2896).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli` passed, including the new\n`sandbox_parses_permissions_profile_short_alias` parser test.","tree":{"sha":"9d603f68b52fec547cc228d9c2e0a2a0d722f02e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9d603f68b52fec547cc228d9c2e0a2a0d722f02e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJy0rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWcMQAF02YKVSWLyCd1AguEHBBnnD\ndKyDs8Zf/JknTC5q+eMnLV+05f4nwjdHBVrMoiixS1ICy9ApzEBAgoyptNCqauGh\nJJertnGA5phz7athuPSLXzgNn2nMvgCmiYmM0dbF/FcZP8nUZX3WeGcBf7vKDyr7\nzXL1Th5dh+NBYSYXtXG6sUe9TKrkr4IU9nk3ZpdahCIac1Y8+HTqBuNZ3iN5JXOU\nbhHFkX759zMNQt2uA9e1oAKdSKhJPX1u9X1ej/kjTKTMatUVyUf2a+es1mAgDIVZ\n7FogY4fuHVmGIuGOA18UXluzNsEzvqKqTEErB0eJpTu/uaLXrLSVUR5gDozn/CFW\n9Mfb9FY2uyCSIIBoyIVH4SwW0mKR96/alku09xlweU4mpuPYHFjnCapP8FaTIw/E\nLYSFPUV3SpdC86fDXSB0J/ril9ILkbv9FrethJr3mhH4/r/MzxccYKASOurbM+dn\nn9fmcn60CQaVTWDwIr+U97vNaJqv1XVphLDfxXhSspdtgHHgRRRLy9QnayYzpO1R\n7T+lx/90P26grBHNRFR9iZc2u3LCXqUPMicVW0BER8aS7YKO6L+n8SlZqxiQ9DeX\nh2wcPDc23K+Cemu3ptS8WUZ9cd+LLKFJi9mYbau3nk1w5F7U38MfBvQ8ftXOL4eo\njjtSXC6Gb5BK9D1U30Yi\n=db6b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9d603f68b52fec547cc228d9c2e0a2a0d722f02e\nparent f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780952363 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780952363 +0000\n\ncli: add -P sandbox permissions profile alias (#27054)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex sandbox --permissions-profile` is useful when running commands\nunder a named permissions profile, but the long option is cumbersome for\na debugging-oriented command. `-p` is already used for the config\nprofile selector, so `-P` gives the permissions profile selector a\ncompact, non-conflicting alias.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `short = 'P'` to the `permissions_profile` option for the macOS,\nLinux, and Windows sandbox command structs in\n[`codex-rs/cli/src/lib.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/6d9f9c5cdcaa0a156aa2dabbde259ae5e9e8bc0b/codex-rs/cli/src/lib.rs#L29-L112).\n- Added parser coverage for `codex sandbox -P :workspace -- echo` in\n[`codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/6d9f9c5cdcaa0a156aa2dabbde259ae5e9e8bc0b/codex-rs/cli/src/main.rs#L2883-L2896).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli` passed, including the new\n`sandbox_parses_permissions_profile_short_alias` parser test.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T20:59:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0ee491df351ad85d35f879d2e2b8b30c866814f/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3"}]},{"sha":"f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYzYzEyODM0MTFlZGFkY2MwNTIyYmVhMzc2ZDBhZGM2OTYxZDVjYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:55:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:55:15Z"},"message":"Pair thread environment settings (#26687)\n\n## Why\n\nThread cwd and environment selections are a single logical setting in\ncore: updating one without the other can silently desynchronize the\nnext-turn execution context. This change makes that relationship\nexplicit in the internal thread settings flow while preserving the\nexisting app-server public API shape.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Moved the cwd/environment pair through internal\n`ThreadSettingsOverrides.environment_settings` instead of a top-level\ninternal `cwd` field.\n- Kept `thread/settings/update` public params unchanged, with app-server\ntranslating top-level `cwd` into the paired internal settings shape.\n- Moved `Op::UserInput` environment overrides into thread settings so\nuser turns and settings updates use the same core path.\n- Updated core, app-server, MCP, memories, sample, and test callsites to\nconstruct the paired settings shape.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Local test run starting after PR creation.","tree":{"sha":"6d75eaa7ecd67c9471e4177f3ede6100b47b25c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6d75eaa7ecd67c9471e4177f3ede6100b47b25c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJywzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiTMQAAFPLJPC7KosWh7EoFq/4iaI\nmi3CIfT8TudRa5osVeNOaTnZ1UM37fit9+b/Q/RnQK5mIgj4AaQaDsqGmsCDfTJD\norHmhEBBf24NtEZTNkgH+BuLnSOwKW4TWN+GAH3nQsSNBoO3K0Gp5qcnSbqFzZ62\nbYmHJWDH7aOTs//HACj4gLwo2xORAJDDFaSkYAdZznSq/MOLDo/ISgEie43c/HL/\nR1IhTCQeXojq0s5nmEB86wD7Gp0MqTQHxyAaY2QrmdG8yvVGL/JZXRF1JX0niilU\n4SpVn7TzuE+iAiEr/07xqN+7bZsjoYO0Dfd7Jk5vhj3uBukdI0E9rjfkiSxAuZ8i\nQMzpgqJk0t5fzoin0CvftCvrI24W9djcuO7GIxtj9N/znPttq2EExupWeQtCUzBL\nbf+cfsjkubUu2NlnaEgVNZbuhsUAP8SQ0iCi+GAHJ4Dr81cacFUa0eEhfU/JVQ+f\nUWys+lCTH6jJvJ40D3OM7MpVYuF+oa+vQNJe0FuXPTYKsxhjaxrOiaqTrzFOX691\nUPUErfLevy0wyvpKydQCO52Iu4Z1JVi2V/6CXyjtg/b6/LCNNTsfOLBPegZ7Ky2l\nmA4YM13Qo/gHv1MieEO8pQuv8HJxHZSPfmkifKh53QTvhCL/ySn7PPwCowK+kRoQ\na5NFuObpfcqgr9oH/rli\n=9GWB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6d75eaa7ecd67c9471e4177f3ede6100b47b25c8\nparent f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780952115 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780952115 -0700\n\nPair thread environment settings (#26687)\n\n## Why\n\nThread cwd and environment selections are a single logical setting in\ncore: updating one without the other can silently desynchronize the\nnext-turn execution context. This change makes that relationship\nexplicit in the internal thread settings flow while preserving the\nexisting app-server public API shape.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Moved the cwd/environment pair through internal\n`ThreadSettingsOverrides.environment_settings` instead of a top-level\ninternal `cwd` field.\n- Kept `thread/settings/update` public params unchanged, with app-server\ntranslating top-level `cwd` into the paired internal settings shape.\n- Moved `Op::UserInput` environment overrides into thread settings so\nuser turns and settings updates use the same core path.\n- Updated core, app-server, MCP, memories, sample, and test callsites to\nconstruct the paired settings shape.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Local test run starting after PR creation.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T20:55:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f3c1283411edadcc0522bea376d0adc6961d5ca3/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9"}]},{"sha":"f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY5YTY4MGI5MDc1NTYyMDkzZmY3OGU0NWZmNGZjYjJlOWEwMzQ4Zjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:32:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:32:10Z"},"message":"[codex] Calm multi-agent v2 usage prompts (#27037)\n\n## Summary\n- tighten the default multi-agent v2 root and subagent usage hints to\nbias toward local work\n- add a pre-call gate to the v2 spawn_agent description for independent,\nbounded, parallelizable subtasks\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- started just test -p codex-core, but it was interrupted before\ncompletion per follow-up request to commit and push immediately","tree":{"sha":"c553bfe9a44b3b69136bd6b6a398692af196bb46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c553bfe9a44b3b69136bd6b6a398692af196bb46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJybKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASYgQAHK3HchTZFZpotadbNxg8LEJ\n4H6mmLQdsPRZ6Nr979hjjUWMdTiGV5LT7KRjOxbSNJMqO29F+f8n2XxeIDZWu4ol\nWj8L/VZueb0nlI9ssyd8w5UxfCdkZkxYGqzfPejS6txDE4sukEv5mrtecawY6Es6\nc/TIwMhvGYJj3JuIXfJ7iw+Bokggs96tYmJrc12GejfKoLcDPna4E2Hh81vRuLGN\nthliM1YzI4KHB6TcEcGXcEGpFKrTXFGiBqmfkNCtOO1PS2fFDQLXN1oPICfgQW86\nmLB0SYYmqkHgDQ+ofpb+LmRR414dP4evIVMda+tPQhEv6w3AvqHsHMydmLNVZ3AH\nwHssh5xftPpZ91kWouHUlS5dZjEW2RIOx77r28pHbVf5M5Vkzgf/gI0NlYcWB8hs\nEAIPU22vgguF2xjw0JR6MipG31i7e7U2P6+MaygyPND5FtCyNrqoc0bhIj/PANpy\nig7sgrul1gIcVxAC62qTsCZ2NRVDipit0OXGLkZ6LipIsmxiWKiIJXHNFcUPyJez\ntrEG5+g5kawH5Yk7MEBMLjALtxqpzXg5RAnrxR2GuR1jQgnN3QV9hBuYt4Nyt4kL\n3QPVKUmuc/dYHK9lJpwagNk0lPgjreTR8+A2N/8N47oq+D5+T2z7YlNAghh7RdIf\nRHO4e+kxYZBhQooYDDQ6\n=UoaF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c553bfe9a44b3b69136bd6b6a398692af196bb46\nparent f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780950730 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780950730 +0200\n\n[codex] Calm multi-agent v2 usage prompts (#27037)\n\n## Summary\n- tighten the default multi-agent v2 root and subagent usage hints to\nbias toward local work\n- add a pre-call gate to the v2 spawn_agent description for independent,\nbounded, parallelizable subtasks\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- started just test -p codex-core, but it was interrupted before\ncompletion per follow-up request to commit and push immediately","verified_at":"2026-06-08T20:32:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f9a680b9075562093ff78e45ff4fcb2e9a0348f9/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1"}]},{"sha":"f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYzYTgwNzQ5NzU5MGE4Yjg2ZWY0NDQ4MDYwNmY5MmNjNzFjZjUyZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:09:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T20:09:06Z"},"message":"[codex] Clarify PR babysitter state mutations (#27038)\n\n# Why\n\nCodex is doing a bit too much on my PRs that it's babysitting. In\nparticular I'd like it to not interact with comment threads that involve\nother humans -- I should be the one doing human interaction. This is\ntricky because it's still very useful to be able to drop review comments\nmyself and have Codex iterate on them.\n\n## What\n\nThis updates `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/SKILL.md` with an explicit GitHub\nstate mutation policy.","tree":{"sha":"9b6f5ae4188100795c79d99343cb7b7236c66d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9b6f5ae4188100795c79d99343cb7b7236c66d46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJyFiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZTsQAH2FYZPY+27PcrXFuu5b452v\nULMuJ1ToqKmkrTrOoD8mkGPu1wZRZLKPZqWLYI0PZmhxkTH3INKJqRnhZXrkqain\nLVyV6wiQS6MFA0u7Zonbv1v4i+KA2OB9AFzfMxPXBvEfOmaJIzjSyQUwW3F6NFAl\nfpo7cJsWtcxqlfkPA8Y4fDZti3OHcOyJG3Ns5XQWnr/fRP0X3hRdUznUlG8lamFF\nCbQL5s3V5wNY0GhnxjAcfHraBdjZwsEgeyg3LZde5l4BQwgXz7cRSIJdqbMYBHe6\n+76G8hcpRx91l2SgiPiYHRdVrecoEMVfyTmGChAsF3vwt/FIIAixrILI3cGs+HDj\ncLlH/LVc55DNMe8uqDKCyzFxsDmJrXJC5NN3uxTKZ+I4UinkeaX+AY+5k+mf0Mc9\nL4l2i7F5wXR3pk0gDaE/CHiQW/LvrmvfcbHe6UoFC17wl/ZWLgIIaaGStuoTUatM\nfok4G0SzUFuMVl49p1uh5ldCEs2FrBi8aCZZWtvV6sylJO4UcJvhl8GVawOR7G6B\nvxgy6ZrlNNtYsDmhma2ws3GdT9Fng/S4b32mQuTgdN0V2DGc6MxL0wudnl/kmcee\nJ9agwUSqvNAq4WZzjJ3uCobcuUAAn2FFE8roA3zNXNhotjS84WBmHGkrCrmjZnPY\n2Muj/2a2W4smp20TdlAU\n=NkFP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9b6f5ae4188100795c79d99343cb7b7236c66d46\nparent 9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780949346 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780949346 -0700\n\n[codex] Clarify PR babysitter state mutations (#27038)\n\n# Why\n\nCodex is doing a bit too much on my PRs that it's babysitting. In\nparticular I'd like it to not interact with comment threads that involve\nother humans -- I should be the one doing human interaction. This is\ntricky because it's still very useful to be able to drop review comments\nmyself and have Codex iterate on them.\n\n## What\n\nThis updates `.codex/skills/babysit-pr/SKILL.md` with an explicit GitHub\nstate mutation policy.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T20:09:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f3a807497590a8b86ef44480606f92cc71cf52f1/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf"}]},{"sha":"9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDllMGQ3ZjAyYzk0MTZjNDZkZGU2ZTU3MTA2OGEwZmIwM2E0ZmFjZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:59:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:59:50Z"},"message":"fix: preserve auto review across config and delegation (#26230)\n\n## Why\n\nAuto Review should remain the effective approval reviewer when settings\ncross runtime boundaries. A config or app-server round trip must not\nchange the reviewer identity, and delegated work must not silently fall\nback to user review.\n\nThis requires both a stable canonical serialized value and propagation\nof the effective setting. `auto_review` is the canonical value across\nprotocol and app-server output, while `guardian_subagent` remains\naccepted as backward-compatible input.\n\n## What changed\n\n- serialize `ApprovalsReviewer::AutoReview` consistently as\n`auto_review` across core protocol and app-server v2\n- continue accepting `guardian_subagent` when reading existing config or\nclient requests\n- carry the active turn's approval reviewer into spawned agents\n- update config/debug expectations and add delegated-task regression\ncoverage\n\n## Scope\n\nThis does not change Guardian policy or remove compatibility with\nexisting `guardian_subagent` inputs. It preserves the selected reviewer\nacross serialization, config reloads, app-server settings, and delegated\ntask setup.\n\nRelated Guardian changes are split independently:\n\n- #26231 adds denials and soft denials\n- #26334 retries transient reviewer failures\n- #26333 reuses narrowly scoped low-risk approvals\n- #26232 adds TUI denial recovery\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` (224 passed)\n- regression coverage for delegated task reviewer propagation\n- serialization coverage for canonical `auto_review` output and legacy\n`guardian_subagent` input\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: saud-oai <saud@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b3c99dace3b799d0b66130ad97bfe31674bf92e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3b3c99dace3b799d0b66130ad97bfe31674bf92e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJxEmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbHIQAJeEzCC0GURzQ/WZum1F+07L\nfra+ENmrnY5bAhteRATrh4PyNgJc1DUVKM6oe3AgE3HNN5hsx0WX5qFFvNVN3NIx\nwmkua+IJ/D290noGrIeZOZa2e2uYLBgG9nTFlSa2mLNjGtbbYgMjDynh8L9dh3lB\nG4gYzjukijVIpRzhnuAvnOXvLW596sHRhUZN/XE6hTSFCQyc52r5bvaWIPVjhWN+\nhSEXCir1gODmYSYyM/8T9f/VaEEv2CCAB7jTOPTy1zorAkBgGXJXmVFQU/v81abd\nvdFUkjUBVtRK1BGPDJZuxvupx9OJdlQTEzd7oJ9JEkMWNwK4B8p3W2EplTtwoMNc\nmcjvdbFZwty7BQ4KKrZAgp6XwCrQ4ggnGG54KHtkSD0K0B+7g+qg+RqSly1+YYHu\n5qDLpNm8toh83DbHbabDN6tvv0TfXuYhCkeGoBQf3lVQtJr+2qskjTqaJLH42DnQ\nkWBSBMmOlMmjMTitTzdCegKOGtCibcoGPSXFFr1H4EnGG+xHxgOAT2E5USv/RBC2\nnUxiYkbbjkVcD5rBw4+Zc5gS+zaMQvKcEHrfOQ2Rhltz8oBwVsbG7ha6hVN3V+2u\nmgmZI1ImqAABa5+qpVvUK30UyKNckchQoowV4JbIGQpWgBqb58dPHZWd2gDM3pF2\nQBVDZvbOBEsbwf6MH/uE\n=5kC8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3b3c99dace3b799d0b66130ad97bfe31674bf92e\nparent 2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780945190 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780945190 +0000\n\nfix: preserve auto review across config and delegation (#26230)\n\n## Why\n\nAuto Review should remain the effective approval reviewer when settings\ncross runtime boundaries. A config or app-server round trip must not\nchange the reviewer identity, and delegated work must not silently fall\nback to user review.\n\nThis requires both a stable canonical serialized value and propagation\nof the effective setting. `auto_review` is the canonical value across\nprotocol and app-server output, while `guardian_subagent` remains\naccepted as backward-compatible input.\n\n## What changed\n\n- serialize `ApprovalsReviewer::AutoReview` consistently as\n`auto_review` across core protocol and app-server v2\n- continue accepting `guardian_subagent` when reading existing config or\nclient requests\n- carry the active turn's approval reviewer into spawned agents\n- update config/debug expectations and add delegated-task regression\ncoverage\n\n## Scope\n\nThis does not change Guardian policy or remove compatibility with\nexisting `guardian_subagent` inputs. It preserves the selected reviewer\nacross serialization, config reloads, app-server settings, and delegated\ntask setup.\n\nRelated Guardian changes are split independently:\n\n- #26231 adds denials and soft denials\n- #26334 retries transient reviewer failures\n- #26333 reuses narrowly scoped low-risk approvals\n- #26232 adds TUI denial recovery\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` (224 passed)\n- regression coverage for delegated task reviewer propagation\n- serialization coverage for canonical `auto_review` output and legacy\n`guardian_subagent` input\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: saud-oai <saud@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-08T18:59:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e0d7f02c9416c46dde6e571068a0fb03a4facdf/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678"}]},{"sha":"2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIzNzVjYjY0NDkzMzY3YzNmOGZmM2NiOThmY2ZmMmI2MzUwYWM2Nzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:47:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:47:23Z"},"message":"ci: template custom runner names by repo (#27024)\n\n## Why\n\nThese workflows currently hard-code the `codex` runner group and custom\nrunner labels. That makes the same workflow definitions less portable\nacross repository copies or renamed repos, even though the runner fleet\nfollows the repository name scheme. Template the runner identities from\nthe repository name so `openai/codex` still resolves to the existing\n`codex-*` runners while other repos can use their own `<repo>-*` runner\nnames.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaced custom runner `group` values such as `codex-runners` with\n`${{ github.event.repository.name }}-runners`.\n- Replaced custom runner labels such as `codex-linux-x64` and\n`codex-windows-arm64` with `${{ github.event.repository.name }}-...`.\n- Covered direct `runs-on` objects, matrix `runs_on` entries, reusable\nworkflow runner inputs, and release runner labels.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Parsed all `.github/workflows/*.yml` files as YAML with Ruby.\n- Searched `.github/workflows` to confirm no hardcoded runner-field\n`codex-runners` or `codex-*` labels remain.","tree":{"sha":"743e3b9fe14f301136a21e87169e55f69b0934fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/743e3b9fe14f301136a21e87169e55f69b0934fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJw47CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc0oQACtxvhCf7EYyHCUsT+pjyaur\nfrLGK/CmBhRlfMBBOh5vfrdYVJJH+04SsophC5YCfzAdkxbaWDNwOXHoAz1JKmid\n2xUOOmYJi48NuxAoO/m2Du2gD3FD/P+Dkqeaj2Mt+010oQmZP7fHDQ14MyPn1BWp\n1f7EFZlPIkRwHxgbmKml+C1SSwrjaE2S6hVIgFOTEDJGja79CyHDFw1G6/8EuPr3\nwwBNdufCw+h+QAXfzK5uSWzxepWYXSUBe8OgYVgq6ZHsY2pS1ZbNmsPgJZeMaoJo\nIWGewt52hRrQKe3z95xE+WiT8PMeqmrb4sFamRV7y6Df7jap/Ry8yvgKDL/co4xc\nz+4NmmvC3xdr9XurubBbKE24C7SmclzNb/4wly2stfv9MpBFwVM9jdi7JHHcIiIA\nO3VRXlvfPPAEQ2y61mbmL2L3GTa/S2Vsvx9r8Ioz132DF95olYpuX3Z83eF/C2M6\nDq1itL32cCTfzcUHmoTaGs3RgjanqmIfj6nEEqn3s9uU7z9zz3PsVct1YkffEi3x\ng3moxPKAWWiXfb8UcaKkZaeBPo/F5by/IbZ9HxVznbhvhdKiIdlENG6ZVzm1cCsj\nwFQuf5LyTQdW66e9uyVRRML9Ss3bMNojYtnConUO3E8XxOVO8ZaG+vB/EgOZ4dcH\nGDLcLn3qmhV17TIr3SIg\n=3gyZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 743e3b9fe14f301136a21e87169e55f69b0934fa\nparent 0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780944443 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780944443 -0700\n\nci: template custom runner names by repo (#27024)\n\n## Why\n\nThese workflows currently hard-code the `codex` runner group and custom\nrunner labels. That makes the same workflow definitions less portable\nacross repository copies or renamed repos, even though the runner fleet\nfollows the repository name scheme. Template the runner identities from\nthe repository name so `openai/codex` still resolves to the existing\n`codex-*` runners while other repos can use their own `<repo>-*` runner\nnames.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaced custom runner `group` values such as `codex-runners` with\n`${{ github.event.repository.name }}-runners`.\n- Replaced custom runner labels such as `codex-linux-x64` and\n`codex-windows-arm64` with `${{ github.event.repository.name }}-...`.\n- Covered direct `runs-on` objects, matrix `runs_on` entries, reusable\nworkflow runner inputs, and release runner labels.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Parsed all `.github/workflows/*.yml` files as YAML with Ruby.\n- Searched `.github/workflows` to confirm no hardcoded runner-field\n`codex-runners` or `codex-*` labels remain.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T18:47:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2375cb64493367c3f8ff3cb98fcff2b6350ac678/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8"}]},{"sha":"0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBhYTk5MzFhZWFkZDljYmIxZDZkMDJmODU0ZDE0MDJmOGRiMmJlYzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"mpc-oai","email":"mpc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:37:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:37:55Z"},"message":"[plugins] Expose marketplace source in marketplace list JSON (#27009)\n\n## Summary\n- Follow-up to #26417 and #26631\n- Add `marketplaceSource` to `codex plugin marketplace list --json`\nentries for configured marketplaces\n- Reuse the existing `marketplaceSource` shape from `codex plugin list\n--json`\n- Keep human-readable marketplace list output unchanged\n- Add CLI coverage for configured local and git marketplace sources\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"marketplaces\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"debug\",\n      \"root\": \"/path/to/.codex/.tmp/marketplaces/debug\",\n      \"marketplaceSource\": {\n        \"sourceType\": \"git\",\n        \"source\": \"https://example.com/acme/agent-skills.git\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just test -p codex-cli marketplace_list`\n- `just test -p codex-cli`","tree":{"sha":"53deed422596b979dce09880d92d8642ed7b581e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/53deed422596b979dce09880d92d8642ed7b581e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJwwDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXHAQAGmEKpJztTJhsGOAH1V9kD2y\n6O3WXuShmEWTo0kGk8KgoHDmSvFW+NF/gne4Pbc8QTBpGXPhmIjqtkT5Fb+79XqO\n+TS3BasMR7LwxkmJzlG/L6EKs1tsLUwDS9kzb61HwR9sdj4MMtrU8/cJ75QEGBqf\n7PTM5EraZHxwYqOzEz8984ewMcyft9KB0/vdALCKF3exW4+bHra2qAVyNkugbp3G\n6HAuYok+tFgvwTnTFYck8gAy9oVVUfgw+IKEDCCQttaAViLlR1YA7r/bOt5hYx9k\nRE7peZOaS4vapW8R+wqMzPTgmix5j2fL2awpG6X5/h2b3Kk7xKCZyChYY4t1hF5W\nlnUm+tI6f129cx5AjCsO7whzaxTAmsGlVtXTuNAG4upNOKrD8vUN9r51JrRDyqZU\ntB7SMfH/2XmCOUTLTqPf6h3pcfm7S5McGyblv8VFGQkbyLDDGH3OGDsLqabSI05q\njgiKvP329EBHiVKNlC29+endQt1DLnMO6uP3r6Ac+l//GDIHzj9k2jsj3ApKkdg2\n2BPw1cCAmKfWdMz3jtuS1OvtYwdLBSlbykDm+4QhZ39FcFOJIeHSmyXy0ls2jdMv\ngR4bMt2c9muTExsuPlXjPPyCxULvdpnvkAhma6btPNcHA54lgZO/TZKMouthNttv\niflz4PEqbddhNbLhRaim\n=AVwn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 53deed422596b979dce09880d92d8642ed7b581e\nparent 6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c\nauthor mpc-oai <mpc@openai.com> 1780943875 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780943875 -0500\n\n[plugins] Expose marketplace source in marketplace list JSON (#27009)\n\n## Summary\n- Follow-up to #26417 and #26631\n- Add `marketplaceSource` to `codex plugin marketplace list --json`\nentries for configured marketplaces\n- Reuse the existing `marketplaceSource` shape from `codex plugin list\n--json`\n- Keep human-readable marketplace list output unchanged\n- Add CLI coverage for configured local and git marketplace sources\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"marketplaces\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"debug\",\n      \"root\": \"/path/to/.codex/.tmp/marketplaces/debug\",\n      \"marketplaceSource\": {\n        \"sourceType\": \"git\",\n        \"source\": \"https://example.com/acme/agent-skills.git\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just test -p codex-cli marketplace_list`\n- `just test -p codex-cli`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T18:37:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0aa9931aeadd9cbb1d6d02f854d1402f8db2bec8/comments","author":{"login":"mpc-oai","id":278119679,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJPE_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278119679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/mpc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c"}]},{"sha":"6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkOGUxMmFjNDI1MDhjMTBiYmUxZDE3NjlhZWU3ZjQ5ZDE1MGJhNWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"stefanstokic-oai","email":"stefanstokic@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:16:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T18:16:32Z"},"message":"[codex] Speed up external agent session imports (#26637)\n\n## Why\n\nImporting large external-agent session histories currently starts a full\nlive Codex thread for every imported session. This initializes unrelated\nruntime systems and repeats expensive transcript, metadata, hashing, and\nledger work.\n\nOn a 50-session, 238 MiB fixture, the existing path took roughly 70\nseconds to complete the import and 77 seconds end to end.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Persist imported sessions directly through `ThreadStore` instead of\nstarting full live threads.\n- Process imports through a bounded five-session pipeline.\n- Parse, extract, and hash each source file in one pass.\n- Move blocking source preparation onto the blocking thread pool.\n- Reuse prepared content hashes and update the import ledger once per\nbatch.\n- Avoid metadata readback for newly written rollouts.\n- Preserve imported conversation history and visible thread metadata.\n- Keep the implementation out of `codex-core` and avoid changes to the\npublic `ThreadStore` trait.\n\n## Performance\n\nFor the same 50-session, 238 MiB fixture:\n\n| Path | Import completion | End to end |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Existing import | 69.61s | 76.62s |\n| This change | 5.95s | 6.58s |\n\nAll 50 sessions imported successfully with no warnings or contention\nsignals.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-external-agent-sessions`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server external_agent_config_import`\n- Verified imports do not initialize unrelated required MCP servers.\n- Verified previously imported source versions are skipped and changed\nsources can be imported again.\n- Verified imported rollouts remain readable through thread listing and\nhistory APIs.","tree":{"sha":"1b44e25eb3237ccb52c4e6af0c6a62168c9530d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1b44e25eb3237ccb52c4e6af0c6a62168c9530d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJwcACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmRwQAFxeBIyV/PnEUXax5Edaug0+\nEwuGIbIFkqDD8fslYaMXnjHCIZhmLiqvSWnLng7zCH4aI+sLe+PB+MoWs/9ekNJh\ncFTtpccX0MMG3lfSkSuW+7vdUnIPf5taU29MAunxtm8WwOOvP3sdvyCEgzYCxDVK\nCaD4hth+JWcApmSAYiNDqzSODGV3pR9wdWyOVI2WIa/ytv+AKro9i1rhuOE980Z/\nf0p+m2clUHn49NXsHeWU+PstkBIT2c8MNwAhof215YJxgSMIZ2qkYKVnaYGyE0Iv\n6QQffywEMtb8d3OnG56udZXrBN0vkGOzCIVxZfjNMa8bVDC1W6w4hFnby3oFGnji\n5AJn0Is1ZD5xjq0g9r6jF13/bKaqnrP6mQ+zAIZ3YPbcBqRIWKXIYCAoJ/jnliup\nPKx/addjuMPLiW+Wfh9EMKh7LL48o6GpQqNTKkf8rqfJ1QYINgvIrOrs+fznaymu\nVPIvVJ5GKDtQjkcXbndIRrP84Du8n7m94nM+1GucY9CZFOSSJ216AEBbx38E6cbj\nqNkGmcrM/p6Sx5vwj1sQ1RCGBixIh9oaWdb0BWDTSOm1gWzhy9LjTsaPHJkWL2v+\nzchN1M6iM9+BEdwDhLDlsLwq6uCU7dXYr08q/zwSCGyAsLOkQlG8aQk9+CIzEw3U\nad1s5FoAZKhgQE35R6lw\n=KabN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1b44e25eb3237ccb52c4e6af0c6a62168c9530d7\nparent f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705\nauthor stefanstokic-oai <stefanstokic@openai.com> 1780942592 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780942592 -0400\n\n[codex] Speed up external agent session imports (#26637)\n\n## Why\n\nImporting large external-agent session histories currently starts a full\nlive Codex thread for every imported session. This initializes unrelated\nruntime systems and repeats expensive transcript, metadata, hashing, and\nledger work.\n\nOn a 50-session, 238 MiB fixture, the existing path took roughly 70\nseconds to complete the import and 77 seconds end to end.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Persist imported sessions directly through `ThreadStore` instead of\nstarting full live threads.\n- Process imports through a bounded five-session pipeline.\n- Parse, extract, and hash each source file in one pass.\n- Move blocking source preparation onto the blocking thread pool.\n- Reuse prepared content hashes and update the import ledger once per\nbatch.\n- Avoid metadata readback for newly written rollouts.\n- Preserve imported conversation history and visible thread metadata.\n- Keep the implementation out of `codex-core` and avoid changes to the\npublic `ThreadStore` trait.\n\n## Performance\n\nFor the same 50-session, 238 MiB fixture:\n\n| Path | Import completion | End to end |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Existing import | 69.61s | 76.62s |\n| This change | 5.95s | 6.58s |\n\nAll 50 sessions imported successfully with no warnings or contention\nsignals.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-external-agent-sessions`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server external_agent_config_import`\n- Verified imports do not initialize unrelated required MCP servers.\n- Verified previously imported source versions are skipped and changed\nsources can be imported again.\n- Verified imported rollouts remain readable through thread listing and\nhistory APIs.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T18:16:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d8e12ac42508c10bbe1d1769aee7f49d150ba5c/comments","author":{"login":"stefanstokic-oai","id":278208182,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJUetg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278208182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanstokic-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705"}]},{"sha":"f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYxYzE4ZGY5YWVhY2IxMGJiODhmNTZmZjY3MjViZTI1Mjc5MWM3MDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:52:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:52:31Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] report compaction analytics details (#26680)\n\n## Why\n\nCompaction analytics adds retained image count and compaction summary\noutput tokens for v1.5 specifically.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add nullable `retained_image_count` and `compaction_summary_tokens`\nfields to `codex_compaction_event`.\n- Populate them only for `responses_compaction_v2`: retained images come\nfrom the retained v2 compacted history, and summary tokens come from\n`response.completed.token_usage.output_tokens`.\n- Leave local and legacy remote compaction events as `null` for these\ndetail fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_v2_compacted_history_counts_retained_input_images`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"16d531c299c075aea54b3614484b400e9ef28fca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/16d531c299c075aea54b3614484b400e9ef28fca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJwFfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+D8QAG8tDkHgyg9HgB2106nrZtyK\nCnQlFQGgKk3/m9HmulBNyUYOMXwAAh9skA4qy0rEe7oF0LKBiv+vepQprFfePxAg\nBvmXKIYlQvrRMLKjSUN3ZnKqlrOaTgRvKk2bDvy79gxwXpT2mq6XUQXiv7SMWHx1\n4R+nRznAwU4ZAHvVZs0H9Ahp1LbStsWNRNJ/tRZ09t1C6xRBmY6VmkXBC2HgiI1Z\n8v0HfPFicbeeviOvna8NchdaG06aovVTEiDRkN6USPbQr/cfz/dDnwNU/7AAdeZy\nBlsDboPHrW+OiZKO4X8+vTqJ0kcf2gkhtdv6jdvnl1n7v1fxoXZ4nmFAwiIBYygj\nxQVK10DubzdSKalv96/ywxV8CMzruCiEgp63+6lcz6WMVUdBFtRRcWvl9ik/QRqr\nDBpLYWTQJVZjT7PPxewuAfYTtwi8wGNp3gdGIcVGZGbBntGD3KaGfV3EHTBW4Htr\nSfZa3iJueIg728EN74kp9pVy1dgoZKdHd3XV9TbCiQ3CiQ9Km8K7akBzmwoxv+fQ\nl67zKJ27GyxJnxSu33/HIbXAN7b+tyE6HWNT+wvu75g/I1+LG66Ykkp0nAltIt6G\nJB9B2N8ssiVy2pmPGODj29+zskbBQjJNeFCbG8wgWooKDC3Dlala9n5SF4/RSQ1/\nTd/2LL6+MWjLqnjwWqc8\n=wbJx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 16d531c299c075aea54b3614484b400e9ef28fca\nparent a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1780941151 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780941151 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] report compaction analytics details (#26680)\n\n## Why\n\nCompaction analytics adds retained image count and compaction summary\noutput tokens for v1.5 specifically.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add nullable `retained_image_count` and `compaction_summary_tokens`\nfields to `codex_compaction_event`.\n- Populate them only for `responses_compaction_v2`: retained images come\nfrom the retained v2 compacted history, and summary tokens come from\n`response.completed.token_usage.output_tokens`.\n- Leave local and legacy remote compaction events as `null` for these\ndetail fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_v2_compacted_history_counts_retained_input_images`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:52:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1c18df9aeacb10bb88f56ff6725be252791c705/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7"}]},{"sha":"a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE4MTUzMTE0NjYwOWEyNTg0N2FlOGQwNDVmMzAyMzRlNmM3ZWFmZDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"ningyi-oai","email":"ningyi@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:49:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:49:59Z"},"message":"Add HTTP window ID to Responses client metadata (#26923)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Keep the existing `x-codex-window-id` HTTP header unchanged.\n- Also send the same window ID in Responses `client_metadata`, allowing\nsupported backend paths to surface it as\n`x-client-meta-x-codex-window-id`.\n- Cover normal HTTP Responses and remote compaction v2 requests without\nchanging window generation or compaction behavior.\n\n## Why\n\nIn the `2026-06-06T23` production hour, all 28,729 HTTP compaction\nrequests had `window_id` in `x-codex-turn-metadata`, but only 73\nretained the direct `x-codex-window-id` header. The request-body\n`client_metadata` path is already used for installation ID and is\npreserved through supported Responses API paths.\n\nThis is additive metadata only. It does not change the direct header,\nrequest count, model input, compaction routing, window generation, or\nuser response behavior.\n\nLegacy `/v1/responses/compact` is intentionally unchanged. Its current\nserver-side `CompressBody` schema does not accept `client_metadata` and\nrejects unknown fields, so supporting that path requires a backend\nschema change before the Codex client can safely send this field.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Current head: `219baef3c`, rebased onto `origin/main` at `26d932983`.\n- The post-rebase diff remains limited to the original five files (`22`\ninsertions, `6` deletions); the legacy experiment remains fully\nreverted.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_stream_includes_subagent_header_on_review`: passed; validates\nnormal HTTP Responses metadata.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_compact_v2_reuses_compaction_trigger_for_followups`: passed;\nvalidates remote compaction v2.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_manual_compact_chatgpt_auth_reuses_service_tier_and_prompt_cache_key`:\npassed; validates that legacy compact keeps its accepted payload shape.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_manual_compact_api_auth_omits_service_tier_and_reuses_prompt_cache_key`:\npassed; validates the legacy API-key payload as well.\n- `just fmt`: passed; an unrelated root `justfile` rewrite produced by\nthe formatter was discarded.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: passed.\n\nThe focused server pytest could not start in the local monorepo\nenvironment because test setup is missing the `dotenv` module. Server\nsource and tests explicitly show that `CompressBody` omits\n`client_metadata` and `/v1/responses/compact` returns HTTP 400 for\nunknown body fields.","tree":{"sha":"1912f6ede621a0441d288a47b5f8685667d28de0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1912f6ede621a0441d288a47b5f8685667d28de0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJwDHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFnEQACDqJbiWwT76UF16h7fW8Seq\nKpna7Z6sLu2d7HH/Z6m0O5An6ga+jr/MyoQgruQJ7tdnA8g8Epq+ITEqJbKUOI7A\nAmbVqLJ9ywxSChtId6vhh+nS76hBf21YhQ7w3cBSJw2g1fMbAn9+hu+UOir/JadT\nzwReMNNXcoreWm88kUWVzfYsd5CnzDiw43gNSU4rR49zdgiswuxs270EvFDn15Zv\n8gBgN0VuiU6X4lcN/PscSAeO/i0EEFbIj/mO8jAT9GXDUluMM530UBWdN5BBqHzD\n1iwYgVV1zJkNozEaZGFvXQLgo212vNr93tTcwkOm7vLQYgdDoCMIz/4s/YZMFlN+\n7vOOzeqbr7d4znjt2aGm16UXKtr5q0YkTK9yagdH1Ss/d2Rz+ZJUHciRhbR6a/IQ\nbSaxCU+8FD4gEvxwDP9s25T367xyLW1Lez5VTg3hz29j+0NZOvtrqDP2IPsxyy6/\neRFSJnSSi9AXepYJdy+ohm9TRZNXWvEfceQ0Fl76IpWnGbG/Xs2ApCFou7Y/tTJh\nf6DQYRUAYnwdwO3od9eVN6qHEgEEb10HJdXyaWF44eNPclXOYVZMEN8HFQMOEwJo\n4uEOUVZs6tfswzpWPtERF8Dwvv+nzioWHHR3IPIAC2DNKU20CgyV3PtYQoOleXZ8\nszRbqnBPbao/196MuUPc\n=LEMy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1912f6ede621a0441d288a47b5f8685667d28de0\nparent b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4\nauthor ningyi-oai <ningyi@openai.com> 1780940999 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780940999 -0700\n\nAdd HTTP window ID to Responses client metadata (#26923)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Keep the existing `x-codex-window-id` HTTP header unchanged.\n- Also send the same window ID in Responses `client_metadata`, allowing\nsupported backend paths to surface it as\n`x-client-meta-x-codex-window-id`.\n- Cover normal HTTP Responses and remote compaction v2 requests without\nchanging window generation or compaction behavior.\n\n## Why\n\nIn the `2026-06-06T23` production hour, all 28,729 HTTP compaction\nrequests had `window_id` in `x-codex-turn-metadata`, but only 73\nretained the direct `x-codex-window-id` header. The request-body\n`client_metadata` path is already used for installation ID and is\npreserved through supported Responses API paths.\n\nThis is additive metadata only. It does not change the direct header,\nrequest count, model input, compaction routing, window generation, or\nuser response behavior.\n\nLegacy `/v1/responses/compact` is intentionally unchanged. Its current\nserver-side `CompressBody` schema does not accept `client_metadata` and\nrejects unknown fields, so supporting that path requires a backend\nschema change before the Codex client can safely send this field.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Current head: `219baef3c`, rebased onto `origin/main` at `26d932983`.\n- The post-rebase diff remains limited to the original five files (`22`\ninsertions, `6` deletions); the legacy experiment remains fully\nreverted.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_stream_includes_subagent_header_on_review`: passed; validates\nnormal HTTP Responses metadata.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_compact_v2_reuses_compaction_trigger_for_followups`: passed;\nvalidates remote compaction v2.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_manual_compact_chatgpt_auth_reuses_service_tier_and_prompt_cache_key`:\npassed; validates that legacy compact keeps its accepted payload shape.\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_manual_compact_api_auth_omits_service_tier_and_reuses_prompt_cache_key`:\npassed; validates the legacy API-key payload as well.\n- `just fmt`: passed; an unrelated root `justfile` rewrite produced by\nthe formatter was discarded.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: passed.\n\nThe focused server pytest could not start in the local monorepo\nenvironment because test setup is missing the `dotenv` module. Server\nsource and tests explicitly show that `CompressBody` omits\n`client_metadata` and `/v1/responses/compact` returns HTTP 400 for\nunknown body fields.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:49:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a81531146609a25847ae8d045f30234e6c7eafd7/comments","author":{"login":"ningyi-oai","id":242065200,"node_id":"U_kgDODm2fMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242065200?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/ningyi-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ningyi-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4"}]},{"sha":"b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIxMjhkYTI3MmU2NDAzNzFjNzU5MTMwMzNiZGNjOTZiY2VhODVlYzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:20:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:20:54Z"},"message":"fix(app-server): avoid blocking connection cleanup (#26852)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote-control app-server sessions can reconnect every 5-7 seconds when\nthe shared transport-event queue fills. The queue's consumer handled\n`ConnectionClosed` by awaiting all in-flight RPCs for the disconnected\nconnection. A stuck RPC therefore blocked processing of replacement\nconnection and initialize events until remote-control forwarding hit its\nfive-second timeout and reconnected again.\n\nRelated issue: N/A (internal remote-control incident investigation).\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Split fast RPC admission closure from draining:\n`ConnectionRpcGate::close()` rejects queued and future RPCs, while\n`shutdown()` continues waiting for RPCs that already started.\n- Close a disconnected connection's RPC gate before spawning the\nexisting RPC drain and resource cleanup in a tracked background task, so\nthe transport-event consumer remains available without waiting for\nactive RPCs.\n- Reap completed cleanup tasks during normal operation, drain them\nduring graceful shutdown, and abort them during forced shutdown.\n- Add regression coverage for closing with an active RPC, rejecting\npost-close requests without polling them, and preserving the existing\nshutdown wait behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\n`just test -p codex-app-server --lib connection_rpc_gate` passes all 6\ntests, including the new close-versus-drain regression coverage.","tree":{"sha":"0c746c1378f1d6d4a518f599bce50cb6369acc17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0c746c1378f1d6d4a518f599bce50cb6369acc17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJvn2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYMEQAExS0oFHB5EDCXaqJ3ilxEo/\npLQDvmK2qu8louUOP6o/6gQpc7sM0hcBY9W7M4BFC/PEEdy4ozLRe80x5Xaj9kNa\nyrvdCidEkaHxG6bsa5/qgs+vE6bGBzvTxMAQk9P8hLIJ4QfhHd3yxRVTVDT2Zc9N\nEcPCvQjJ8bdigjWjLvS92ZbJRMI+D2a34aW1Gejt8EDkfykgor8OgwNw7z9iwK9R\nb5YeUl7UW1zDLUZg0cocMukfr9nBnGGQpvcjvBF5TzSAFFq93Cx0DSaBSrQXb5k6\nJYmphIAdBgGoAK9lws4yLReBK8r1nNKBXuoEpvgYCQlI0bmcaHwBzG2eyHKCuxBo\nBSg2REgtt+osOEEG436GHkW5qRP+3cU4TV7o36qpg7rh4wOhsTuitkAmYckHwjBD\nfgxIioPvBc6QfU2G+96OwBEp1oNb4Gwnfbp907mT1Ifl+4YC0/mln+EurUi42lYV\nIgl4sYe2nhe+BBBnUEVXGwltRjNCfr4pHtAs9c9bH28J7NbWb/A3cW5Pg5l1ATo/\niL5SVjKQEd6PKTXfi+ivQ8RCppF1Jfq6blo3qX+PNR0cz61qesenmtU9PXBLhjoC\nDUv3+SPGe9HxcHYYbMXkqLJ7XySzgquz9X4rYkRU7VQjWKdAXptpb9z5tTKt4aLu\nwWGmj6pnLJqOl1uwXrrB\n=eE8G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0c746c1378f1d6d4a518f599bce50cb6369acc17\nparent 6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1780939254 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780939254 -0700\n\nfix(app-server): avoid blocking connection cleanup (#26852)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote-control app-server sessions can reconnect every 5-7 seconds when\nthe shared transport-event queue fills. The queue's consumer handled\n`ConnectionClosed` by awaiting all in-flight RPCs for the disconnected\nconnection. A stuck RPC therefore blocked processing of replacement\nconnection and initialize events until remote-control forwarding hit its\nfive-second timeout and reconnected again.\n\nRelated issue: N/A (internal remote-control incident investigation).\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Split fast RPC admission closure from draining:\n`ConnectionRpcGate::close()` rejects queued and future RPCs, while\n`shutdown()` continues waiting for RPCs that already started.\n- Close a disconnected connection's RPC gate before spawning the\nexisting RPC drain and resource cleanup in a tracked background task, so\nthe transport-event consumer remains available without waiting for\nactive RPCs.\n- Reap completed cleanup tasks during normal operation, drain them\nduring graceful shutdown, and abort them during forced shutdown.\n- Add regression coverage for closing with an active RPC, rejecting\npost-close requests without polling them, and preserving the existing\nshutdown wait behavior.\n\n## Verification\n\n`just test -p codex-app-server --lib connection_rpc_gate` passes all 6\ntests, including the new close-versus-drain regression coverage.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:20:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b128da272e640371c75913033bdcc96bcea85ec4/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8"}]},{"sha":"6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZkMGUzMTNlMjM3YjZjMWRkMDU1ZmM5YjFkNzQ2OTk2MWU4YzAyZjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:16:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T17:16:36Z"},"message":"[codex] Restore release symbol artifacts with line tables (#26202)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Restore separate release symbol archives for macOS, Linux, and Windows\nbinaries.\n- Build release binaries with `line-tables-only` debuginfo instead of\nfull debuginfo.\n- Strip Unix distribution binaries after extracting symbols, preserve\nWindows PDBs, and keep symbol archives available to the release job.\n- Strip the packaged Linux `bwrap` binary before hashing it so the\nembedded digest matches the distributed bytes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe first symbol-artifact implementation enabled\n`CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=full`. In the June 2 release runs, macOS\nARM primary builds reached the 90-minute timeout while still inside\n`Cargo build`. After the symbol changes were reverted, the same primary\nbuild completed in about 22 minutes. The archive step itself completed\nin tens of seconds when reached.\n\nRust's `line-tables-only` debuginfo level preserves function names and\nsource locations for symbolication without emitting the heavier variable\nand type information from full debuginfo.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just fmt` from `codex-rs`.\n- Ran `just test-github-scripts` from the repository root: 23 tests\npassed.\n- Ran `bash -n` and `shellcheck` on\n`.github/scripts/archive-release-symbols-and-strip-binaries.sh`.\n- Parsed both modified workflows as YAML and ran `git diff --check`.\n- Built a macOS release smoke binary with `line-tables-only`, archived\nits dSYM through the restored script, stripped the production binary,\nand verified that `atos` resolves `symbol_smoke_function` to\n`main.rs:2`.\n- Ran Linux archive-script control-flow coverage with stubbed `objcopy`\nand `strip` commands.\n- Ran Windows PDB archive staging coverage and verified\nunderscore-emitted Rust PDB names are staged under shipped hyphenated\nbinary names.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe release workflow only runs for tags or manual dispatches, so CI\ncannot dry-run the full release matrix on this PR. The next release run\nwill verify runner time and memory behavior under `line-tables-only`.","tree":{"sha":"20dfff2a73be39c2fabd8413e45fae364db28b80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/20dfff2a73be39c2fabd8413e45fae364db28b80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJvj0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV3QQAJL4LadTT8edwmS4aLtSrlvE\nSsOVmopkYhAKd+ZJ1O4quW+nc6SZki8u8Q2idsk5PjeO62qJr6iGHawKYQP1vDgQ\n6KG4OodoH3c0c2/UdvLgX/FyaIaLE2Rd0NOduGFVd9wV3CNMqQ4r/8xVk1qmld6q\nwLWtj15Hy/gdkikyRRKj0Ddw9zcKNvuYo08ZkoxFn6qZk+hGugtxQD7MLaF483CA\ndFQSGOmvoL4jTkYgkT8BdVUnj1ui/oqP7EbBNyLLvdF76Dn+wmteUZ54Nge2z28E\n0YMK2y5A7DpWCEsNXtxXejT9N1Fhu0akYOW12ksGJNQhE3D3jwYSi/X0mcIOstnb\nJsZEG9UkdKStq6NL6aE6+UjQcesKfni8zXHwxn34zsbCNIKQbavoeBtfYIzzD/I4\nTIYpztuLsm9Qo4RX9XwGE5VpHyh4p9IBIzBUuSwZURVBYJcSuYOCmRkue8fdLNN7\nH6Hx7QYvOvHkduDsCDiacuhpbpC5YZtv3HcLNCHWswQjC70g+46TvUzRCHw4nijs\nlMlor3Nf3eaiMwAmaKD06wB/nzr6DynSsvvpppf7YGctzKPqNYG7KbZ8nm3SxUg0\ncfj79wqSFNVImWV62RTvsAmYSFikS7lI9Ex1TqwSi1Qs85Mw9oFfKBlSForLm6Tt\ndw68UXrGmy+R/doO//cY\n=0DxR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 20dfff2a73be39c2fabd8413e45fae364db28b80\nparent 26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c\nauthor Jeremy Rose <172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780938996 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780938996 +0000\n\n[codex] Restore release symbol artifacts with line tables (#26202)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Restore separate release symbol archives for macOS, Linux, and Windows\nbinaries.\n- Build release binaries with `line-tables-only` debuginfo instead of\nfull debuginfo.\n- Strip Unix distribution binaries after extracting symbols, preserve\nWindows PDBs, and keep symbol archives available to the release job.\n- Strip the packaged Linux `bwrap` binary before hashing it so the\nembedded digest matches the distributed bytes.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe first symbol-artifact implementation enabled\n`CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=full`. In the June 2 release runs, macOS\nARM primary builds reached the 90-minute timeout while still inside\n`Cargo build`. After the symbol changes were reverted, the same primary\nbuild completed in about 22 minutes. The archive step itself completed\nin tens of seconds when reached.\n\nRust's `line-tables-only` debuginfo level preserves function names and\nsource locations for symbolication without emitting the heavier variable\nand type information from full debuginfo.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just fmt` from `codex-rs`.\n- Ran `just test-github-scripts` from the repository root: 23 tests\npassed.\n- Ran `bash -n` and `shellcheck` on\n`.github/scripts/archive-release-symbols-and-strip-binaries.sh`.\n- Parsed both modified workflows as YAML and ran `git diff --check`.\n- Built a macOS release smoke binary with `line-tables-only`, archived\nits dSYM through the restored script, stripped the production binary,\nand verified that `atos` resolves `symbol_smoke_function` to\n`main.rs:2`.\n- Ran Linux archive-script control-flow coverage with stubbed `objcopy`\nand `strip` commands.\n- Ran Windows PDB archive staging coverage and verified\nunderscore-emitted Rust PDB names are staged under shipped hyphenated\nbinary names.\n\n## Follow-up\n\nThe release workflow only runs for tags or manual dispatches, so CI\ncannot dry-run the full release matrix on this PR. The next release run\nwill verify runner time and memory behavior under `line-tables-only`.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T17:16:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6d0e313e237b6c1dd055fc9b1d7469961e8c02f8/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c"}]},{"sha":"26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI2ZDkzMjk4MzM5ODE0N2U0NDQzYmQ2NTVjZTI0YTZjZTY4MzNhMWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T16:53:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T16:53:04Z"},"message":"[codex] Exclude external tool output from memories (#26821)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add contains_external_context() to tool output so other tools can be\nopted out of influencing memory when disable_on_external_context=true\n- Classify standalone web-search output as external context (to match\nbehavior as hosted web search)\n- Verify with integration test","tree":{"sha":"805d18997bc27eadeba7b5f2beb4a42a2985a4b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/805d18997bc27eadeba7b5f2beb4a42a2985a4b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJvNwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKvIQACXbP0pMdTsv+Hp12kbjZnSx\nRw1Vw6RNSm2YNEtGzEUuE6KinunJF708qepX87wvaM4Rx3lsQe/tbwhpSFSLVnJf\npA+wniSuljicyRw9FzIdsXB5PL6FArZCGbpYeslY90mKyNYiHh/go/V94pwwkSmB\nhxl4xsV2uDTUtCyptyclMc95r+/G6Y4UEDW0MH4tYSRPT0qAH5LB0ZEZSs6IGjZC\nCl2LgpUVr7y0ALwOWtCUFBzlcbEBcbcmUhxE9jobAE/GR7lr5Rd1jg3VzakVmbah\nHbzJ9/NeHGxWHNn+dT+qUgdx3NU1R4QuP+9M1vuIOSNfyCWE4XvonAH3cGtIEN5I\nThnaZx20DERKRDHT1ZZlhPg1U8Rk91SOD5E25Gdi+Vn4XZBlq37m7prYcxOl+myi\nEIJAv1f0/X0qY+geY23XEsmMLNWEezl435WraTtmjRz7DECEWd7QELauGn/mqCT2\n1We9g1zKtYorcsAe6AnTRgX4rnNyabqo7l6D/gPRG56VLmxlLP9yjg9n0hk5bJen\ni0pCQYj+wsNBjWzyd8JDK/r91hsqYANNPY9oeQpMcXx1IRwj8Kr+dk6ChbW+m2bH\nSxLeAOwUmmDGsP0qrDlz95FVLfXsyRlkr5zUdXNgOlFqCYfcxqsXJnzBvQfJnMg9\nAzV9jARAPwudZ3VYfOsm\n=wMeQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 805d18997bc27eadeba7b5f2beb4a42a2985a4b1\nparent 0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1780937584 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780937584 +0000\n\n[codex] Exclude external tool output from memories (#26821)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add contains_external_context() to tool output so other tools can be\nopted out of influencing memory when disable_on_external_context=true\n- Classify standalone web-search output as external context (to match\nbehavior as hosted web search)\n- Verify with integration test","verified_at":"2026-06-08T16:53:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/26d932983398147e4443bd655ce24a6ce6833a1c/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290"}]},{"sha":"0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA1MjZjYjU2YWMzNTAxYTAyOTY4MDEwZDAzODczOTkzYzMxOWUyOTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T14:44:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T14:44:50Z"},"message":"Avoid reopening v2 descendants on resume (#26997)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 residency is intended to keep only the threads that need\nto be live. The existing rollout resume path still walked persisted open\ndescendants and reopened the entire descendant tree when resuming a v2\nroot, which turns resume into an eager reload of work that should stay\nunloaded until it is explicitly needed.\n\nThe interrupted-agent path has a related residency issue. Interrupted\nagents remain open by design, so an idle interrupted resident should be\neligible for eviction just like an idle completed or errored resident.\nOtherwise a resident set full of interrupted agents can consume every v2\nslot and block later spawns or reloads with `AgentLimitReached`.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Return early from `resume_agent_from_rollout` after resuming a v2\nthread so persisted v2 descendants are not reopened eagerly.\n- Treat idle `Interrupted` v2 residents as unloadable in the LRU\nresidency path.\n- Add focused coverage for v2 root resume leaving descendants unloaded\nand for eviction of an idle interrupted v2 resident when a new slot is\nneeded.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded targeted `codex-core` tests covering:\n\n- v2 root resume with persisted descendants, verifying only the root is\nloaded after resume.\n- residency eviction of an idle interrupted v2 agent when the resident\nset is full.","tree":{"sha":"f16ea7c766aed8275569492d7238fb99836d21e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f16ea7c766aed8275569492d7238fb99836d21e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJtViCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsKgQAFBf+QdLD98raEWRZZMAirJ4\nCFSUwLSGPQpzJkEWbbV0R0AgIAlx2pebZx+Bix3uOqB/RT1V93BGIFSODALAoNr0\nkdCdXQT8EJZfpzLIyiwZkA4fzEunZnEdvDyZs0Pt0Gja8awNlOgO8vuXK3MuIuMB\nihrNWbU7GA76kPa5a142hG7Re2yVN4J09AhZtZT9t0G16zjqkjMKfGU4lWv/U9YN\nYmAZghPCV0tdHtKB+gGKPHFJDohNfE0jFXVEFrLhg/Q+1Cc7jTUon5VKej01DPLj\nXjnCUNeT1AEs1yUbitOvW1nlEr11gWltk5APBiUYe6TxatYSWLfSmYcXq0RGhTzc\n65YbvAkDH77RmJ6rEykZfQ0l4WgyftMeiF4b4Ga3iUOxYxGPRUF39DYBTgKSfTb7\nlpwK6xff1kJDUWOBnfB38VXicghSd1jfsUk4ftaZIQMQ2zFiUJOuFmAEA/L9W+2k\nQIAEpPP+3NMizZQQmWEnfuZu1CS9N9y9jSQDnnL1FskOApe/fPYQvzT6Sql+is0E\na/ImxnyL7gCBAJdTDQdu00UE8jIylLHNOBULfmvlAwl5AmKLfgny0Pmy5O5wverF\nWBuJC7yVW+MEx73DaWEcjnJfpWhGjNDyF8rwzKRihe5GNIjJoahLUz22PsMQ62tf\nFCKMGoWoF21MNYBeAPro\n=VOgv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f16ea7c766aed8275569492d7238fb99836d21e0\nparent 8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780929890 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780929890 +0200\n\nAvoid reopening v2 descendants on resume (#26997)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 residency is intended to keep only the threads that need\nto be live. The existing rollout resume path still walked persisted open\ndescendants and reopened the entire descendant tree when resuming a v2\nroot, which turns resume into an eager reload of work that should stay\nunloaded until it is explicitly needed.\n\nThe interrupted-agent path has a related residency issue. Interrupted\nagents remain open by design, so an idle interrupted resident should be\neligible for eviction just like an idle completed or errored resident.\nOtherwise a resident set full of interrupted agents can consume every v2\nslot and block later spawns or reloads with `AgentLimitReached`.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Return early from `resume_agent_from_rollout` after resuming a v2\nthread so persisted v2 descendants are not reopened eagerly.\n- Treat idle `Interrupted` v2 residents as unloadable in the LRU\nresidency path.\n- Add focused coverage for v2 root resume leaving descendants unloaded\nand for eviction of an idle interrupted v2 resident when a new slot is\nneeded.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded targeted `codex-core` tests covering:\n\n- v2 root resume with persisted descendants, verifying only the root is\nloaded after resume.\n- residency eviction of an idle interrupted v2 agent when the resident\nset is full.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T14:44:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0526cb56ac3501a02968010d03873993c319e290/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453"}]},{"sha":"8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhkNDE1MDUwZmNlNGI0ZWJjNmRhMWJhMjQ3Mzc5ODQ0MjM1ZmE0NTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T12:46:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T12:46:35Z"},"message":"Rename multi-agent v2 close_agent to interrupt_agent (#26994)\n\n## Why\n\n`close_agent` is the wrong model-facing name for the v2 operation after\nthe residency changes. V2 agents remain reusable by task name, and\nresidency/unloading owns capacity management; the exposed tool should\ndescribe the action it actually performs: interrupt the target agent's\ncurrent turn without making the agent unavailable for future messages or\nfollow-up tasks.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Rename the multi-agent v2 tool from `close_agent` to\n`interrupt_agent`.\n- Keep the v1 `close_agent` surface unchanged.\n- Update the v2 handler to send `Op::Interrupt`, keep interrupted agents\nregistered, and reject root/self targets with interrupt-specific errors.\n- Route interrupt delivery through the existing dead-thread cleanup path\nso stale resident entries do not keep consuming capacity.\n- Update tool planning and handler tests for the new v2 surface and\nsemantics.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded focused coverage in:\n\n- `core/src/tools/spec_plan_tests.rs`\n- `core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_tests.rs`","tree":{"sha":"ed8b98e9d0cfd24b53cf2655f4740631fc2f8ac1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ed8b98e9d0cfd24b53cf2655f4740631fc2f8ac1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJrmrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAShYQAKlbOHRgB/aQHkiYWQA9UAVb\np1w962GGcx09Q3f1WLvjMUF+Yr/QdddZidT0j7xfowJF9jm31B8eoMXMJhOhkfsD\nHgujBKHcy7jsJJdpSjbOkoHKmHCNsW5RLJUvU3BjPnaGHo8JW/ytJA2K0OUEneFD\nXCledTsmJgvnnelRx1Prs75m1oupl7NYApdoiibcGNS34rdF00kNK1SA8n4fx8rF\n/xwVSmfBZYl3GKr9pz4loZeCRpBrdUbGje8qOMx9233QOXwBgaxZyUqR3RzXjBp8\nERpZpDrnXFAnBzujyZfc68eQiryLD5Q3VTbXxzqtrPIkHkFUCU7jf5pju2fT9+Dw\nkwK+3DKH2RPzqexGIZ48lmYsMR+mqxyZO9MXMI/BsIhJzrTlTZLrb3rsAo06MupN\nkEORqKQ88VcT7nSlvgdRhHLQTJa77XMnAi7Urm+OMZrdEpNejvzgkJg4eO9fLKVZ\nBGxZEaJ5Hhn/Y98AMyZHtBRnMb6qO06noxJ7O4grVZlHwGCpqFxP/fjbNz7y9uCU\nEKYzgo1l+o9bb7Wg5GYv/2OSjNXQ/k/IlsByGHO3IDioBI4wvOt+Q/PF2Id1bzCo\n4c9x2HAvYmbdsXkZ5I/Bm7XvQ2j3wCgcml/rtcXNQmd+yOPv1qJlA4G0NnM1WqmY\nLc3E+MkNo2j/isUdE2HX\n=udwi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ed8b98e9d0cfd24b53cf2655f4740631fc2f8ac1\nparent 743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780922795 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780922795 +0200\n\nRename multi-agent v2 close_agent to interrupt_agent (#26994)\n\n## Why\n\n`close_agent` is the wrong model-facing name for the v2 operation after\nthe residency changes. V2 agents remain reusable by task name, and\nresidency/unloading owns capacity management; the exposed tool should\ndescribe the action it actually performs: interrupt the target agent's\ncurrent turn without making the agent unavailable for future messages or\nfollow-up tasks.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Rename the multi-agent v2 tool from `close_agent` to\n`interrupt_agent`.\n- Keep the v1 `close_agent` surface unchanged.\n- Update the v2 handler to send `Op::Interrupt`, keep interrupted agents\nregistered, and reject root/self targets with interrupt-specific errors.\n- Route interrupt delivery through the existing dead-thread cleanup path\nso stale resident entries do not keep consuming capacity.\n- Update tool planning and handler tests for the new v2 surface and\nsemantics.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded focused coverage in:\n\n- `core/src/tools/spec_plan_tests.rs`\n- `core/src/tools/handlers/multi_agents_tests.rs`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T12:46:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d415050fce4b4ebc6da1ba247379844235fa453/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a"}]},{"sha":"743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc0M2Y1YWFkMzhhY2NkNTJkYTM0YmY0ZGNiZGQxMjE1YThjM2FiOWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T12:21:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T12:21:28Z"},"message":"feat: count V2 concurrency by active execution (#26969)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-Agent V2 concurrency should count active non-root turns, not\nresident or durable agent threads. The limit is intentionally best\neffort: admission checks are synchronous, but concurrent successful\nchecks may overshoot slightly.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep one root-derived execution limit on the shared `AgentControl`.\n- Count active V2 subagent turns with an RAII guard owned by\n`RunningTask`.\n- Check capacity before spawning or starting an idle agent, including\ndirect app-server `turn/start` submissions.\n- Preserve queued delivery for agents that are already running.\n- Exempt automatic idle continuations so `/goal` work is not dropped\nwhen capacity is temporarily full.\n- Keep root and V1 turns outside this limiter.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n- `execution_guards_count_active_v2_subagent_turns`\n- `execution_guards_ignore_root_and_v1_turns`\n- `v2_nested_spawn_checks_shared_active_execution_capacity`","tree":{"sha":"74762edfa9a928dcf3eae04180731e6938ccc16d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/74762edfa9a928dcf3eae04180731e6938ccc16d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJrPICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/aIQAKtlCbZZhRd2Bpm1dS9BFPWK\nK3QJOVQnznsoXnq/QUOOx0sa4Ua9SOKJsnnJvFjWoKckT3DnwSjiw1NI1q6C9n7a\nW0E3rXVPA5lMYiYzTIddJ7LcSveAAI/y+tSaLmeyEIsQjaJAn/hcHLNoJvcscNuY\nJuObo+P3DKIqH+5AohKE9JRM7X8O1vCFISBZRGbYSEzwrDfofMFSVb+GosOtRv0Q\nASTU3Hw8Ofl4jEE786xyoXTcjEU0hX0H/0v9m2kvf6TKgWaFcR7vcW1xhf9ks/Pl\nmIO8IPkd+PaSabm0qgvuZYdjD+5g+QbOZlbzkh/cHL3ZUeGvd+Bz/uhSKexZeslL\naimEiPZiV1hDLFOHmNCzamhCYTMdh03gVFNKhlShuvVdDahNwyYlN7SMg/No+vyn\nkCOk5XmA6fRRY9Jn8wIyzE8AyKT/CuU+Zl2zie2mbZRC6hQ5pwFjCO2/tXNCRaks\n59G68sa4fGwViha1JYR3vzsf3hg7UbssMNsMDDuvz2R9zpPMnPPHDd3SkylniJbE\nVGg4SC/gWGD9nDoNtPZmsu7sT/qUJq6USQEi45C0Jrz0EUSY+HQboXc8DX7Xqx+x\n7ncbzveGS3vFBNlre7fy/wGKZLsR7bQyWCeBUjrrlWM8u0+cpoNNC8ihcujeZk6n\nFNSHegG2e/MxGGRitlpU\n=RlW0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 74762edfa9a928dcf3eae04180731e6938ccc16d\nparent 8f1aad58dc3a684afecdd9efd31d074762da3c24\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780921288 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780921288 +0200\n\nfeat: count V2 concurrency by active execution (#26969)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-Agent V2 concurrency should count active non-root turns, not\nresident or durable agent threads. The limit is intentionally best\neffort: admission checks are synchronous, but concurrent successful\nchecks may overshoot slightly.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep one root-derived execution limit on the shared `AgentControl`.\n- Count active V2 subagent turns with an RAII guard owned by\n`RunningTask`.\n- Check capacity before spawning or starting an idle agent, including\ndirect app-server `turn/start` submissions.\n- Preserve queued delivery for agents that are already running.\n- Exempt automatic idle continuations so `/goal` work is not dropped\nwhen capacity is temporarily full.\n- Keep root and V1 turns outside this limiter.\n\n## Test coverage\n\n- `execution_guards_count_active_v2_subagent_turns`\n- `execution_guards_ignore_root_and_v1_turns`\n- `v2_nested_spawn_checks_shared_active_execution_capacity`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T12:21:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/743f5aad38accd52da34bf4dcbdd1215a8c3ab9a/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f1aad58dc3a684afecdd9efd31d074762da3c24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f1aad58dc3a684afecdd9efd31d074762da3c24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f1aad58dc3a684afecdd9efd31d074762da3c24"}]},{"sha":"8f1aad58dc3a684afecdd9efd31d074762da3c24","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhmMWFhZDU4ZGMzYTY4NGFmZWNkZDllZmQzMWQwNzQ3NjJkYTNjMjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T09:39:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T09:39:08Z"},"message":"Ignore proc-macro-error2 advisory (#26974)\n\n## Summary\n- ignore RUSTSEC-2026-0173 in cargo-deny and cargo-audit config\n- document that proc-macro-error2 is pulled in transitively via\ni18n-embed-fl/age/codex-secrets\n- leave the ignore temporary until codex-secrets moves off age or age\ndrops i18n-embed-fl\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- cargo deny check --hide-inclusion-graph","tree":{"sha":"c0273589387579256297d028c0ca8f91bfdaed01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c0273589387579256297d028c0ca8f91bfdaed01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8f1aad58dc3a684afecdd9efd31d074762da3c24","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJo28CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARK0QAGNe6eHyssritI7iUEeM9iGt\n1S2HmFR66y8t8mm3yYSgQOxLI9vuqADSjdkYEVS8wtAG4VwdQo5GyGGdLbAjzIh+\nZ7cclZ2RGTqCqHiLtcC0e9oNTBu2yncTBTPjOyZWZ+