id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba"}]},{"sha":"4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRlODAzYTAxN2M5NThkZDM3ZWIyNTEzNzJiYTgxMDIzMmQzZTg0YmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T08:24:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T08:24:48Z"},"message":"feat: add v2 agent residency lru (#26632)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 treats agents as durable logical agents, not just live\nentries in `ThreadManager`. After the reload-on-delivery change, a v2\nagent can be addressed even if its thread is not currently loaded.\n\nThis PR adds the next layer: loaded v2 subagents can be paged out of\n`ThreadManager` when the session has too many resident agents. That\nkeeps residency separate from logical identity and prepares the stack\nfor making v2 concurrency count active execution instead of existing\nagents.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add an `AgentControl`-scoped LRU for resident v2 subagents.\n- Reserve residency before spawning or reloading a v2 subagent.\n- If resident capacity is full, unload the least-recently-used idle v2\nsubagent from `ThreadManager`.\n- Keep `ThreadManager` as a primitive loaded-thread store; it does not\nown the LRU policy.\n- Keep unloaded agents registered and durable so they can be reloaded by\nthe delivery path.\n- Preserve the existing v2 cap semantics by using the derived non-root\nv2 cap for residency.\n\nEviction is intentionally conservative. A thread is unloadable only when\nit is a v2 subagent, has completed or errored, has no active turn, and\nhas no pending mailbox work. Before removal, the rollout is materialized\nand flushed.\n\n## Assumptions And Non-Goals\n\n- PR #26623 provides the reload-on-delivery path for unloaded v2 agents.\n- `ThreadManager` membership means loaded/resident, not logical agent\nexistence.\n- `AgentRegistry` remains the logical identity/metadata source for v2\nagents that may be unloaded.\n- `list_agents` remains a recent/resident view for now.\n- This does not change active execution concurrency; that is the next\nPR.\n- This does not change `close_agent` semantics.\n- This does not change or remove `resume_agent`.\n- This does not add a new residency config knob.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. V2 durable lookup and reload on delivery (#26623) - reload unloaded\nv2 agents before delivering follow-up/input.\n2. V2 residency LRU (this PR) - unload idle resident v2 agents from\n`ThreadManager` when resident capacity is full.\n3. V2 active-execution concurrency - count running non-root v2 turns\ninstead of logical agents.\n4. V2 close/interrupt semantics - make v2 close interrupt the current\nturn without deleting durable identity.\n5. V2 resume cleanup - remove the manual resume surface for v2 while\nkeeping internal reload support.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added focused coverage for the residency LRU eviction path.\n- Local clippy/check/tests were not run; CI will cover them.","tree":{"sha":"90116c3a6882ff1c0a13b6f066c8ce788566e9be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/90116c3a6882ff1c0a13b6f066c8ce788566e9be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJnxRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK3EQAB3mw6tq+VzMUZpnFsVP7nRu\nysXytsbe42TGEE3xTE84r+AQ9QpOuPR2m837LcDsbRBQX2oUyLpei5/jvLxtIUnt\nytWE1odnFX4+cztQxak6hYhFJDFb/gobkMNww35dnVFaNAOU+kmwwgdA0SNbIACB\nG6g2qQkSTg1MTaS6FcVBtLmWqbX3lSFsLplf6Kn0T23nQ6lQrfVkVqvOobY1zyZA\n+Y9UffPUeLfzkM2VvfYKn6vRs/Uwmlxj/Xyl/8CewcA+tBtO+yBqrFgY1QsOYBVz\nW5JRoiyz6kWm5wsNmO5Q/O5aRicpIYa1cuFdNKAV1QViv55Jg8K0/hOXEstiAUN0\nzDhe+wupMuKH/YXIFJeMRQsFR0qDPhtUgGdan5gwgA2kIzh+TmjWwMSO5X4EfJsO\nIyihrjq7G4nHGSzfMU6G8n9jFN2h5uOfpwFKavINMy7G8FIiFNwCJmu6dHWU9nC1\nOxyxskE1hJpVjhrpg6LAorn9cmwutUgKqkGdbSGzUsd7wlDp0U8HZ9ttYCG5jafh\nEwbRiWLdhEdUxk+lA21D30I6ppXQUnLwHeJnkKcicRp5OMSU8xU33a0uYpWWoA66\n4EUV79E7hzGRZi2+CjW7YSPwtr2fQSGettELtlDQdYwEyWhPoh2N58hBFi+O6tuG\nlEoQ8sC8EBYZZB8i3n8w\n=+XcN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 90116c3a6882ff1c0a13b6f066c8ce788566e9be\nparent ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780907088 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780907088 +0200\n\nfeat: add v2 agent residency lru (#26632)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 treats agents as durable logical agents, not just live\nentries in `ThreadManager`. After the reload-on-delivery change, a v2\nagent can be addressed even if its thread is not currently loaded.\n\nThis PR adds the next layer: loaded v2 subagents can be paged out of\n`ThreadManager` when the session has too many resident agents. That\nkeeps residency separate from logical identity and prepares the stack\nfor making v2 concurrency count active execution instead of existing\nagents.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add an `AgentControl`-scoped LRU for resident v2 subagents.\n- Reserve residency before spawning or reloading a v2 subagent.\n- If resident capacity is full, unload the least-recently-used idle v2\nsubagent from `ThreadManager`.\n- Keep `ThreadManager` as a primitive loaded-thread store; it does not\nown the LRU policy.\n- Keep unloaded agents registered and durable so they can be reloaded by\nthe delivery path.\n- Preserve the existing v2 cap semantics by using the derived non-root\nv2 cap for residency.\n\nEviction is intentionally conservative. A thread is unloadable only when\nit is a v2 subagent, has completed or errored, has no active turn, and\nhas no pending mailbox work. Before removal, the rollout is materialized\nand flushed.\n\n## Assumptions And Non-Goals\n\n- PR #26623 provides the reload-on-delivery path for unloaded v2 agents.\n- `ThreadManager` membership means loaded/resident, not logical agent\nexistence.\n- `AgentRegistry` remains the logical identity/metadata source for v2\nagents that may be unloaded.\n- `list_agents` remains a recent/resident view for now.\n- This does not change active execution concurrency; that is the next\nPR.\n- This does not change `close_agent` semantics.\n- This does not change or remove `resume_agent`.\n- This does not add a new residency config knob.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. V2 durable lookup and reload on delivery (#26623) - reload unloaded\nv2 agents before delivering follow-up/input.\n2. V2 residency LRU (this PR) - unload idle resident v2 agents from\n`ThreadManager` when resident capacity is full.\n3. V2 active-execution concurrency - count running non-root v2 turns\ninstead of logical agents.\n4. V2 close/interrupt semantics - make v2 close interrupt the current\nturn without deleting durable identity.\n5. V2 resume cleanup - remove the manual resume surface for v2 while\nkeeping internal reload support.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added focused coverage for the residency LRU eviction path.\n- Local clippy/check/tests were not run; CI will cover them.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T08:24:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4e803a017c958dd37eb251372ba810232d3e84ba/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb"}]},{"sha":"ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVkNmU1Y2Y5MTlmZGI4YjM4OGViNTY0MzY2OWRjMTc1ZjI2MTg4Y2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T06:18:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T06:18:23Z"},"message":"[codex] Enable standalone web search in code mode (#26719)\n\n## What\n\n- Consume plaintext `output` from standalone search while retaining\noptional `encrypted_output` parsing.\n- Expose `web.run` to code mode and return search output to nested\nJavaScript calls.\n- Cover direct and code-mode standalone search paths with integration\ntests.\n\n## Why\n\n`/v1/alpha/search` now returns plaintext output, which code mode needs\nto consume standalone search results.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-api`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-core code_mode_can_call_standalone_web_search`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_web_search_round_trips_output`","tree":{"sha":"e9d9f82aa196d392e3a1525baf992f189bd63164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e9d9f82aa196d392e3a1525baf992f189bd63164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJl6vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWAgQAIY/PSB3ztGt9S60iTdEm8EW\nWCIDQYWy3zd7OCGw/8ddWnRJKLVOXnXEC17j+oT8TO8TuPYmUBSZvdJ3Yc6B2Y1G\n9XmJEYHrDnMOHRSKFDin/jbLRf0LHHRRBco8uZBIHU4sNh2KtF3F8vtcKMnt8jNd\nI1sH1wG7UMVETOEKDq7UzHvhXGR0hYRFW6VgiExOtz5BjT4UXGuOIiD/0MXjdK+K\nWPU0v9CxN6sjEn48WDNuGMpTLNiEPyn7C89btIYon+KKcuuShO6ex085HOiieyTT\nx2EP0zGxDSYzL9c6RukmiUcDLch8l1XfTUFfJn1srAJacpcCMm8szXNjquua/h7U\n0wvYolDDyv0teN22B3mBYF85DjH+Om03es4dsKTDNlmHBcUNyyk9khIN2CrdHMfK\n1tmbrvebZeQ+jZYz+V7yfgtwNsrj6XkEfRw4u+gq4yRNq+lkFnH515BK/Ju13BNx\nkAyU96ZW93q5XNqHrwmbUCQ+ugskyuc+tQVTKqSzpCms61YMT/JOcBZkkCufKOkX\nm2dEOnmpWY3RjSp7jQ2RCEZv/odk+AqtrqfU/r8+4AC4oTvpS7xpdQYiHxMm6r16\npcWbrGo8Xiv0voq+07IMZtMW4PsC/jnvbSurQeFmuaY0CKaToI/kzH1+IvSuoNeE\nTGiq2ZKeC1kAvD6YPyvY\n=Q1oQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e9d9f82aa196d392e3a1525baf992f189bd63164\nparent 5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1780899503 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780899503 -0700\n\n[codex] Enable standalone web search in code mode (#26719)\n\n## What\n\n- Consume plaintext `output` from standalone search while retaining\noptional `encrypted_output` parsing.\n- Expose `web.run` to code mode and return search output to nested\nJavaScript calls.\n- Cover direct and code-mode standalone search paths with integration\ntests.\n\n## Why\n\n`/v1/alpha/search` now returns plaintext output, which code mode needs\nto consume standalone search results.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-api`\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-core code_mode_can_call_standalone_web_search`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_web_search_round_trips_output`","verified_at":"2026-06-08T06:18:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ed6e5cf919fdb8b388eb5643669dc175f26188cb/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e"}]},{"sha":"5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVhNDQwYzAzZjJmMzM5MzE2OWM1ZGY1MTdkMWZkOGVlZTk2OWU0NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T03:12:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T03:12:05Z"},"message":"fix(tui): scope MCP startup status by thread (#26639)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP startup failures from spawned subagents were rendered as global\nnotifications, so a child thread's failure could pollute the visible\nparent transcript. Routing the notification to the child exposed two\nrelated replay problems: session refresh could discard the buffered\nevent, and a newly created child `ChatWidget` did not know the expected\nMCP server set, which could leave its startup spinner running after\nevery server had settled.\n\nMCP startup diagnostics should remain visible in the thread that owns\nthe startup without affecting other transcripts. The protocol also needs\nto support a future app-scoped MCP lifecycle where startup is not owned\nby any thread.\n\n## Reported Behavior\n\nThe [originating Slack\nreport](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C08JZTV654K/p1780604538859939)\ncalled out that using subagents could turn MCP startup failures into a\nwall of yellow CLI warnings because repeated failures were not\ndeduplicated. The intended behavior is for those diagnostics to remain\nvisible once in the thread that owns the startup, without polluting the\nparent transcript.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- add nullable `threadId` ownership to `mcpServer/startupStatus/updated`\n- populate it from the app-server conversation ID for the current\nthread-scoped lifecycle and regenerate the protocol schema and\nTypeScript artifacts\n- treat a missing or null `threadId` as app-scoped without injecting it\ninto the active chat transcript\n- route and buffer thread-owned MCP startup notifications by thread in\nthe TUI\n- preserve buffered MCP startup events across child session refresh\n- seed expected MCP servers before replaying a thread snapshot so\nstartup reaches its terminal state\n- suppress an identical repeated failure warning for the same server\nwithin one startup round\n\nThe owning thread still renders the detailed failure and final `MCP\nstartup incomplete (...)` summary.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Configure an optional MCP server named `smoke` that exits during\ninitialization.\n2. Launch the TUI with multi-agent support enabled.\n3. Confirm the main thread's own startup failure renders one detailed\n`smoke` warning and one incomplete-startup summary.\n4. Spawn exactly one subagent.\n5. Confirm the parent transcript does not receive the subagent's MCP\nstartup failure.\n6. Switch to the subagent thread and confirm it contains exactly one\ndetailed `smoke` failure and one incomplete-startup summary.\n7. Confirm the subagent's MCP startup spinner disappears and the thread\nremains usable.\n8. Switch between the parent and subagent and confirm the warnings\nneither move nor duplicate.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_start_emits_mcp_server_status_updated_notifications`\n- `just test -p codex-tui mcp_startup`\n\nThe parent/child behavior and spinner completion were also exercised\nmanually in tmux. `just argument-comment-lint` was attempted but blocked\nby an unrelated local Bazel LLVM empty-glob failure; touched Rust\ncallsites were inspected manually.","tree":{"sha":"d28111bca6bd2bf05ae643ddeac923a5dbe4b1ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d28111bca6bd2bf05ae643ddeac923a5dbe4b1ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJjMFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMXYQAJKaYVtLyLic1Okijjfwa7bG\n5z2XwpACy9x2nrPNwq3Fi1drm0MLC39/kPJD4+PYtfdvEfNG7NU7MSdy1JpV1kV5\nEfpawfJ3aaQ1lKGhWEDCHzdy/8poYVFglNZKWEdZd/fwFXtzNXZuEmUJGV9jUDr0\nFUzB3QrI1iS0jzj2GLCqewbLvC7tDNrcYlSCwr1utAI7YY6/TQK1wO9ZCuQOprns\nOkhhhFpt9uAYOM4tvnHh2PUcgQFn/Cao72YYmcfjFlMZ1JfYCbQxLU53fC9tSHOf\n8nZkAPogz5orqRmbwKFY1QiETCXN5eBTDzHG1VhQrIB44ni+oVvwnZpNsqhbnKFr\nOAhyxGDc7I/hmW+0330dbai01Y2fBdpvDe8kygiBosBa+BN5sEkU6rdjav9QNSkn\nGMqhljC+ervXnpiMdFiCmkSXxkQVH28TtcpRqk1wG5UeMrtkfzuIWHAsSodMPPgX\nOJbka32qOffg27epHGTA8oeB5u6pZpEIq6MwVExJchBJd+sgym6PKrAeSI9P7FMe\nGE3d1vYaRkj5r25NfI2Wa1Mda/IQRCyk1BeSZ7oxFsCYtks/7+fL1UG8QXUps2Bc\nLiBHte7ZGH7as8vnSHWjx8sJgogOZMnuwejni1HhoLLk7c6cTyXWQFgMmxFB49rv\nfZGIp7z32jxI8KST7ok6\n=2NSw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d28111bca6bd2bf05ae643ddeac923a5dbe4b1ad\nparent e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780888325 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780888325 -0700\n\nfix(tui): scope MCP startup status by thread (#26639)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP startup failures from spawned subagents were rendered as global\nnotifications, so a child thread's failure could pollute the visible\nparent transcript. Routing the notification to the child exposed two\nrelated replay problems: session refresh could discard the buffered\nevent, and a newly created child `ChatWidget` did not know the expected\nMCP server set, which could leave its startup spinner running after\nevery server had settled.\n\nMCP startup diagnostics should remain visible in the thread that owns\nthe startup without affecting other transcripts. The protocol also needs\nto support a future app-scoped MCP lifecycle where startup is not owned\nby any thread.\n\n## Reported Behavior\n\nThe [originating Slack\nreport](https://openai.slack.com/archives/C08JZTV654K/p1780604538859939)\ncalled out that using subagents could turn MCP startup failures into a\nwall of yellow CLI warnings because repeated failures were not\ndeduplicated. The intended behavior is for those diagnostics to remain\nvisible once in the thread that owns the startup, without polluting the\nparent transcript.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- add nullable `threadId` ownership to `mcpServer/startupStatus/updated`\n- populate it from the app-server conversation ID for the current\nthread-scoped lifecycle and regenerate the protocol schema and\nTypeScript artifacts\n- treat a missing or null `threadId` as app-scoped without injecting it\ninto the active chat transcript\n- route and buffer thread-owned MCP startup notifications by thread in\nthe TUI\n- preserve buffered MCP startup events across child session refresh\n- seed expected MCP servers before replaying a thread snapshot so\nstartup reaches its terminal state\n- suppress an identical repeated failure warning for the same server\nwithin one startup round\n\nThe owning thread still renders the detailed failure and final `MCP\nstartup incomplete (...)` summary.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Configure an optional MCP server named `smoke` that exits during\ninitialization.\n2. Launch the TUI with multi-agent support enabled.\n3. Confirm the main thread's own startup failure renders one detailed\n`smoke` warning and one incomplete-startup summary.\n4. Spawn exactly one subagent.\n5. Confirm the parent transcript does not receive the subagent's MCP\nstartup failure.\n6. Switch to the subagent thread and confirm it contains exactly one\ndetailed `smoke` failure and one incomplete-startup summary.\n7. Confirm the subagent's MCP startup spinner disappears and the thread\nremains usable.\n8. Switch between the parent and subagent and confirm the warnings\nneither move nor duplicate.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_start_emits_mcp_server_status_updated_notifications`\n- `just test -p codex-tui mcp_startup`\n\nThe parent/child behavior and spinner completion were also exercised\nmanually in tmux. `just argument-comment-lint` was attempted but blocked\nby an unrelated local Bazel LLVM empty-glob failure; touched Rust\ncallsites were inspected manually.","verified_at":"2026-06-08T03:12:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5a440c03f2f3393169c5df517d1fd8eee969e45e/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f"}]},{"sha":"e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2NDhlYzc3MWYxZjEzMGU4MjExMGM5YjMwOTMyMzYxZGNlZmU4NWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-08T00:35:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-08T00:35:33Z"},"message":"deps: update starlark to 0.14.2 (#24820)","tree":{"sha":"e0a19b5a4ecee8750fed4e7a40b1eac34ad148e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e0a19b5a4ecee8750fed4e7a40b1eac34ad148e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJg5VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAblQQADJfJ7RQORsTsN1R8xKBGQfZ\nxK5BPj/kTCJs+O0C40YaTYCVxK+zHC/PIUpYG/zR/8QjMnao2SpwIUbVpY1igPrB\nqT8ffxGYMMvlblTbwFrlToJjM9z3HLjCsPqGMG+4qQ1WdWZiug/v7/PrqbVLfFWe\n+aphVbN4NrCwN+lnLYsgBBW0K53glh/U8nYDEVz/j9p8uZ/lO/iLpgc0LFzbzEI/\nfU+UABHI2r1d6BPwKHk2/lTbLtxe0zZTECHaIIQd3g8zkUHnuxBqeYrow933AArs\nIYNkvQOH3sJ8pSZc/BhvuiPJ8ftgtxTjGVTV9v5PZuYUX9EC61fwQg32pnskotGP\nUJDTZYctV6WzC5UiJ6g7x7pzrodpiucD7ZEiMexVVVP3ltFKZLS0PVQdbScVcAQK\njNcUIyNPww9lnHImZiUuA97NlL7/mKW/V5Jcehqew1zA/UVQMifrTtY1jUvsSjqh\ndoKOd7l2swl/X5zXXNl8d/Olu1/nQjXWpEypFi/vuFP7tAPWgSS21Dq/TXhQSn7e\ntJknn/paC17P5vSdii738mJZIyZvr/bWEGLLjpDkJXJ8f2O16L9Slt1oestBzM8U\nU36cH0uEcsMJrQLc0eqYsMZHmC5Dbddszg7OmE9hncSDUEXZtMeRq31xkKRJSVEB\nNtG/yivEqK1zZJG6nbMG\n=+zBu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e0a19b5a4ecee8750fed4e7a40b1eac34ad148e1\nparent e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780878933 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780878933 -0700\n\ndeps: update starlark to 0.14.2 (#24820)","verified_at":"2026-06-08T00:35:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e648ec771f1f130e82110c9b30932361dcefe85f/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897"}]},{"sha":"e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUwOTNkODE5ODI2MTI3YmUwMTM1NGUyODg1Yzg2ZDdmY2JmYjI4OTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-07T21:34:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T21:34:35Z"},"message":"fix(tui): accept prompts with resume and fork (#26818)\n\n## Why\n\nInteractive `codex resume` and `codex fork` expose both a session ID\npositional and an initial prompt positional. With `--last`, Clap still\nassigns the first positional to the session ID, so a command such as\n`codex fork --last \"/compact focus on auth\"` either fails parsing or\nattempts to look up the prompt as a session ID instead of sending it to\nthe latest session.\n\nThis makes it impossible to select the latest session and immediately\nprovide a follow-up prompt, even though `codex exec resume --last`\nalready supports that workflow.\n\n<img width=\"1746\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-06-06 at 17 00\n47@2x\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86885c07-a23c-48ee-b0ee-47f2484f6eb7\"\n/>\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Reinterpret the first positional as the initial prompt when\ninteractive `resume --last` or `fork --last` is used and no explicit\nsecond prompt was parsed.\n- Preserve the existing `resume SESSION_ID PROMPT` and `fork SESSION_ID\nPROMPT` behavior.\n- Add parser-level regression coverage for latest-session and\nexplicit-session prompt forms.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start an interactive session, exit it, then run `codex resume --last\n\"continue from the latest session\"`.\n2. Confirm Codex resumes the latest session and submits the supplied\nprompt instead of treating it as a session ID.\n3. Run `codex fork --last \"take a different approach\"`.\n4. Confirm Codex forks the latest session and submits the supplied\nprompt.\n5. Also verify `codex resume SESSION_ID \"continue here\"` and `codex fork\nSESSION_ID \"branch here\"` still target the explicit session and submit\nthe prompt.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `just test -p codex-cli` (267 passed)","tree":{"sha":"acab792ee7d9c1e7371230836e713a97dcaaaa08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/acab792ee7d9c1e7371230836e713a97dcaaaa08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJePrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnpoQAFzBn3bpuvf4+MIdPgv2ebGP\nWbI7geghJXYBc/umOJyZmDlRX1eVj2n1zaSy0WFvkVEnAjE/8mmproUXyv2ISBSM\n6Eo2Mkkzj8w8iff/z4aXfzbhEe+Y8nzZ7z7mnH3EgO1atk3FzAE3WNcUpA3wS3Sb\nIOEL/v4MJ0ztSYwDVW9SR3ZOc0O7CmOzbSnj5us7rxf3kkUAsGJRAkA9VYDIYjzq\nRt3Vi/1XKy+DrtWvZEqZD9THyZsWaJY6InHtmAW+V4PL+gEVFN/sgi7TZtftceSe\nmF38P9Vg/aH1o5pfkqE2Zm68+wVdRHUPLrcubcW8TDyzuxeqdmLfKwVqNxCoRAQe\n3/fOnZrxSVeyOPb6iY8RHLq/lKM/ALuBrF/rYgbodc6gIESqjMW4KAfOoohhDR1f\nLmpAr/KqbiR3r48+vHUa7ran11C+1VCH9P4KRXW9ldz8oUDTcgR783cGXqXbP5Pm\n81dPsVaejSr7NN3KmXdgil9VqmDQSZKlAokDokbV8cUFPScqZn9FR70W0xXKhhN6\n//vAHrRJdRMh/2Idk0q9SmAyuO3uZAZ1rc6L4akSZrA28dX+hc42DafRNqzuM2WS\ncl38O+WSBmvzxv2G9itV1dhcCv1TMpixiTsz55DlGXD2oITGaGJA4QrJeWqOnByx\nwB+seUqYVuXKMXn5boX0\n=buDq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree acab792ee7d9c1e7371230836e713a97dcaaaa08\nparent e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780868075 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780868075 -0400\n\nfix(tui): accept prompts with resume and fork (#26818)\n\n## Why\n\nInteractive `codex resume` and `codex fork` expose both a session ID\npositional and an initial prompt positional. With `--last`, Clap still\nassigns the first positional to the session ID, so a command such as\n`codex fork --last \"/compact focus on auth\"` either fails parsing or\nattempts to look up the prompt as a session ID instead of sending it to\nthe latest session.\n\nThis makes it impossible to select the latest session and immediately\nprovide a follow-up prompt, even though `codex exec resume --last`\nalready supports that workflow.\n\n<img width=\"1746\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-06-06 at 17 00\n47@2x\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86885c07-a23c-48ee-b0ee-47f2484f6eb7\"\n/>\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Reinterpret the first positional as the initial prompt when\ninteractive `resume --last` or `fork --last` is used and no explicit\nsecond prompt was parsed.\n- Preserve the existing `resume SESSION_ID PROMPT` and `fork SESSION_ID\nPROMPT` behavior.\n- Add parser-level regression coverage for latest-session and\nexplicit-session prompt forms.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start an interactive session, exit it, then run `codex resume --last\n\"continue from the latest session\"`.\n2. Confirm Codex resumes the latest session and submits the supplied\nprompt instead of treating it as a session ID.\n3. Run `codex fork --last \"take a different approach\"`.\n4. Confirm Codex forks the latest session and submits the supplied\nprompt.\n5. Also verify `codex resume SESSION_ID \"continue here\"` and `codex fork\nSESSION_ID \"branch here\"` still target the explicit session and submit\nthe prompt.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `just test -p codex-cli` (267 passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-07T21:34:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e093d819826127be01354e2885c86d7fcbfb2897/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c"}]},{"sha":"e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2YzQ3MDk1N2RlNTM1NzI3MDZhZmQxOWY3ZDhlZmI0Mjk4NTg2NGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-07T18:33:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T18:33:16Z"},"message":"fix: preserve approval sandbox decisions in unified exec (#24981)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR fixes approval sandbox semantics in the unified-exec path. The\nzsh-fork runtime exposed the bug because the shell can do meaningful\nwork before any intercepted child `execv(2)` exists: redirections,\nbuiltins, globbing, and pipeline setup all happen in the launch process.\nIf the model requested `sandbox_permissions=require_escalated`, or an\nexec-policy `allow` rule explicitly bypassed the sandbox, that approved\nsandbox decision needs to be preserved for the launch path and for\nintercepted execs that use the same approval machinery.\n\nThe behavior is not only about zsh fork. The production changes are in\nshared approval/escalation code, so they also affect non-zsh-fork\nintercepted exec paths that go through the same sandbox decision logic.\nThe narrow intent is to preserve the approval decision while still\nkeeping denied-read profiles and bounded additional-permission requests\nsandboxed.\n\n## Production Changes\n\n- `codex-rs/core/src/tools/runtimes/unified_exec.rs`: derives a\n`launch_sandbox_permissions` value from the requested sandbox\npermissions and the runtime filesystem policy, then uses that value for\nmanaged-network/env setup and launch sandbox selection. This keeps full\napproval or policy-bypass decisions visible to the first unified-exec\nattempt, while still preventing a full sandbox override from discarding\ndenied-read restrictions. Direct unified exec keeps the same decision\nsurface; the important difference is that zsh-fork launch setup no\nlonger accidentally loses the approved parent sandbox decision.\n\n- `codex-rs/core/src/tools/runtimes/shell/unix_escalation.rs`: makes\nintercepted-exec escalation selection explicit for the three sandbox\npermission modes. `UseDefault` only escalates when an exec-policy\ndecision allows sandbox bypass, `RequireEscalated` escalates when\nunsandboxed execution is allowed, and `WithAdditionalPermissions`\nescalates through the bounded additional-permissions path instead of\nbeing treated as a full unsandboxed override. Unsandboxed intercepted\nexecs now also rebuild the environment as `RequireEscalated`, which\nstrips managed-network proxy variables consistently with other\nunsandboxed execution.\n\n## Test Coverage\n\nMost of the PR is tests. The new coverage verifies:\n\n- unified exec preserves parent approval and exec-policy sandbox\ndecisions for zsh-fork launch selection;\n- bounded `with_additional_permissions` remains sandboxed and\npermission-profile based;\n- denied-read profiles are not weakened by parent approval;\n- explicit prompt rules still prompt for intercepted execs after the\nparent command is approved;\n- unsandboxed intercepted execs strip managed-network env vars.\n\nNo documentation update is needed; this is an internal approval/sandbox\ncorrectness fix.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/24981).\n* #24982\n* __->__ #24981","tree":{"sha":"e98afa7713f2a48891914e76671a286ef92156dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e98afa7713f2a48891914e76671a286ef92156dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJblsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5UkQAK5rf3iGa4RJQuWKDQ7CkNR+\nhvXWecUE56a9YAZqEbzebmUzFaCsyQByqbU65fklK06w/gd3E1AziYhdIq5LE5ll\nqt8+pXOvNuIOiCGtiFl97HAYt7rbgS0181SPFSW89OWOqcthbtqb7Y30p5DK/G64\njFMJcdGrfU6dTZUl87VzksK9nfikYXaV83SjoG5ux5G5Ww29koUkjdNhnHYKFpzA\nq0xpRY35zfdJpKHpzmXcuqS3vzMZymae1rl8lp7zX8UXavyf9R738KDd1NL6rjBX\n1PR77w77y97YlWh7cPasWzUZtasw8jSwevSU614N8NOiUXbp/iyGUIqe83I81XPO\n+fMD81QLe8nIlhDP1kvZD3C52ollGeHER9qxjmNsQNOUC/LRUmRMplr3Ne/7CnaT\nz8SrXbLgUWi4tkP5+YGpmTra06qYLVwxXKFRIjyvfDS/A3pj2+vmSed0tytxyKQr\nr+b0+FoE6RksJgjvxyNiiQLqhrrYWZeTR5kZNrW1FgjEuYVAGVe7xBHP907q3KDW\nSb1laiIqyW3twcjXkU//x9HTQoqGbxVLN4KCaz1z0sq6cSkJF0+l9dVPZ44bEbZx\no4thEWObJZgfO4Peur0exWfPa8cOZ5Xtb4z+XkGVhihGQjpasxsvNXcD1FGPnGwY\ngTlCKKwgUImFW0WrTbOC\n=46n6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e98afa7713f2a48891914e76671a286ef92156dc\nparent 2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780857196 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780857196 -0700\n\nfix: preserve approval sandbox decisions in unified exec (#24981)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR fixes approval sandbox semantics in the unified-exec path. The\nzsh-fork runtime exposed the bug because the shell can do meaningful\nwork before any intercepted child `execv(2)` exists: redirections,\nbuiltins, globbing, and pipeline setup all happen in the launch process.\nIf the model requested `sandbox_permissions=require_escalated`, or an\nexec-policy `allow` rule explicitly bypassed the sandbox, that approved\nsandbox decision needs to be preserved for the launch path and for\nintercepted execs that use the same approval machinery.\n\nThe behavior is not only about zsh fork. The production changes are in\nshared approval/escalation code, so they also affect non-zsh-fork\nintercepted exec paths that go through the same sandbox decision logic.\nThe narrow intent is to preserve the approval decision while still\nkeeping denied-read profiles and bounded additional-permission requests\nsandboxed.\n\n## Production Changes\n\n- `codex-rs/core/src/tools/runtimes/unified_exec.rs`: derives a\n`launch_sandbox_permissions` value from the requested sandbox\npermissions and the runtime filesystem policy, then uses that value for\nmanaged-network/env setup and launch sandbox selection. This keeps full\napproval or policy-bypass decisions visible to the first unified-exec\nattempt, while still preventing a full sandbox override from discarding\ndenied-read restrictions. Direct unified exec keeps the same decision\nsurface; the important difference is that zsh-fork launch setup no\nlonger accidentally loses the approved parent sandbox decision.\n\n- `codex-rs/core/src/tools/runtimes/shell/unix_escalation.rs`: makes\nintercepted-exec escalation selection explicit for the three sandbox\npermission modes. `UseDefault` only escalates when an exec-policy\ndecision allows sandbox bypass, `RequireEscalated` escalates when\nunsandboxed execution is allowed, and `WithAdditionalPermissions`\nescalates through the bounded additional-permissions path instead of\nbeing treated as a full unsandboxed override. Unsandboxed intercepted\nexecs now also rebuild the environment as `RequireEscalated`, which\nstrips managed-network proxy variables consistently with other\nunsandboxed execution.\n\n## Test Coverage\n\nMost of the PR is tests. The new coverage verifies:\n\n- unified exec preserves parent approval and exec-policy sandbox\ndecisions for zsh-fork launch selection;\n- bounded `with_additional_permissions` remains sandboxed and\npermission-profile based;\n- denied-read profiles are not weakened by parent approval;\n- explicit prompt rules still prompt for intercepted execs after the\nparent command is approved;\n- unsandboxed intercepted execs strip managed-network env vars.\n\nNo documentation update is needed; this is an internal approval/sandbox\ncorrectness fix.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/24981).\n* #24982\n* __->__ #24981","verified_at":"2026-06-07T18:33:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e6c470957de53572706afd19f7d8efb42985864c/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad"}]},{"sha":"2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlZTMzNThjMDBhNGQ3NWRiMzE5ZDAxMTAxMzc1NGE0NTJkZGRkYWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-07T16:24:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-07T16:24:54Z"},"message":"ci: use bazel environment for BuildBuddy secret (#26895)\n\n## Why\n\n`BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY` now lives in the `bazel` GitHub Actions environment\nas an environment secret. Jobs that need BuildBuddy credentials must opt\ninto that environment so `${{ secrets.BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY }}` resolves\nfrom the protected environment secret instead of relying on an unscoped\nrepository/organization secret.\n\nThis follows the same environment-secret migration pattern as #26466.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Attach each workflow job that reads `BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY` to the\n`bazel` environment.\n- Set `deployment: false` on those job-level environment blocks.\n\n`deployment: false` lets the job enter the `bazel` environment to access\nits environment secrets without creating GitHub deployment records for\nthese CI jobs. That keeps the environment as a secret/access-control\nboundary without making ordinary Bazel CI runs look like deploys.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Parsed the modified workflow YAML files with Ruby's YAML parser.\n- Checked the modified workflow files for trailing whitespace.","tree":{"sha":"f653ff8c7eb9d876166e4292ae4106e478ddb23e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f653ff8c7eb9d876166e4292ae4106e478ddb23e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqJZtWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlAYQABC5fwdPMF2g9crB7YuG7jRd\nMQBYfeWMM7ZFXZHiW6JEdBph5pjDrxQPHaagZYKaZKxwoqbWpwBqT2VTgeBM8XnN\nAw5rhpoAn+g8JMWtwTPqnzLaOdarG8HdQ/2mwkUjXMO7EGzlR+nqRrbdTgVfLzo+\nAH2QhqKuio1HwKxJNxwu4vmsIAyON5a1gcQCrYZmZYnqPudCS8vFWTvJYSc4Z86b\nfs8+R25tbMjkSJe5883UR7mbEw7UoSKcF2byMyNF6GE8JDzzFktuLo0RIhwQ15Tm\nCL7FTs4BoQBea39hISFefh9O8yxZFRMbRRgzbGXpXBhxTuMXL6PxiubffPm4SdjM\nNrMYmiStxZRf7icbD/ycPRPdLT0bCVZ1WOZFQe/qvw2VJ7eHpGBhleHv+wf1WT5z\nd78jCNidCEfQjwSK1A9XCertrmObg7dSyshZT4Pn0xi0myzD6gDEsNdi4IpbYiTS\nPHu31wqNnF/SYdYgSlf8p/dDDpsKxkf0dKEknjkubdXtAwE21oHTu3qB8oHt8H9C\nHqsdJrXtgWAiLVtKn/SBwYmm7ugMaEFoXfXNpEg8fOkcGrqtf9bGNZOYtx/sCIZ7\n93/WDMBibEawwljtBGfe1IiZoaWiEyRFH1xnEq0Btk+vDBEVi2Vj/lpi+xvVTpDp\nbkJ04IvXcMjybpgIdV/u\n=GKds\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f653ff8c7eb9d876166e4292ae4106e478ddb23e\nparent b89ce9a2bcedcfddf3a48f387b7912d602d6d87c\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780849494 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780849494 -0700\n\nci: use bazel environment for BuildBuddy secret (#26895)\n\n## Why\n\n`BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY` now lives in the `bazel` GitHub Actions environment\nas an environment secret. Jobs that need BuildBuddy credentials must opt\ninto that environment so `${{ secrets.BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY }}` resolves\nfrom the protected environment secret instead of relying on an unscoped\nrepository/organization secret.\n\nThis follows the same environment-secret migration pattern as #26466.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Attach each workflow job that reads `BUILDBUDDY_API_KEY` to the\n`bazel` environment.\n- Set `deployment: false` on those job-level environment blocks.\n\n`deployment: false` lets the job enter the `bazel` environment to access\nits environment secrets without creating GitHub deployment records for\nthese CI jobs. That keeps the environment as a secret/access-control\nboundary without making ordinary Bazel CI runs look like deploys.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Parsed the modified workflow YAML files with Ruby's YAML parser.\n- Checked the modified workflow files for trailing whitespace.","verified_at":"2026-06-07T16:24:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ee3358c00a4d75db319d011013754a452ddddad/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ